{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development","id":1463822,"title":"Hunter the Reckoning done with Development!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-14T07:01:10-07:00","id":1463822,"title":"Hunter the Reckoning done with Development!","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/world-of-darkness-brand-update\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/world-of-darkness-brand-update\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/world-of-darkness-brand-update\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/world-of-darkness-brand-update </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Seems that it'll be done faster than W5 even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T08:15:04-07:00","id":1463828,"title":"","content":"Huh. Wasn't expecting a new edition of Hunter being up sooner rather then later.<br /> <br /> And at least explains why PDX reportedly shot down a Hunter20...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T08:28:02-07:00","id":1463830,"title":"","content":"Okay I am legitimately surprised here. Both that H5 is being done but that also sounds like that it might actually be here <i>before</i> W5 and really the rest of the WoD Five. Like I would have figured that they would want to at least do the other two of the Big Three and get them out before even beginning to work on a minor line like HtR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T08:36:35-07:00","id":1463832,"title":"","content":"So a prerecorded interview with Justin Achilli is going on right now on the <a href=\"https://www.twitch.tv/worldofdarkness\" target=\"_blank\">worldofdarkness twich channel</a><br /> <br /> The main takeaway is that there is no more imbued any more, it seems to be more akin to Hunter the Vigil with disparate groups hunting. It includes Creeds as philosophies and approaches to hunting and Endowments that cover all kinds of powers, artifacts and even True Faith. It also seems to be a game about hope and taking back the world from the monsters.<br /> <br /> Note: the description is short, the traditional Imbued might be a subtype but not explicitly mentioned? But not a lot of details was given.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T08:38:42-07:00","id":1463833,"title":"","content":"I was a little taken aback too. Disappointed that its still going to be a while before we get even a glimpse of M5 but my guess is that Hunter is an easier lift mechanically based on the already produced mechanics of V5, the hunters in second inquisition book that is upcoming and W5 development. Based on the vagueness of the statement its really not clear what kind of Hunter we are talking about here. Is it imbued hunters with powers like in the old Hunter the reckoning or is it taking a leaf out of the Hunter the Vigil book and presenting different tiers - local mortal hunters, hunter organizations with some special edge and genuinely empowered Hunters? So it may be something more like a mortals book, which would make sense for it to be earlier in the production schedule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T09:00:32-07:00","id":1463836,"title":"","content":"It seems that the Imbued are definitely out. &quot;The Imbued will not be carried over from the old game&quot;<br /> CCA: 55 minutes in","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T09:23:16-07:00","id":1463842,"title":"","content":"And suddenly my interest in this has taken a near fatal hit. I love the Imbued and if I wanted to play disparate hunter groups working together, I'd play Hunter: the Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T09:48:07-07:00","id":1463845,"title":"","content":"Also in the last few questions it was confirmed that the game will be out before Werewolf, but that they won't commit to dates due to the shipping issues currently plaguing the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T10:58:42-07:00","id":1463856,"title":"","content":"\u2026yeah this is a bizarre that they take the name of \u201cHunter: the Reckoning\u201d but\u2026remove the integral splat tied to it? <br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m left with the cynical outlook that they lifted the name purely for branding since I imagine they don\u2019t want to call it \u201cHunters Hunted 3\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T11:12:00-07:00","id":1463860,"title":"","content":"And Hunter: the Reckoning 2 works better? Though Reckoning had three video games.... so maybe Paradox cares about that more than anything else?<br /> <br /> But yeah, I do not understand why WW and now Paradox seem obsessed with making choices that will obviously piss off some old fans, for what can only the be most minor branding rationales. No Reckoning fan is going to appreciate being tossed out of the new edition, and nobody that prefers HH or HtV is going to be excited by using the HtR brand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T11:37:27-07:00","id":1463864,"title":"","content":"Yeah, like if they wanted to do a book on regular hunters, they should have done a Hunters Hunted 3 or something like OPP's Ghost Hunters where it's a book dedicated to those hunters, with the Imbued like in HH2 being separated from the rest and kept in their gameline. A book that consolidates all the hunters that aren't Imbued, the Society of Leopold or the SI. Fans old and new would have been happy with that. But now they've pissed off old fans of HtR by getting rid of the Imbued and slapping the HtR label on... well I guess all the Hunters now.<br /> <br /> Once again it seems that people behind 5E can't help but make at least one major change in each gameline that frustrates and angers people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T18:42:08-07:00","id":1463924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1463864#post1463864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again it seems that people behind 5E can't help but make at least one major change in each gameline that frustrates and angers people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to say that at this point I know that's to be expected from 5E...but:<br /> <br /> <i>Erasing the entire splat</i>?<br /> <br /> Like, wow - I find hard to believe it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T18:48:52-07:00","id":1463927,"title":"","content":"I never played the original HtR so to me this feels like a fresh start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T18:52:19-07:00","id":1463929,"title":"","content":"Pros:<br /> -I kinda like the idea of hunters hunted and even more with them being at odds with the Second Inquisition (which makes sense btw).<br /> -They are keeping supernatural powers.<br /> -I'm crossing my fingers for them giving me a DA:Inquisitor like game in the modern age.<br /> <br /> Cons:<br /> -I liked the imbued.<br /> <br /> Btw I think I understand why they want to get rid of the imbued. They were a metaplot-heavy splat intimately tied to D:tF which is a bit hard to sell to new players. I don't like this logic but I can see the reasoning behind it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T19:06:03-07:00","id":1463931,"title":"","content":"I'm disappointed they decided to cut Imbued out all together but maybe the other changes will make up for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T19:45:50-07:00","id":1463934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1463929#post1463929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw I think I understand why they want to get rid of the imbued. They were a metaplot-heavy splat intimately tied to D:tF which is a bit hard to sell to new players. I don't like this logic but I can see the reasoning behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure they were but that knowledge was completely out of the PC's knowledge. They had no idea who or what the Messengers were. In fact that was reoccurring thing in the chat room conversations they were having, with the Imbued throwing around different ideas on what they were. In fact there was a UFO-nut who utterly believed the Messengers were aliens.<br /> <br /> It would have been very easy for H5 to take the simple stance of never explaining what the Messengers were, saying to ST that they can be anything they want to be, angels, aliens, eldritch gods, etc.<br /> <br /> The only thing I can think of as to why they are doing this is... well the theory that the higher ups want the Chronicles of Darkness but with the World of Darkness brand name. Because the way H5 is being described, it's Hunter: the Vigil but for WoD. And like I said, if I wanted to play HtV, I'd play HtV. I have no interest in buying a new book to play HtV but in a different setting. If I wanted to play normal hunters in WoD, I'd pull out one of the multiple hunter books for WoD. I play HtR because I want to play an Imbued. If I can't play that, why should I buy the HtR in name only H5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T23:03:53-07:00","id":1463962,"title":"","content":"I am not a fan of the announcement.<br /> I enjoyed the Imbued and the higher ups are pushing too hard for Chronicles of Darkness 2.0 instead of making World of Darkness 5.0<br /> But, hey, if people out there enjoy it and want to play this version? Then I wish them all the best and to have many long years of playing.<br /> My table? I am not even suggesting the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T05:06:36-07:00","id":1464009,"title":"","content":"I think the company is targeting H5 at new fans who aren\u2019t familiar with (or at least don\u2019t care about) all the old backstory stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T06:27:29-07:00","id":1464023,"title":"","content":"First they do some weird shit with Vampire, then they shoot Gaia in the head, and now they've removed the Reckoning part from Hunters: The Reckoning (more like Hunters: The Gelded now)? What in the name of the Dark Father are the writers smoking!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T09:27:14-07:00","id":1464043,"title":"","content":"Speaking as someone who's a huge fan of Hunter: The Vigil, I would love to see a Hunter: The Reckoning V5 that features ragtag independent hunter cells, the Second Inquisition, the Imbued from OG Hunter, and brand new factions, all updated and thrown together into a cohesive whole. <br /> <br /> Instead of eliminating Imbued entirely, couldn't they be re-flavored as just another hunter conspiracy, with their &quot;Edges&quot; re-worked to give them equal weight to the True Faith, Hedge Magic, and psychic powers other augmented hunters use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12641-aldosalt","name":"AldoSalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12641_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T11:30:18-07:00","id":1464063,"title":"","content":"Once you stop to think about it, it isn't as surprising as it seems.<br /> <br /> We got used to H:tR as a proper game line, but <i>Hunters Hunted</i> was actually one of the oldest supplements and came before WtA IIRC. In a sense it is actually late.<br /> <br /> And for this same reason it also makes sense that it is about disparate groups, as HtV organized this style very well but HH was already done like that.<br /> <br /> Let's wait and see what they do with the book. There are lots of groups that need some update if they make it to the book.<br /> <br /> But I have a hunch that the Imbued are really gone, simply to not take the show from the Second Inquisition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T11:53:40-07:00","id":1464065,"title":"","content":"&quot;There are monsters hidden in the midst of the masses. You were a normal person, ignorant like the rest, but now you can <i>see </i>them and have powers to do something about it&quot;. Is this a hard premise to sell w/o demons and whatnot?. I don't think so. There's A LOT of fiction about people that are empowered to figth monsters.<br /> <br /> HtR was a game about this people - it wasn't about the messengers, nor demons, nor the 6th maelstrom. It wasn't even about monsters. It was about <i>the Imbued</i>. Do the experiment of trying to erase them from the original HtR corebook: You're going to be left with <i>almost nothing.</i> It's as if in Masquerade there were no actual vampires.<br /> <br /> W/o them, HtR 5e can't be called &quot;an edition&quot; by any sane standard: It's a different game altogether. It's like calling HtR a &quot;new edition&quot; of Hunters Hunted - which it was most emphatically not (it doesn't <i>allow</i> to tell the same stories, one book doesn't replace the other).<br /> <br /> Hunters Hunted 3 sounds like a more apt name.<br /> <br /> And, yes, one can see how that would make a game more similar to HtV. I think at this point one would have to be in denial to not see the movement from oWoD to nWoD that's being forced - not in rules but in actual &quot;game structure&quot; (the narrative). Albeit I fail to understand why anyone would want to do this - maybe it's, as some said, to try to lure CoD fans back to the fold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-15-2021, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T16:03:35-07:00","id":1464100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464009#post1464009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the company is targeting H5 at new fans who aren\u2019t familiar with (or at least don\u2019t care about) all the old backstory stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why fall back to and old title?<br /> <br /> And it's not like the Imbued have a lot of backstory or history to deal with. They were one of the last original run splats to be introduces, and their backstory is mostly a giant mystery. New fans aren't going to be part of the &quot;We don't like HtR for not being HH&quot; crowd... because they weren't there for that. The Imbued could just be presented as part of the setting and new fans wouldn't know all that backstory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AldoSalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464043#post1464043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of eliminating Imbued entirely, couldn't they be re-flavored as just another hunter conspiracy, with their &quot;Edges&quot; re-worked to give them equal weight to the True Faith, Hedge Magic, and psychic powers other augmented hunters use?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly possible, but the Imbued are a lot more involved that Numina users or Endowments. Edges and Conviction are a whole interactive design that can't be recaptured by turning Edges into standard 1-5 dot powers (I mean, they're already basically the V5 Discipline design anyway in terms of selection one Edge off a list in a fashion that means they can't ever get all of them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464063#post1464063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once you stop to think about it, it isn't as surprising as it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine anything that comes off as surprise is that H5 is already this far along as nWW/Paradox never really hinted to that. Nobody knew to prepare themselves for what changes to HtR they'd expect Paradox to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I have a hunch that the Imbued are really gone, simply to not take the show from the Second Inquisition. </div> </div> </div>If the Imbued aren't going to be in the book titled Hunter: the Reckoning 5th Edition, they're really gone. Reintroducing them in some other later book is so nonsensical Paradox should have already collapsed as a company with that level of bad decision making.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T16:42:32-07:00","id":1464103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464065#post1464065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;There are monsters hidden in the midst of the masses. You were a normal person, ignorant like the rest, but now you can <i>see </i>them and have powers to do something about it&quot;. Is this a hard premise to sell w/o demons and whatnot?. I don't think so. There's A LOT of fiction about people that are empowered to figth monsters.<br /> <br /> HtR was a game about this people - it wasn't about the messengers, nor demons, nor the 6th maelstrom. It wasn't even about monsters. It was about <i>the Imbued</i>. Do the experiment of trying to erase them from the original HtR corebook: You're going to be left with <i>almost nothing.</i> It's as if in Masquerade there were no actual vampires.<br /> <br /> W/o them, HtR 5e can't be called &quot;an edition&quot; by any sane standard: It's a different game altogether. It's like calling HtR a &quot;new edition&quot; of Hunters Hunted - which it was most emphatically not (it doesn't <i>allow</i> to tell the same stories, one book doesn't replace the other).<br /> <br /> Hunters Hunted 3 sounds like a more apt name.<br /> <br /> And, yes, one can see how that would make a game more similar to HtV. I think at this point one would have to be in denial to not see the movement from oWoD to nWoD that's being forced - not in rules but in actual &quot;game structure&quot; (the narrative). Albeit I fail to understand why anyone would want to do this - maybe it's, as some said, to try to lure CoD fans back to the fold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. It'd be like VtM Rulebook only having rules for Ghouls yet still wanting to call it Vampire: the Masquerade. While you can play Ghoul games, VtM is not about Ghouls, it's about Vampires. By that same token Hunter: the Reckoning is about the Imbued, not the various other Hunters. Releasing a Core Book that strips out the Imbued while calling it HtR is absurd.<br /> <br /> So far everything I've heard about this project says to me that it's not Hunter: the Reckoning Fifth Edition, it's Hunters Hunted Fifth Edition. It's just that someone got it in their head to call it Hunter: the Reckoning to appeal to HtR fans despite gutting the actual hunters of HtR.<br /> <br /> As it's been said, newcomers who have no idea about the original iteration of HtR so the name doesn't mean much to them while long time fans are going to annoyed or worse at the loss of the Imbued. So who does this appeal to exactly? Why destroy HtR and replace it with HtV: WoD Edition? Why not just do HH5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T17:30:17-07:00","id":1464111,"title":"","content":"So Werewolf took up way more of my attention and time, but I went back and listened again to the hunter stuff. The idea is that it's a street level game about driven individuals taking back the night and doing it on their own terms. They may have been members of organisations in the WoD, but now the organisations are occasionally allies and usually antagonists. The Hunters follow Creeds, which are splats that revolve around their approaches to the hunt and the world. They have Edges, a smorgasbord of skills and perks that include mundane things like allies and arsenals as well as True Faith or Investments.<br /> <br /> One of the themes they are going for is the conflict between the big organisations and the cells of the Hunters. But these Hunters are not imbued, but ordinary people taking back the night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T17:37:11-07:00","id":1464112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464100#post1464100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then why fall back to and old title?<br /> <br /> And it's not like the Imbued have a lot of backstory or history to deal with. They were one of the last original run splats to be introduces, and their backstory is mostly a giant mystery. New fans aren't going to be part of the &amp;quot;We don't like HtR for not being HH&amp;quot; crowd... because they weren't there for that. The Imbued could just be presented as part of the setting and new fans wouldn't know all that backstory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's certainly possible, but the Imbued are a lot more involved that Numina users or Endowments. Edges and Conviction are a whole interactive design that can't be recaptured by turning Edges into standard 1-5 dot powers (I mean, they're already basically the V5 Discipline design anyway in terms of selection one Edge off a list in a fashion that means they can't ever get all of them).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd imagine anything that comes off as surprise is that H5 is already this far along as nWW/Paradox never really hinted to that. Nobody knew to prepare themselves for what changes to HtR they'd expect Paradox to make.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If the Imbued aren't going to be in the book titled Hunter: the Reckoning 5th Edition, they're really gone. Reintroducing them in some other later book is so nonsensical Paradox should have already collapsed as a company with that level of bad decision making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you happy about the Imbued being gone? Or do you hate it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T17:40:03-07:00","id":1464113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464103#post1464103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. It'd be like VtM Rulebook only having rules for Ghouls yet still wanting to call it Vampire: the Masquerade. While you can play Ghoul games, VtM is not about Ghouls, it's about Vampires. By that same token Hunter: the Reckoning is about the Imbued, not the various other Hunters. Releasing a Core Book that strips out the Imbued while calling it HtR is absurd.<br /> <br /> So far everything I've heard about this project says to me that it's not Hunter: the Reckoning Fifth Edition, it's Hunters Hunted Fifth Edition. It's just that someone got it in their head to call it Hunter: the Reckoning to appeal to HtR fans despite gutting the actual hunters of HtR.<br /> <br /> As it's been said, newcomers who have no idea about the original iteration of HtR so the name doesn't mean much to them while long time fans are going to annoyed or worse at the loss of the Imbued. So who does this appeal to exactly? Why destroy HtR and replace it with HtV: WoD Edition? Why not just do HH5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because \u201cHunter: the Reckoning\u201d sounds cooler than just \u201cHunters.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T18:21:56-07:00","id":1464118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464111#post1464111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hunters follow Creeds, which are splats that revolve around their approaches to the hunt and the world. They have Edges, a smorgasbord of skills and perks that include mundane things like allies and arsenals as well as True Faith or Investments.<br /> <br /> One of the themes they are going for is the conflict between the big organisations and the cells of the Hunters. But these Hunters are not imbued, but ordinary people taking back the night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did anyone over there read Hunter: First Contact? Because the old game had all of this. What's the point of dumping the Imbued? &quot;We want ordinary people taking back the night... with access to supernatural abilities, but not the Imbued who were ordinary people taking back the night with access to supernatural abilities.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464112#post1464112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you happy about the Imbued being gone? Or do you hate it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither exactly?<br /> <br /> I don't like V5's mechanically implementation (among many other things), and I haven't seen anything that would sway me to think I'm going to like H5 on that alone. As such I don't care too much about what 5e does with them. If H5 was actually a new edition of HtR (and HtR needs a revision badly), I'd probably still never play it, but if it focused on making the Imbued a more well executed splat I would consider buying the PDF for my stack of house rules for HtR.<br /> <br /> I hate that we're not getting H20 and H5 is dumping the Imbued at the same time though. If they're going to dump the Imbued, they could have given HtR fans a chance at a revised core book of the game that we love before the strange branding choice being done here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464113#post1464113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because \u201cHunter: the Reckoning\u201d sounds cooler than just \u201cHunters.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters Hunted is pretty cool, and already a title associated with the WoD and books that cover multiple types of humans with maybe some supernatural perks that hunt monsters. It's not like Paradox can't come up with a new title if they want to as well.<br /> <br /> Are you actually going to answer what I asked? Or is this some giant deflection from the points being made?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T18:42:17-07:00","id":1464123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464118#post1464118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did anyone over there read Hunter: First Contact? Because the old game had all of this. What's the point of dumping the Imbued? &quot;We want ordinary people taking back the night... with access to supernatural abilities, but not the Imbued who were ordinary people taking back the night with access to supernatural abilities.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know!<br /> <br /> A lot of the stuff they are presenting as big changes and revamps and new shinyness for 5E just seems like they skipped what the lines evolved into and looked like by the end of the WoD. Which is kinda sad, but I guess not everyone can be experts on everything WW did, and they sure did a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T19:29:42-07:00","id":1464129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464100#post1464100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd imagine anything that comes off as surprise is that H5 is already this far along as nWW/Paradox never really hinted to that. Nobody knew to prepare themselves for what changes to HtR they'd expect Paradox to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>For now I take this as another hint that they're going to ditch the Imbued altogether, as adapting HH is at least an order of magnitude simpler. And they've been working on it in the sense that they've been working on the SI.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464103#post1464103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. It'd be like VtM Rulebook only having rules for Ghouls yet still wanting to call it Vampire: the Masquerade. While you can play Ghoul games, VtM is not about Ghouls, it's about Vampires. By that same token Hunter: the Reckoning is about the Imbued, not the various other Hunters. Releasing a Core Book that strips out the Imbued while calling it HtR is absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is worse than that. At least Ghouls are a thing from VtM. HH is ALSO a thing from VtM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464103#post1464103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far everything I've heard about this project says to me that it's not Hunter: the Reckoning Fifth Edition, it's Hunters Hunted Fifth Edition. It's just that someone got it in their head to call it Hunter: the Reckoning to appeal to HtR fans despite gutting the actual hunters of HtR.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest there is a reason to do it that way. I'm not saying it is a good reason, but there is.<br /> <br /> HtR is a game line. It isn't a supplement, it is an entire game line you can write follow-ups for and don't have to lean in other lines while doing so. This is the big difference they're bringing from HtV to cWoD. As interesting as HH, and HX for that matter, were, they're don't stand on their own and rely heavily on other lines and on being relatively small books.<br /> <br /> With this move they're using their proprietary Hunter brand to make a proper Hunter-based line, so it does make a lot of sense. Even if doing the Imbued it would make sense to have other hunters under this line instead of any other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464123#post1464123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the stuff they are presenting as big changes and revamps and new shinyness for 5E just seems like they skipped what the lines evolved into and looked like by the end of the WoD. Which is kinda sad, but I guess not everyone can be experts on everything WW did, and they sure did a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as they want to simplify presentation for new players, being an expert on everything WW is literally their job.<br /> <br /> Otherwise it isn't even this case. As good as the line is (I don't know, I don't know HtR in dept), the core concept is an old trope played straight. This is HtV, this is HtR, HH, Buffy the Vampire Slayer, Blade, Ravenloft, playing as Cleric in D&amp;D, this is the fucking <i>Malleus Maleficarum</i>, Jesus exorcising pigs and about half of the epic of Gilgamesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T19:41:55-07:00","id":1464131,"title":"","content":"HtR was one of my favorite gamelines in WoD.I devoured all the books. I loved them. I loved them due to the Imbued and all the stuff tied to them.The way Edges worked. The whole Messengers being mysterious was always great. Hell, even the fact that their Edges and Second Sight literally broke the powers of the other splats. It was amazing. It made you feel like you -COULD- take back the night, one monster at a time.<br /> I understand the appeal of fighting a losing war like in Hunters Hunted and Hunter the Vigil. Hell, even in Werewolf the Apocalypse was like that. I get the appeal but I liked the fact that Imbued COULD do so.<br /> <br /> Also, to all the people talking about how &quot;They are so tied into DtF&quot; please remember that the corebook came out a full three years before DtF. So the ties were done in a nice retcon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T19:50:26-07:00","id":1464134,"title":"","content":"HtR was originally tied to Wraith and the events in Ends of Empire as the Sixth Maelstrom resulted in a lot of ghosts suddenly in the skinlands, and thus zombies being frequent inciting incidents for Imbuing and common enemies for the Imbued. While it was clear that there was more to it, HtR started with the idea that the sudden (re-)appearance of the Imbued was a react to the sudden mass of supernatural energy being tossed out of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> DtF hooked into that for what broke open the abyssal prison, and defining demons in a highly Miltonian way that allows them to be connected to the Messengers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T20:30:13-07:00","id":1464142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464123#post1464123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know!<br /> <br /> A lot of the stuff they are presenting as big changes and revamps and new shinyness for 5E just seems like they skipped what the lines evolved into and looked like by the end of the WoD. Which is kinda sad, but I guess not everyone can be experts on everything WW did, and they sure did a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah and really frustratingly they could have done what they talked about H5 containing with the Imbued. It's been 20+ years since the Imbued started appearing. Groups and factions would have formed among them since then. HtR had street-level action by default and design as the whole point was that these were random people being chosen.<br /> <br /> As for the metaplot and being tied to the looming Time of Judgement, 5E has very much taking the stance that perhaps the Apocalypse did happen but not as everyone was expecting. Even if the 6GM is retconned away, the Week of Nightmares isn't and things like the Beckoning and it's implications, there's still plenty to justify the Messengers Imbuing people. And it's not like the Imbued themselves actually knew what the Messengers were and why they were being Imbued. Hell, even the knowledge they gained about the 6GM came from a vampire and Carpenter, a Specter thrown out into the Skinlands and made into a Risen due to the 6GM, that were led to the hunter-net by the Messengers. And neither were exactly trusted by the Imbued nor had a lot of the details of the 6GM. They just knew that some major storm hit the Underworld and violently shook things up. They could easily retcon it to a less severe state, making their comments a bit mistaken but not entirely wrong either.<br /> <br /> Hell they could have followed it up with a HH3 and do the one thing HH2 didn't do, factor in the Imbued and their relations with other hunters and hunter groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T21:04:21-07:00","id":1464150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464118#post1464118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did anyone over there read Hunter: First Contact? Because the old game had all of this. What's the point of dumping the Imbued? &amp;quot;We want ordinary people taking back the night... with access to supernatural abilities, but not the Imbued who were ordinary people taking back the night with access to supernatural abilities.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Neither exactly?<br /> <br /> I don't like V5's mechanically implementation (among many other things), and I haven't seen anything that would sway me to think I'm going to like H5 on that alone. As such I don't care too much about what 5e does with them. If H5 was actually a new edition of HtR (and HtR needs a revision badly), I'd probably still never play it, but if it focused on making the Imbued a more well executed splat I would consider buying the PDF for my stack of house rules for HtR.<br /> <br /> I hate that we're not getting H20 and H5 is dumping the Imbued at the same time though. If they're going to dump the Imbued, they could have given HtR fans a chance at a revised core book of the game that we love before the strange branding choice being done here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hunters Hunted is pretty cool, and already a title associated with the WoD and books that cover multiple types of humans with maybe some supernatural perks that hunt monsters. It's not like Paradox can't come up with a new title if they want to as well.<br /> <br /> Are you actually going to answer what I asked? Or is this some giant deflection from the points being made?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the name has brand recognition. Even fans who have never played HtR (like me) will recognize the title and pick it up just for that (like me again) and not really care that much that the Imbued are gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T23:51:30-07:00","id":1464159,"title":"","content":"You're really going to buy the &quot;5th&quot; edition of a game, sight unseen, because you recognize the title from somewhere? No Googling it? No reading a Wikipedia page about it? Not listening to the video of Justin talking about it that spawned this thread where he talks about how there's not going to be Imbued PCs and getting curious what that means?<br /> <br /> I... really doubt that anyone at Paradox is banking on that market. People that played the video games because the found it for a few bucks on Steam or whatever? OK... but they played game with the old lore. V5 fans that are new to the franchise and have read up on some of the old stuff? Same issue.<br /> <br /> Yes, HtR as brand value... but it's value built on game that had the Imbued in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T23:54:48-07:00","id":1464161,"title":"","content":"This seems like it's catering to people who didn't give HtR a chance rather than fans who are more likely to pick up a new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T05:14:50-07:00","id":1464175,"title":"","content":"It almost seems like someone said, 'What were the big arguments that a minority of fans made in the 90s about each game? Okay, let's design to accommodate those people!'<br /> <br /> So, Humanity not being central enough, HTR not being HH2, etc.<br /> <br /> But in all seriousness, I think that an updated HTR with the option to play 'little sibling' lower-case hunters like ghouls or Thin-Bloods in Vampire, would have satisfied more people.<br /> <br /> Inquisitor already presented a version of hunters and Imbued-like beings mingled together. More of that, and less throwing everything in the bin, and they would be laughing all the way to the bank.<br /> <br /> I'm also not really sure why we need both the SI book and Inquisition: The Seconding as an official line. It would be like giving vampire a book called Lupines alongside WTA. Though maybe the SI book is primarily an adventure book?<br /> <br /> On the plus side, H5 might be an opportunity to iron out the creases in the 5e mechanics, so that these can be backported to V5. I'm always looking for those silver linings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T05:46:19-07:00","id":1464180,"title":"","content":"Ditching the Imbued is a bad move. It may not alienate some players like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26996_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26996\" data-vbnamecard=\"26996\">Amethyst</a> and, tbh, me, but it will alienate a lot of people for absolutely no reason. I mean, I'm not that a fan of the concept of the Imbued, but I could just keep ignoring then as I did until now. As was brought up in other topics, I get nothing out of the deal but the &quot;satisfaction&quot; of laughing off from the people affected. Wtf?<br /> <br /> But they demonstrated time and again that they have a very specific vision for the setting and will thoroughly ditch anything that distract too much from that vision. The Sabbat as a playable option is a fine example. The SI is their main hunter theme, they may accept to break it as its metaplot develops, but they won't let the Imbued outshine their chosen toy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T06:08:38-07:00","id":1464183,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to think of a way of asking &quot;isn't this just hunter the vigil again?&quot; While not seeming dismissive.<br /> <br /> ......I've got nothing. Which is probably what I'll be giving to them because I already own hunter the vigil corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-16-2021, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T06:50:14-07:00","id":1464191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464183#post1464183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to think of a way of asking &quot;isn't this just hunter the vigil again?&quot; While not seeming dismissive.<br /> <br /> ......I've got nothing. Which is probably what I'll be giving to them because I already own hunter the vigil corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the simple answer is yes.. and no. Yes this looks much closer to hunter the vigil than it does to reckoning as it was. Its pretty clear that the WoD5 range is part reboot of OWoD and part part comic book style multiversal post crisis merging of universes in that it is adapting both mechanical and thematic elements from NWoD/CoD and folding them into this new continuity. This seems to be a good example of that. They have clearly decided (perhaps with good reason, perhaps not) that something more akin to H:tV fits better into the new continuity than H:tR and so they are folding that into the new universe. My guess is this is far less about older gamers who love V20 or H:tR or even H:tV than it is about expanding the universe for newer gamers who have entered this world via V5. So depending on how they do it, this will either be a great melding of to NWoD hunter ideas into WoD5, pleasing new (and some old) players who want to play the mortal flipside of the V5 world they have already been playing in, or a monstrous frankenstein (and not in a good way!) that will please no one. I'm open to the possibilities and will happily play this new game and draw on what i like from H:tV and thus get the best of both worlds!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T07:33:37-07:00","id":1464194,"title":"","content":"The thing is, I love Vigil. I don't think it's a bad idea to introduce the ideas and options of that into classic WoD. However, why delete the Imbued? Why not make them another option? Make things more inclusive and give people options, don't tell them that what they did before is irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T07:48:24-07:00","id":1464196,"title":"","content":"The frustrating thing is that we're not going to get an H20 so all we have is the original material now. And if I remember right OPP did have an H20 proposal that Paradox shot down so it's not like such a project wouldn't have happened. If we had gotten H20, I think many of us long time fans would have grumbled about H5 but we would have been content that at least we had a 20E to tune up the game and better help us play the original game in the modern day.<br /> <br /> And if I'm completely honest, the cynical part of me now thinks that Paradox shot it down because they already had the H5 concept and didn't want OPP reminding people of the Imbued and/or competing against H5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T10:59:34-07:00","id":1464209,"title":"","content":"Wait... What the fuck? They took out the Imbued? So what the hell happens to their connection with the KotE and the fact that they were granted their powers by the remnants of the Celestial Bureaucracy? This entire 5th has been a dumpster fire. Who actually wanted this?<br /> <br /> I knew it was a real red-flag that they seemingly did a H5 right after V5, instead of W5. It's easy to churn out since this is just going to be regular Hunters that are essentially the ones from Vigil.. It doesn't require much work, no real need to re-observe the past material to make sure everything aligns-up right, and it gives more fodder for these nu-writers to just stuff things from CofD without being original. I have nothing against CofD, mind you, but this is just how it seems to me.<br /> <br /> Like jesus, I wonder how the minority amount of fans for HtR line even feel about this.. if they even still care about this franchise anymore. It just makes me shudder of how they're going to massacre WtO5 if they ever get around to it... lol<br /> <br /> And most of these dumb decisions stem from the platitude that, &quot;everything must be simplified&quot; for the so-called &quot;new players who are just streaming into WoD (lol)&quot;. Why must everything be simplified just because someone is new to the franchise? I literally only got into oWoD in 2017 and consumed a large part of the material within a couple of months to understand most of things in this formerly great setting. Making everything reduced will not entice new people, because then people who will look into it.. won't be interested in it at all.<br /> <br /> Or maybe these unnecessary reductions are due to them not even knowing the past material or not even bothering to review it.<br /> <br /> I didn't really got much into Hunter the Reckoning, but the thing that appealed to me the most, was that all the Hunters were average regular people. Then out of nowhere they gain these supernatural abilities and now have a burden of fighting against the various other splats in the WoD Universe. It reminded me somewhat like the Mother series, akin to how Ness was just a regular Middle Schooler, but now he suddenly gains psychic powers and has to fight an interdimensional all-consuming evil.<br /> <br /> Now they're just mundane boring Hunters... I'm sure some people may like that angle.. but the major appeal to me in WoD is the supernatural elements of the setting (obviously) mixed with the intrigues of how the players can interact with it and grow whatever supernatural abilities they have. Now the Imbued are an eliminated factor in this. I don't see how this Hunter Fifth Edition will possibly appeal to me now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were a metaplot-heavy splat intimately tied to D:tF which is a bit hard to sell to new players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? HtR had little to do (if almost nothing) with D:tF. Most of the background of the Imbued was a mystery, but there was an overarching connecting/theming toward KotE if anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 10-16-2021, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T12:01:21-07:00","id":1464211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464191#post1464191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think the simple answer is yes.. and no. Yes this looks much closer to hunter the vigil than it does to reckoning as it was. Its pretty clear that the WoD5 range is part reboot of OWoD and part part comic book style multiversal post crisis merging of universes in that it is adapting both mechanical and thematic elements from NWoD/CoD and folding them into this new continuity. This seems to be a good example of that. They have clearly decided (perhaps with good reason, perhaps not) that something more akin to H:tV fits better into the new continuity than H:tR and so they are folding that into the new universe. My guess is this is far less about older gamers who love V20 or H:tR or even H:tV than it is about expanding the universe for newer gamers who have entered this world via V5. So depending on how they do it, this will either be a great melding of to NWoD hunter ideas into WoD5, pleasing new (and some old) players who want to play the mortal flipside of the V5 world they have already been playing in, or a monstrous frankenstein (and not in a good way!) that will please no one. I'm open to the possibilities and will happily play this new game and draw on what i like from H:tV and thus get the best of both worlds!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah.....I think I'll pass. Paying for a game you already own pretending to be another game which you already own is absurd. I'm gonna spend it on beer instead.<br /> <br /> Late stage capitalism man....we can't keep this up, especially on current pay levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-16-2021, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T12:26:10-07:00","id":1464214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464209#post1464209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... What the fuck? They took out the Imbued? So what the hell happens to their connecting with the Kuei-Jin and the fact that they were granted their powers by the remnants of the Celestial Chorus? This entire 5th has been a dumpster fire. Who actually wanted this?<br /> <br /> I knew it was a real red-flag that they seemingly did a H5 right after V5, instead of W5. It's easy to churn out since this is just going to be regular Hunters that are essentially the ones from Vigil.. It doesn't require much work, no real need to re-observe the past material to make sure everything aligns-up right, and it gives more fodder for these nu-writers to just stuff things from CofD without being original. I have nothing against CofD, mind you, but this is just how it seems to me.<br /> <br /> Like jesus, I wonder how the minority amount of fans for HtR line even feel about this.. if they even still care about this franchise anymore. It just makes me shudder of how they're going to massacre WtO5 if they ever get around to it... lol<br /> <br /> And most of these dumb decisions stem from the platitude that, &quot;everything must be simplified&quot; for the so-called &quot;new players who are just streaming into WoD (lol)&quot;. Why must everything be simplified just because someone is new to the franchise? I literally only got into oWoD in 2017 and consumed a large part of the material within a couple of months to understand most of things in this formerly great setting. Making everything reduced will not entice new people, because then people who will look into it.. won't be interested in it at all.<br /> <br /> Or maybe these unnecessary reductions are due to them not even knowing the past material or not even bothering to review it.<br /> <br /> I didn't really got much into Hunter the Reckoning, but the thing that appealed to me the most, was that all the Hunters were average regular people. Then out of nowhere they gain these supernatural abilities and now have a burden of fighting against the various other splats in the WoD Universe. It reminded me somewhat like the Mother series, akin to how Ness was just a regular Middle Schooler, but now he suddenly gains psychic powers and has to fight an interdimensional all-consuming evil.<br /> <br /> Now they're just mundane boring Hunters... I'm sure some people may like that angle.. but the major appeal to me in WoD is the supernatural elements of the setting (obviously) mixed with the intrigues of how the players can interact with it and grow whatever supernatural abilities they have. Now the Imbued are an eliminated factor in this. I don't see how this Hunter Fifth Edition will possibly appeal to me now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen people who didn't care for HtR and preferred HH and HtV expressing displeasure at this as well, not because it's something they don't want but because they too feel it's an insult to the HtR fans who loved playing the Imbued and/or that they are taking away options from players which is never a popular thing.<br /> <br /> Not helped that it doesn't feel like we can talk to the WoD Devs. While they do have a Youtube Channel and a Discord, there isn't to my knowledge an official forum where people could express their feelings and potentially hear back from the Devs. Instead, it really feels like it's a one way street with them telling us what's going on and the most we can do is talk to PR people and maybe if there's enough of us it might get back to those people directly involved in the projects. Here in the OPP forums, OPP Devs can and often do show up, responding to peoples' comments and questions. It feels like OPP listens to us, it's fans. They even give out manuscripts of their projects to their KS backers and will listen to our comments on it. WoD on the other hand, doesn't. It feels like WoD is doing their thing, deciding to only periodically tell us what it's doing and expecting us to just cheer them on for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Huh? HtR had little to do (if almost nothing) with D:tF. Most of the background of the Imbued was a mystery, but there was an overarching connecting/theming toward KotE if anything else. </div> </div> </div>If I remember right, the Messengers are tied to the last two angels on Earth, the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen. They're the ones that started the Imbuing. But again, that's something the Imbued don't really know and could be left vague without any issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T13:25:16-07:00","id":1464216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen</div> </div> </div> </div>They are Angels/High Spirits from the Celestial Bureaucracy, made by the August Personage of Jade. They have little to nothing to do with what went on with D:tF. The source material itself, HtR, was the one to even tie-in these plot hints in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 10-16-2021, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T13:55:42-07:00","id":1464217,"title":"","content":"Incredibly disappointed with this turn of events and even more so with the expectation that any vocal dissidents to these decisions should roll over and accept whatever nebulous amalgamation of trite buzzwords and soft-gaslighting the spin doctors at the marketing department are going to be cooking up for us. <br /> <br /> Especially because...we've had Hunter's Hunted for nearly three decades now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T14:07:14-07:00","id":1464218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464191#post1464191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think the simple answer is yes.. and no. Yes this looks much closer to hunter the vigil than it does to reckoning as it was. Its pretty clear that the WoD5 range is part reboot of OWoD and part part comic book style multiversal post crisis merging of universes in that it is adapting both mechanical and thematic elements from NWoD/CoD and folding them into this new continuity. This seems to be a good example of that. They have clearly decided (perhaps with good reason, perhaps not) that something more akin to H:tV fits better into the new continuity than H:tR and so they are folding that into the new universe. My guess is this is far less about older gamers who love V20 or H:tR or even H:tV than it is about expanding the universe for newer gamers who have entered this world via V5. So depending on how they do it, this will either be a great melding of to NWoD hunter ideas into WoD5, pleasing new (and some old) players who want to play the mortal flipside of the V5 world they have already been playing in, or a monstrous frankenstein (and not in a good way!) that will please no one. I'm open to the possibilities and will happily play this new game and draw on what i like from H:tV and thus get the best of both worlds!</div> </div> </div> </div>I really Like this opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T14:18:56-07:00","id":1464219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464209#post1464209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh? HtR had little to do (if almost nothing) with D:tF. Most of the background of the Imbued was a mystery, but there was an overarching connecting/theming toward KotE if anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon really liked to shit in everyone's backyard explaining how they knew the real scoop and everyone else was just deluding themselves.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T14:20:46-07:00","id":1464220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464219#post1464219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demon really liked to shit in everyone's backyard explaining how they knew the real scoop and everyone else was just deluding themselves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>if they were so smart how come I bound one with prime and spirit?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T14:26:04-07:00","id":1464221,"title":"","content":"And to go even further with how ridiculous this all is... imagine all the wasted Creedbooks, all the signs/code/sigils, setting supplements, now just going down the drain since the Imbued are being removed for this arbitrary unexplained reason..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T15:51:45-07:00","id":1464226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464220#post1464220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if [demons] were so smart how come I bound one with prime and spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing? If you listen to real life exorcists; they\u2019ll confirm in fact that demons are actually really really stupid. They\u2019re stubborn and keep trying the same (admittedly pretty successful on the unaware) tactics against people again and again and just can\u2019t seem to innovate or adapt at all.<br /> <br /> Sin dulls the intellect they say and angels/demons are being of pure intellect so the demons are especially affected by this, being more like beasts of low cunning who hunt easy prey, but no match for a well-formed conscience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T16:40:38-07:00","id":1464229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>scifirabbi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464191#post1464191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My guess is this is far less about older gamers who love V20 or H:tR or even H:tV than it is about expanding the universe for newer gamers who have entered this world via V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep seeing this but it's never actually explained on how this matches any of the facts in evidence.<br /> <br /> What does cutting the Imbued have to do with expanding the universe for newer gamers? What's the evidence, at all, that nWW first, and now Paradox, are actually making the games more new player friendly? V5 is full of stuff that calls back to the older games that new people aren't going to understand without going online to look or asking old fans about. V5 kept Generation because of VtM lore instead of just getting rid of the idea and swapping in VtR's Blood Potency alone, forcing a clunky compromise of both layered together.<br /> <br /> I would buy this if the decisions had any clear indication of actually accomplishing this goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464194#post1464194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's a bad idea to introduce the ideas and options of that into classic WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>And importantly... the only think that Vigil does that wasn't already in cWoD for playable hunters? Having it all in one book. The cWoD books were full of groups that slot into the broad &quot;hunter&quot; idea, but were scattered all over the games, and had varying degrees of support for being playable. <br /> <br /> Slashers are actually HtV's bigger innovation here as something that the cWoD never quite did as distinctly... and they weren't even in HtV 1e's core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464220#post1464220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if they were so smart how come I bound one with prime and spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>If only binding a real world gaming manual were as easy.<br /> <br /> Also, DtF demons aren't really biblical demons. It's Paradise Lost the RPG.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T16:40:48-07:00","id":1464230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464216#post1464216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They Angels/High Spirits from the Celestial Bureaucracy, made by the August Personage of Jade. They have little to nothing to do with what went on with D:tF. The source material itself, HtR, was the one to even tie-in these plot hints in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the DtF Book of Nod equivalent, Days of Fire connects the pair to DtF as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [72]<br /> So great, then, the lamentation of the earth<br /> That two Angels shall turn their ears and hear.<br /> One a woman of scarlet lights<br /> The other a beast of sheltered shadows.<br /> They shall spark, and breathe, and illuminate<br /> And those who feel, and hear, and see, shall be infused<br /> These Bright Shiners come forth to witness, in the last days and final night. </div> </div> </div>Obviously we're talking about an in-universe book which has it's own questionable legitimacy but it was supposedly written by Lucifer and he would the one to know who's an angel and who's not, especially since he was the only Fallen not subjected to the Abyss and the memory loss and distortion it caused. And he calls them Angels so we have to assume he's talking about his fellow Angels and not some other kind of entity.<br /> <br /> And while it rather poetic and flowery, it's pretty clear that the verse is talking the Scarlet Queen, the Ebon Dragon and the Imbued. At the same time, the verses before and after this one talk about events tied to the Rev Ed like the 6GM, the Red Star, the Perfect Metis and the Last Daughter of Eve. So yeah, it's pretty clear that they are talking about the Rev Ed era there which includes the Imbued.<br /> <br /> As for the August Personage of Jade, most who have studied the WoD lore have assumed/concluded that God and the August Personage of Jade are one and the same and by that same token, the Celestial Bureaucracy and the Hierarchy of Angels are two names for the same thing. In fact, the White Wolf Wiki's page on <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/God_(WOD)\" target=\"_blank\">God (WOD)</a> as them as one and the same.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T18:21:31-07:00","id":1464236,"title":"","content":"Problem with that is, like I said before and alluded to by other posters, D:tF retrocon'd stuff from other lines without even properly understanding them or just took stuff, that in doing so messed up the lore from other lines as well. (Accounting HtR already per this post alone, WtO, WtA, CtD, and MtAs were effected by this too)<br /> <br /> Not once did Lucifer make any note of knowing about the Ten Thousand Immortals (the precursors of the Kuei-Jin before they got punished by the August Personage of Jade) or the Yama Kings, at all in D:tF; neither did any of the other Elohim/Abrahamic Angels either. For D:tF to have any tie-in with H:tR, it had to at least recognize some lore from KotE, because HtR drew heavily from that with numerous hints throughout many Creedbooks.. but they never did. And again, with D:tF being the last gameline before cWoD ended, it had troves of material to just riff-off and shove into its line just to give more &quot;legitimacy&quot; so to speak.. It relied more on retroconning, than coming up with its own truly unique identity.<br /> <br /> So it just listing off a bunch of things that were going on in Revised doesn't really mean anything.. because D:tF never mentions anything about the Imbued or the Wan Xian (who were the precursors of the Kuei-Jin) at all or the Age of Legends. There is no Lucifer in KotE, no Angel Houses, no Adam and Eve, and most importantly there is no Cain mentioned anywhere in KotE at all. Cain in D:tF, was the catalyst for Lucifer and his followers to begin fighting the &quot;Heavenly Host&quot; for real due to &quot;first murder&quot;. With that, the rebel Elohim didn't have to &quot;metaphysically hold their punches (or um, blades to be accurate)&quot; from the shockwaves from Cain committing the first murder.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, before D:tF was even a speck of a thought; The Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen were material that began with KotE. If you read the book, the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen made the Wan Xian/Ten Thousand Immortals to fight monsters and the Yama Kings, after seeing them preying on humanity all of a sudden. Looking at the central conflict in D:tF, however, the rebel Elohim/Abrahamic angels get in trouble with <i>their</i> God for interfering with humanity in the first place... see how contradictory it is?<br /> <br /> If the Ebon Dragon and the Scarlet Queen, reportedly with the logic/claim from D:tF about them being the last remaining &quot;Abrahamic Angels&quot;; could possibly be accurate, when the Angels/Elohim described to be loyal to the Abrahamic God in D:tF, fought against the rebel Elohim to stop them from interfering with humanity? I know I sound like a broken record, but I just wanted to double reiterate so this point can get across on why D:tF was badly organized in its lore and not caring about what material it processed into its gameline. The Messengers have nothing do with D:tF Angels, because from their earliest activity, they were literally giving humans supernatural powers to fight other splats; which is a direct contradiction from what Angels were doing in D:tF.<br /> <br /> The Ten Thousand Immortals are never even mentioned once when the Demons were waging war against the Heavenly Host at all. None of the Demons from D:tF even know a single thing about the Yama Kings. They don't even know the Middle or High Umbra even exist. It also breaks the notion that the August Personage of Jade and the Abrahamic God described in D:tF are the same at all. If the logic is that the August Personage of Jade and Abrahamic God are the same, why did they imprison the rebel Elohim but left the Yama Kings alone to remain active?<br /> <br /> The Imbued from Hunter: The Reckoning were supposed to be the-coming-back of the Wan Xian, who were the precursors of the Kuei-Jin; the uncorrupted, uncursed versions who were granted a grand spiritual commission to rid the world of monsters. They're one of the same, just from different ages of time.<br /> <br /> I think this is why the Imbued were ultimately cut. A lot of writers in WoD seem to have a grudge with ANYTHING related to or greatly connected with KotE, so much to this point they're literally cutting out the focal splat from their own game.. and literally replacing them... again, this 5th edition is.. not good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 10-16-2021, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T20:50:56-07:00","id":1464241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464236#post1464236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem with that is, like I said before and alluded to by other posters, D:tF retrocon'd stuff from other lines without even properly understanding them or just took stuff, that in doing so messed up the lore from other lines as well. (Accounting HtR already per this post alone, WtO, WtA, CtD, and MtAs were effected)<br /> <br /> Not once did Lucifer make any note of knowing about the Ten Thousand Immortals (the precursors of the Kuei-Jin before they got punished by the August Personage of Jade) or the Yama Kings, at all in D:tF; neither did any of the other Elohim/Abrahamic Angels either. For D:tF to have any tie-in with H:tR, it had to at least recognize some lore from KotE, because HtR drew heavily from that with numerous hints throughout many Creedbooks.. but they never did. And again, with D:tF being the last gameline before cWoD ended, it had troves of material to just riff-off and shove into its line just to give more &quot;legitimacy&quot; so to speak.. It relied more on retroconning, than coming up with its own truly unique identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because they tend not to reference the creation myths of other lines in their material. Even when Caine, the First Murder and his transformation into a vampire is brought up in DtF it's different from how it's presented in VtM.<br /> <br /> For example in the previously mentioned Days of Fire, while it roughly starts the same with Caine murdering Abel for... well differing reasons depending on the source, what happens next is different. Caine starts slandering God and basically causes not just the birth of murder and lies but sparks the war between the Rebel Angels and the Loyalists. Likewise Caine's transformation into a vampire stares similarly to other versions with God and the Angels offering forgiveness for his sins only for Caine to reject it but ends differently. Instead of Caine being cursed for his rejections of their offers, Caine rejects Gods and his own Humanity resulting in his own transformation into a vampire. There's no Seven-fold Curse or Lillith in the story.<br /> <br /> Likewise the book speaks the Garou and Mages but doesn't really talk about their origins at all. Well beyond the Mages getting a vague passage about the first humans to look at the world around them and wonder how it works.<br /> <br /> Would you expect VtM to explain the backstories of WtA, MtAs, CtD and WtO? No. You'd want VtM to talk about it's own backstory. So why should DtF be obliged to explain the backstories of all the other lines? Especially when it's established in the first or second chapter of the Rulebook that memories of the Fallen are damaged because of their imprisonment in the Abyss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So it just listing off a bunch of things that were going on in Revised doesn't really mean anything.. because D:tF never mentions anything about the Imbued or the Wan Xian (who were the precursors of the Kuei-Jin) at all or the Age of Legends. There is no Lucifer in KotE, no Angel Houses, no Adam and Eve, and most importantly there is no Cain mentioned anywhere in KotE at all. Cain in D:tF, was the catalyst for Lucifer and his followers to begin fighting the &quot;Heavenly Host&quot; for real due to &quot;first murder&quot;. With that, the rebel Elohim didn't have to &quot;metaphysically hold their punches (or um, blades to be accurate)&quot; from the shockwaves from Cain committing the first murder. </div> </div> </div>Yes and at the same time, none of that happens in VtM either yet Caine is vital to it's lore. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meanwhile, before D:tF was even a speck of a thought; The Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen were material that began with KotE. If you read the book, the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen made the Wan Xian/Ten Thousand Immortals to fight monsters and the Yama Kings, after seeing them preying on humanity all of a sudden. Looking at the central conflict in D:tF, however, the rebel Elohim/Abrahamic angels get in trouble with <i>their</i> for interfering with humanity in the first place... see how contradictory it is? </div> </div> </div>It's almost like every WoD gameline has it's own idea as to the origin of the world and everything, ideas that don't line up with other games. Almost like the members of every line believe they are right and everyone else is wrong. Almost like this mythic age was supposed to be mythic and barely understood by modern day people. Or in the case of the Fallen, beings that were a torturous state for eons and have had their minds have been damaged by it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Ebon Dragon and the Scarlet Queen, reportedly with the logic/claim from D:tF about them being the last remaining &quot;Abrahamic Angels&quot;; could possibly be accurate, when the Angels/Elohim described to be loyal to the Abrahamic God in D:tF, fought against the rebel Elohim to stop them from interfering with humanity? I know I sound like a broken record, but I just wanted to double reiterate so this point to get across on why D:tF was badly organized in its lore and not caring about what material it processed into its gameline. The Messengers have nothing do with D:tF Angels, because from their earliest activity, they were literally giving humans supernatural powers to fight other splats; which is a direct contradiction from what Angels were doing in D:tF. </div> </div> </div>Because there's implications that God has disappeared much like how it's believed that August Personage of Jade will disappear for the Sixth Age. Certainly the Angels aside from those two are gone from Earth. In fact, in the HtR Storyteller's Companion which lays all this out, straight up says that God has disappeared.<br /> <br /> Also in that same section where it talks about what's behind the Imbuing, it never once refers to the August Personage or the Celestial Bureaucracy. Instead it uses 'god' or 'the Creator of All' while their servants are simply referred to as the 'Ministers'. In fact, it goes on to separate them from the Messengers, making them the agents of the Ministers carrying out their instruction on Earth.<br /> <br /> The whole section is presented in an extremely barebones (intentionally I suspect as WoD always disliked giving a 100% concrete answer to these kinds of things) to the point that we don't know where the Queen and Dragon fall into this. Are they the Ministers or the Messengers? We don't know.<br /> <br /> As for why, the STComp also explains this. The Ministers know the end is coming and cannot be stopped. They are Imbuing people in hopes of making the upcoming apocalyptic age as short as possible. They know it's against God's will but without God to direct, they don't know what else to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ten Thousand Immortals are never even mentioned once when the Demons were waging war against the Heavenly Host at all. None of the Demons from D:tF even know a single thing about the Yama Kings. They don't even know the Middle or High Umbra even exist. It also breaks the notion that the August Personage of Jade and the Abrahamic God described in D:tF are the same at all. If the logic is that the August Personage of Jade and Abrahamic God are the same, why did they imprison the rebel Elohim but left the Yama Kings alone to remain active? </div> </div> </div>Probably because as DtF presents it, God basically erased the existence of the war from Humanity and the Earth. The Ten Thousand Immortals likely arose after all that.<br /> <br /> By that same token, the Yama Kings didn't exist back then because their original purpose didn't exist back then. You see the original Yama Kings were created to purify the souls of the deceased for reincarnation. Something that Humanity didn't need until after the Age of Wrath as prior to that Humanity was of a more simple nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Imbued from Hunter: The Reckoning were supposed to be the-coming-back of the Wan Xian, who were the precursors of the Kuei-Jin; the uncorrupted, uncursed versions who were granted a grand spiritual commission to rid the world of monsters. They're one of the same, just from different ages of time.<br /> <br /> I think this is why the Imbued were ultimately cut. A lot of writers in WoD seem to have a grudge with ANYTHING related to or greatly connected with KotE, so much to this point they're literally cutting out the most focal splats from their own game.. and literally replacing them... again, this 5th edition is.. not good. </div> </div> </div>Except not really, not as much as VtM was connected to KotE. Like I've said, the connections between KotE and HtR are all behind the scenes, things that we the player know but the PCs are completely unaware of. VtM on the other hand had the Cainites and Wan Kuei clashing over the years. The Week of Nightmares saw [Ravnos] fighting a trio of Elder Wan Kuei.<br /> <br /> The only time it comes up in HtR is in the Storyteller's Companion, a book for Storytellers, in a barebones explanation that never once says August Personage of Jade, Celestial Bureaucracy, Scarlet Queen, Ebon Dragon or Wan Kuei.<br /> <br /> The story as we know it was pieced together by readers from multiple books across several lines rather than a single official source. They could have pushed all that back into the murky shadows, taking an approach like with M20 and it's metaplot with a sidebox saying maybe that's what's going on, maybe it's not.<br /> <br /> Hell, they could have played into the Imbueds' own ignorance on these matters and gave us a bunch of conflicting stories on their origins on what they believe is going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T22:39:17-07:00","id":1464242,"title":"","content":"Alright.. let's get into this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you expect VtM to explain the backstories of WtA, MtAs, CtD and WtO? No.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because.. by the simple margin that VTM was the first game in the WoD franchise, it makes sense that it didn't go into the backstories of the other lines. And every game after it tried to be its own thing but at the same time left breadcrumbs to fit against each other nicely, albeit with some components being more incompatible with other things. This is completely different to how DtF barged in, didn't care for what it attempting to tie-in to, and hilariously left plotholes in its own line by doing so and messed with the lore of other lines in the same breadth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why should DtF be obliged to explain the backstories of all the other lines? Especially when it's established in the first or second chapter of the Rulebook that memories of the Fallen are damaged because of their imprisonment in the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>....Because it deliberately reached over and hard-powered through material of things it didn't understand in a really awkward way? It also did have some obligation to actually be a real good wrap-up splat for Classic World of Darkness, explaining how in an actual awesome and original way all the splats tie-in into eachother (its literally a splat about the apparent way the WoD was formed... you'd think they'd pull all the stops to incorporate all the splats of the past years with some moderate write-ups, but no.. and the only time other splats are used or mentioned, is to prop-up and remind you that this still WoD, and not some Book of Genesis fanfiction) .<br /> <br /> There is a recurrent myth in the WoD community that everything wasn't made to be cohesive with another.. and part of that is maybe true, but in many other ways with each new line; things were shaping up to one cohesive WoD universe. But then DtF went on a bible fanfiction spree and just brought things back to square-one before cWoD got its plug pulled.<br /> <br /> And also, remember, the quote you brought up is a poem made by Lucifer. As far as we know, he was never put into the Abyss, so I don't why you bring it up. In vacuum where we both take up sources from both KotE and DtF, evening them against each other, Lucifer wouldn't know anything about the Ebon Dragon or Scarlet Queen because they were part of the Celestial Bureaucracy and not part of any of the Elohim Houses or part of the Heaven Host, the one formed to fight against the rebel Elohim.<br /> <br /> If the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen were really associated with the Abrahamic God and not the August Personage of Jade, they would've been Demons/Rebel Elohim for Imbuing humans since the earliest times. Yet the source you reference from Lucifer, says they're the last Angels.. which they couldn't be, since they would have been casted to Abyss and turned into Demons. This goes to show how D:tF is contradictory to its own plotline (since the entire conflict in the beginning were Angels that chose to interfere with Humanity and then loyalist Angels along with the Abrahamic God who didn't want interference, aka keep Adam and Eve as dumb-dumbs in Eden).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or in the case of the Fallen, beings that were a torturous state for eons and have had their minds have been damaged by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this source from Days of Fire about the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen is referenced from Lucifer though. But the fact that he does is pure plot-hole, for the reasons I noted above. He never went to Abyss or had his mind rendered by it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">God basically erased the existence of the war from Humanity and the Earth</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies for this, since I haven't read Demon in a long time and purely going off memory here; but when did the Abrahamic God erased the war from Humanity or the Earth? If this actually happened, than D:tF should be very different. Or is this headcanon, so to speak?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By that same token, the Yama Kings didn't exist back then because their original purpose didn't exist back then. You see the original Yama Kings were created to purify the souls of the deceased for reincarnation. Something that Humanity didn't need until after the Age of Wrath as prior to that Humanity was of a more simple nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet you're completely incorrect on this. The Yama Kings were congruently active when the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen were active. The Yama Kings are literally the entire reason why the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen made the Wan Xian/Ten Thousand Immortals in the first place. If they weren't active or didn't exist at the same time, then their would be no Imbued at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kindred of the East, pg. 44, Second Age</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soon thereafter, the <b>Ebon Dragon</b> and the <b>Scarlet Queen</b><br /> learned to breathe, and as they breathed, the Ten Thousand<br /> Things of matter and spirit began to take shape. Where breathed<br /> the Dragon, spirits and properties of Yin appeared; where breathed<br /> the Queen, spirits and properties of Yang took form. Soon, the<br /> worlds of matter and spirit had been breathed into existence. Gods<br /> and dragons walked the young, vibrant world, and to them Heaven<br /> ordained duties and positions in the Spirit Courts.<br /> However, as the celestial beings gravitated to their specific<br /> realms, some escaped the notice and tutelage of the Dragon and<br /> the Queen. These beings, deprived of proper instruction,<br /> neglected their duties and failed to make obeisance to the will<br /> of Heaven. Certain creatures became dualisticatty opposed to<br /> others, while others combined Yin and Yang in unwholesome<br /> imbalance. Demons and mpnsters, greedy devourers of Chi,<br /> appeared during the Second Age. *<br /> The worst of these creatures made lairs deep within,the<br /> wildest regions of the worlds. Disregarding the August<br /> Personage's authority, these demons drained entire regions of<br /> Chi, then claimed the blighted and diseased lands as their own.<br /> The demons warred among themselves, and the mightiest<br /> forced the other demons to swear fealty to them. Calling<br /> themselves <b>Yama Kings</b>, these archdemons ravaged their surroundings<br /> and plotted to garner vast amounts of Chi for their<br /> own selfish appetites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even further on, the Yama Kings predate humanity as well; directly conflicting with your headcanon claim that the Yama Kinds didn't exist until humans came into existence:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kindred of the East, pg. 44, Second Age</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Humans</b> also<br /> came into being during the Second Age, a product of the<br /> Dragon and Queen's love for each other. This last act, in<br /> particular, was not received kindly by the monstrous <b>Yama<br /> Kings</b>. Jealous of their fairer brethren, the <b>Yama Kings</b> stalked<br /> amid the first mortals, afflicting upon them sickness, terror and<br /> destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also by some allusion, its referenced that the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen made humanity.. which definitely goes against stuff about them being part of the Abrahamic Heavenly Host from DtF- but this is a slight digression.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kindred of the East, pg. 44, The Coming of the Wan Xian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And so, to protect its newborn charges, the August Personage<br /> bestowed its favor upon certain of the <b>most superior<br /> mortals</b>, and a new race of beings was born.<br /> The members of this race were not called Kuei-jin then \u2014<br /> they were the Wan Xian, the Ten Thousand Immortals. Selected<br /> for their wisdom, power and balance, the Wan Xian were<br /> neither wholly mortal nor wholly spirit, but possessed elements<br /> of both. To become Wan Xian, a mortal soul had to cross into<br /> the spirit worlds, then enter the Middle Kingdom once more.<br /> Thus attuned to the world of spirit, the Wan Xian could draw<br /> upon the stuff of the Yin and Yang Worlds \u2014 Chi \u2014 and utilize<br /> it for sustenance and power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually come to think of it, I was WRONG that it was the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen that <i>first</i> started up the Imbued. The Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen just restarted it during the Sixth Age, but it was the August Personage of Jade who basically started them up.<br /> <br /> Either way, this directly puts more points in my argument why the August Personage of Jade and Abrahamic God presented in DtF are completely different entities. One deliberately enhanced humanity to fight against demons, while the latter one tried to fight the demons who tried to enhance humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole section is presented in an extremely barebones (intentionally I suspect as WoD always disliked giving a 100% concrete answer to these kinds of things) to the point that we don't know where the Queen and Dragon fall into this. Are they the Ministers or the Messengers? We don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all solved through supporting evidence from KotE and from sources above. Also, its kinda obvious they're alluding to the Celestial Bureaucracy when they're talking about Ministers. It should be obvious. I never seen anything in D:tF where they talked about Ministers at all.<br /> <br /> Honestly, this whole argument is moot; because again, HtR had little to do with DtF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 10-17-2021, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T06:06:51-07:00","id":1464249,"title":"","content":"The whole 4th page of this thread is devoted to an In-depth metaliterary discussion about where the Imbuing came from, spanning no less than 3 game lines, two of which have not been updated since 2004: I feel this is quite the explanation for why the Imbued will not be their own thing! <br /> <br /> It seems 5th edition is going more and more towards being a soft reboot of the game, inspired and in many instances derived by prior editions, but not bound by a philological approach. <br /> <br /> Mind you, I actually liked the Imbued, I still hope they use some of the concept: they mentioned Convinction, Creeds and powers, so perhaps we will simply have &quot;softer Imbued&quot;, like powers connected to Creed and powered by Convinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 10-17-2021, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T06:26:27-07:00","id":1464251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464209#post1464209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or maybe these unnecessary reductions are due to them not even knowing the past material or not even bothering to review it.</div> </div> </div> </div>W5, H5 and new material for V5 are developed by none less than Justin Achilli, the man who developed World of Darkness between the end of the 90s and 2004.<br /> <br /> V5 was framed with help by Mark Rein Hagen, the man who actually invented the game, and still is being worked on by extremely knowledgeable freelance, as many materials are written by Onyx Path. Those same freelancers were also involved in the V5 corebook. <br /> <br /> Even new authors, the cadre coming from Sweden and northern Europe, are all long time WOD fans, many of them coming from the LARP scene or involved with the failed WOD MMORPG. Outstar is a top WOD expert. <br /> <br /> Surely, the 5th edition has taken some strong and stern choices, on tone, gameplay and plot: but those who are working on it definitely know and love the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T07:22:02-07:00","id":1464253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel this is quite the explanation for why the Imbued will not be their own thing!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is hardly any excuse whatsoever. HtR by itself in a vacuum by itself was simple: the Messengers give the powers and now the Imbued have to fight monsters to protect the world. But just enjoying some deeper aspects of the background lore is not even half-way justifiable to remove the Imbued from their own damn game. It's just lazy and cheap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">W5, H5 and new material for V5 are developed by none less than Justin Achilli, the man who developed World of Darkness between the end of the 90s and 2004.</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion so far with him being put back-in-saddle is extremely low at this point. When he first got put on, I thought things were going to be back to more cWoD lore and even mechanics (what a naive pitiful thought).<br /> <br /> From how V5 still feels like an ungodly mash-up of VtR and horrible metaplot, W5 rumored to have tribes being removed and the Umbra (one of the most main focal points of the game) will be harder to travel to, and this with &quot;&quot;&quot;H5&quot;&quot;&quot; with no Imbued in their own game; to the worst of all, where the Sabbat have been rendered to antagonist-only metaplot elements... I hardly think anything good of the current writers' work for these 5 edition roll-outs.<br /> <br /> Many people even posited this, but if they're not even going to put the Imbued in their own game, why even bare its title name? Oh wait: easy cash-grabs from &quot;brand recognition&quot; alone and the fact that Reckoning, right next to Masquerade, had one good game way in the past. Paradox probably saw that factor and that's the reason why they even jumpstarted HtR this early, even behind W5. But I don't even know how they think this will work, since the Hunter: The Reckoning game way back in the early 2000s(?) was heavily based on the plot elements and lore of the Imbued.<br /> <br /> The minuscule amount of people who might even look in H5, from playing the game before and getting interested from that, will probably be bewildered by the complete 180 of everything they saw from the video game. It also just goes to show that WoD being acquired by a video game company is just bad, because they'll always make decisions that will lead to possible video game tie-ins or future potential for new video games, instead of taking tabletop and its past indepth material seriously.<br /> <br /> Generally, this whole nonsense with the Imbued being taken out from their own game is foolish. Who do they expect to come in and be halfway interested in H5? Beside the few 5 Edition general loyalists, I hardly doubt anyone beyond that small sector of the WoD fandom will care about H5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 10-17-2021, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T07:28:36-07:00","id":1464254,"title":"","content":"Honestly, who or what gave the imbued powers was irrelevant for the game itself. The biggest &quot;revelations&quot; came from short references within other games drunk on their self importance or the pretty crappy Time of Judgement book that tried to do everything at once. It was something to be built upon and explored within the needs of the chronicle. And just like all the other games had different takes on what was going on in them compared the others, Hunter did a lot of its own. That was its charm and that allowed you take what you wanted and what you needed. So saying that their &quot;mysteries&quot; are stuck in lost games making them irrelevant is a bit silly, as that's the least of their problems (and one exacerbated by fans with extensive libraries and desires to make things click together).<br /> <br /> As for what the new Paradox White Wolf crew is trying to do. Sure they started as ascended fans and hired a number of people with sterling RPG credentials, but they had a very clear vision of what this new WoD would be - this would be a WoD they felt was &quot;correct&quot; and damned be anyone who thinks it should be something else. And while vision and drive are great if you need to build something up and get new people onboard, their vision pretty much fizzed out with Vampire 1st edition as the be-and-all of the WoD. They saw it as the pinnacle and perfection without caring much where things evolved along the way. This was reiterated with their commentary about other lines where they literally went by memes and outrage interpretations of the cringiest material White Wolf had made and actually tried to fix through the ages. Watching their approach is not encouraging in the slightest as it's a way that says that there is only one way to play these games - theirs.<br /> <br /> Justin Achilli is someone I trust on topics Vampire. On anything not Vampire or anything crossing over with Vampire I don't. In general It's a flawed perception to believe that people writing these games have extensive knowledge of other game lines or even necessarily care about things beyond their contribution. Look at Phil Brucatto, his mage was very much a statement to his own views and what he feels the game should be. It's sure as hell a step away from what Bridges had as his own vision. A lot of the people writing this stuff were doing it for a paycheck and given guidelines whats expected, they did that and were done. Occasionally they introduced clever bylines and references and stuff that made them happy, but the majority of the work was informed by the people that set their goals and the need to finish a product. This is the same with the New White Wolf crew.<br /> <br /> Edit: Please note that this is not a diss on the people writing for these games, they are usually passionate and have their own ideas and visions on how they want to make the games work. Their contributions are what made these games better and more interesting and I appreciate their work, even if I had ongoing holy wars when I was younger and dumber with some of them. I'm just slightly cynical about how the sausage is made, how much time people have, how much money they get and who makes these final decisions on what a final <i>product </i>has to look like.<br /> <br /> The funny bit here is that each of these games evolved quite a bit along the way. They evolved within the halls of White Wolf and later Onyx Path, but they evolved at every table and every part of the world where people convened and played these games to give them more life and corrected course towards what they needed. This is pretty much why people care so much about the WoD - its something they built up through the ages along with the material that evolved with them. Again, this is something I feel Wizards understood when they made 5E D&amp;D as they did. And this is something Paradox doesn't seem to get so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 10-17-2021, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T07:28:36-07:00","id":1464255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464251#post1464251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W5, H5 and new material for V5 are developed by none less than Justin Achilli, the man who developed World of Darkness between the end of the 90s and 2004.<br /> <br /> V5 was framed with help by Mark Rein Hagen, the man who actually invented the game, and still is being worked on by extremely knowledgeable freelance, as many materials are written by Onyx Path. Those same freelancers were also involved in the V5 corebook. <br /> <br /> Even new authors, the cadre coming from Sweden and northern Europe, are all long time WOD fans, many of them coming from the LARP scene or involved with the failed WOD MMORPG. Outstar is a top WOD expert. <br /> <br /> Surely, the 5th edition has taken some strong and stern choices, on tone, gameplay and plot: but those who are working on it definitely know and love the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. Justin Achilli was also right there when the WoD was blown up and rebooted the first time. It might be that he's genuinely 'over' the WoD as it was, and is only really interested in doing it again if he gets to make it vastly different this time.<br /> <br /> So it may be true that they *loved* the game as it was, in the past, and now only love it because it's become something almost but not quite entirely unlike the WoD (to steal a bit of Douglas Adams there).<br /> <br /> The game that each of us loves, therefore, isn't necessarily the same thing as the game the devs love. It's a Theseus's ship situation. Even moreso for HTR, I think, than VTM. But perhaps that's because VTM is a more beloved game, so harder for nuWW to completely rewrite while still cashing in on the brand name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T09:14:12-07:00","id":1464258,"title":"","content":"Justin Achilli was also the developer of Rage until it was cancelled (Rage Across Las Vegas is a crossover fever dream that does not count), so one would imagine he knows something about Werewolf matters, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T09:56:39-07:00","id":1464263,"title":"","content":"Wasn't JA mostly involved with organised play and events for Rage? Couldn't find many references to this and his bibliography didn't list it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T17:09:38-07:00","id":1464289,"title":"","content":"While Justin has worked on WtA, he was not &quot;the man who developed World of Darkness between the end of the 90s and 2004&quot; he was the VtM developer. He didn't tell Ethan Skemp what to do with WtA, or Jesse Heinig what to do with Mage, etc. There was, in fact, a very public (if insignificant in the long run) disagreement between the three of them on how XP worked in Revised, of which the official stance from WW was whatever they say is how things work in their game line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T18:00:11-07:00","id":1464293,"title":"","content":"I bet H5 has really good sales. And you know what they say: \u201cSales are the one true God\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Tbh I should admit that one reason I didn\u2019t like HtR is because of the color. The books (I never played the game but I did read the PDFs) were the same awful shade of orange as the cheese in vending machine crackers. I hope they don\u2019t repeat the same mistake with H5. Marketing is important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T18:18:14-07:00","id":1464296,"title":"","content":"Man I wish this forum had multi-quote...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464242#post1464242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright.. let's get into this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because.. by the simple margin that VTM was the first game in the WoD franchise, it makes sense that it didn't go into the backstories of the other lines. And every game after it tried to be its own thing but at the same time left breadcrumbs to fit against each other nicely, albeit with some components being more incompatible with other things. This is completely different to how DtF barged in, didn't care for what it attempting to tie-in to, and hilariously left plotholes in its own line by doing so and messed with the lore of other lines in the same breadth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ....Because it deliberately reached over and hard-powered through material of things it didn't understand in a really awkward way? It also did have some obligation to actually be a real good wrap-up splat for Classic World of Darkness, explaining how in an actual awesome and original way all the splats tie-in into eachother (its literally a splat about the apparent way the WoD was formed... you'd think they'd pull all the stops to incorporate all the splats of the past years with some moderate write-ups, but no.. and the only time other splats are used or mentioned, is to prop-up and remind you that this still WoD, and not some Book of Genesis fanfiction) .<br /> <br /> There is a recurrent myth in the WoD community that everything wasn't made to be cohesive with another.. and part of that is maybe true, but in many other ways with each new line; things were shaping up to one cohesive WoD universe. But then DtF went on a bible fanfiction spree and just brought things back to square-one before cWoD got its plug pulled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except DtF has always admitted that the Fallen's memories are damaged and questionable as well as the fact that early Earth was... weird and abstract before God reacted to what the Fallen were doing and changed/broke the world into what it is in the rest of the WoD. I will be talk more about that below but as it stands, DtF admits that their backstory is strange, incomplete and contradictory, kind of like everybody else's. The only one that has the answers in DtF is Lucifer and he's not exactly going around talking to people anymore than Caine or Lillith is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And also, remember, the quote you brought up is a poem made by Lucifer. As far as we know, he was never put into the Abyss, so I don't why you bring it up. In vacuum where we both take up sources from both KotE and DtF, evening them against each other, Lucifer wouldn't know anything about the Ebon Dragon or Scarlet Queen because they were part of the Celestial Bureaucracy and not part of any of the Elohim Houses or part of the Heaven Host, the one formed to fight against the rebel Elohim.<br /> <br /> If the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen were really associated with the Abrahamic God and not the August Personage of Jade, they would've been Demons/Rebel Elohim for Imbuing humans since the earliest times. Yet the source you reference from Lucifer, says they're the last Angels.. which they couldn't be, since they would have been casted to Abyss and turned into Demons. This goes to show how D:tF is contradictory to its own plotline (since the entire conflict in the beginning were Angels that chose to interfere with Humanity and then loyalist Angels along with the Abrahamic God who didn't want interference, aka keep Adam and Eve as dumb-dumbs in Eden).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, this source from Days of Fire about the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen is referenced from Lucifer though. But the fact that he does is pure plot-hole, for the reasons I noted above. He never went to Abyss or had his mind rendered by it. </div> </div> </div>Actually the first of the Ten Thousand Immortals/Imbued may have been there. I had forgotten about this but there was during the War the rise of a new host of warriors on the side of Heaven, referred to as the Malhim. While it's unclear what they were and how they came to be, there are enough hints there for the suggestion that it was the first Immortals/Imbued to be viable.<br /> <br /> There's also another thing I didn't mention from Days of Fire. Those verses are divided into four sections, each section starting with an accounting of the Angels, how many there are and how many have Fallen. And while they don't say it directly, one can calculate from the numbers how many have been destroyed. The final section starts with the following:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [43]<br /> The Angels of The One Giver<br /> Shall number two.<br /> The Demons of the Abyss shall number<br /> Two million and two thousand and one hundred and ninety and nine.<br /> The Demons of the World shall number five.<br /> While one remains<br /> As ever, with no place to wake or slumber. </div> </div> </div>We have the Fallen trapped in the Abyss, the five Earthbound, Lucifer and then two Angels still loyal to God (The One Giver as Days calls them). And the only time in the rest of the section Angels are brought up is the previously quoted Verse 72. In other words, the last two Angels are the Scarlet Queen and the Ebon Dragon.<br /> <br /> There is also some speculation that the Queen's Angelic Name may have been Ziana, Seraph of the Cycle, leader of the Sixth House, who stayed loyal and has some vague connections to Gaia and the Fera but that's a whole other rabbit hole of vague material across multiple books and lines.<br /> <br /> And if they are Angels, why wouldn't Lucifer know about the pair? Lucifer was at the top of their hierarchy before the Fall and all the Angels came into existence before the Fall. Doubly so if the Queen is Ziana as she too would be at the top of the Angelic Hierarchy and he would have spoken to her many times in the course of their duties. Houses of the Fallen even confirms that Ziana was at some of the debates that led to the Fall.<br /> <br /> If you're referring to Lucifer knowing about their actions following his defeat, it is possible he was aware of them. While his powers were diminished by the Fall and likely after his defeat, we know he wasn't rendered utterly powerless as in the metaplot he makes a manifestation display in LA around the Rev Ed era.<br /> <br /> Also if God and the APJ are different beings then you are saying that two different Gods created two different worlds and presumably two different mankinds at the same time and the same place and then... what exactly? Decide that they each get half or something? Does that meant the WoD has two Gods?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apologies for this, since I haven't read Demon in a long time and purely going off memory here; but when did the Abrahamic God erased the war from Humanity or the Earth? If this actually happened, than D:tF should be very different. Or is this headcanon, so to speak? </div> </div> </div>Actually I kind of mixed two things up. The first part of it was the above mentioned God changing/breaking the nature of the world. In the Rulebook it's talked about how during Primordial Earth things were... well different for a lack of a better word. Creationism and Evolution were both correct. That Earth could be made in seven days and a billion years. Adam and Eve were real but also metaphors for early Man evolved from apes. <br /> <br /> Then the Fall happened and God responded by changing the nature of the world or breaking it depending on who you ask. As it's presented in DtF, it comes across that it was the moment where the Primordial Earth became the Earth as we understand within the World of Darkness. It was after that moment that the war between the Angels and Fallen would start, when Caine would kill Abel, the Fera would be created, the first Mages would arise and various other possible origins of WoD lines<br /> <br /> As for Mankind forgetting the Angels, the Fallen, the Age of Wrath and all that, that happened later towards the end of the Age with cause a bit vague. Though according to the Rulebook, Abel's tribe who sided with God and Michael were turned back to their pre-Fall state of ignorance though it was then noted that it didn't as long as 'Consciousness is contagious' and the war basically ensured that going back to before the Fall was impossible. <br /> <br /> The general consensus is that Humanity willfully embraced forgetting and ignorance (not the primitive ignorance of the pre-Fall, just general ignorance) in the later stages of the war or after it to escape from the horror of... well everything going on around them. Not unlike Delirium of WtA. Something so traumatizing that it scars the collective memory. By the same token, there's talk of the various works of the Fallen being erased from the Earth by the war and natural disasters, leaving little left to discovered and remembered. The only one that seemed to be exempt from this was Caine because he was vampire by that point and no longer human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yet you're completely incorrect on this. The Yama Kings were congruently active when the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen were active. The Yama Kings are literally the entire reason why the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen made the Wan Xian/Ten Thousand Immortals in the first place. If they weren't active or didn't exist at the same time, then their would be no Imbued at all. </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. I did mix up some part of the lore but not the core of it. As per the book, The Thousand Hells, which deals with the Yama Kings and their domains, the original Kings did indeed exist but they were limited to the Umbra (the Yin and Yang Worlds) but eventually the APJ tasked them with the 'instructing and rehabilitating the wayward souls of the Middle Kingdom' which for a time they did until they started to get a little bit too much enjoy in their work and a lust for more, leading them to becoming utterly corrupt and eventually create the Thousand Hells. The way it's written in The Thousand Hells (and for that matter the KotE Rulebook and the DA book, Blood and Silk), fighting the Yama Kings was a task later assigned to the Immortals when they became a threat. But it was one of many tasks assigned to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually come to think of it, I was WRONG that it was the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen that <i>first</i> started up the Imbued. The Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen just restarted it during the Sixth Age, but it was the August Personage of Jade who basically started them up.<br /> <br /> Either way, this directly puts more points in my argument why the August Personage of Jade and Abrahamic God presented in DtF are completely different entities. One deliberately enhanced humanity to fight against demons, while the latter one tried to fight the demons who tried to enhance humanity. </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. A big point of DtF is that the Angels whether Fallen or not, don't really know or understand what God's planning or thinking. Like we know God called back the Angels after the War yet at the same time we know two Angels, not Fallen, remained. Or possibly returned later. It is a little vague in that regard. But had God not wanted every Angel to leave Earth and never return, how is it that two managed it? The only real answer is that God allowed it or ordered it.<br /> <br /> If the Malhim and the Immortals were one and the same, then they were created for than just war. After all, we know the Immortals were doing far more than fighting battles against demons and the like. Which in turn plays into the powers of the Imbued. Plenty of Edges have little to no practical application in combat. If the Imbued are lesser iterations of the Immortals than by that same token many of the Immortals' powers were for things other than combat.<br /> <br /> Also, I kind of alluded to it above when I talked about Abel's Tribe but when the war became violent, it dragged Humanity into it which was also another thing that forced Abel's Tribe to regain their consciousness as they were also pulled into it and those that didn't regard consciousness were basically slaughtered like animals. And based on the few comments about the Malhim we have, they were one of the few things Heaven had that the Fallen feared such was their formidable power. Also by that point, the War had become particularly bloody and awful while the Fallen were living up their name as Demons. Giving those humans worthy of it among Abel's Tribe the power to help end the madness and suffering wouldn't be out of the question.<br /> <br /> Of course that's assuming that it all wasn't part of God's plan which is it's own matter entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is all solved through supporting evidence from KotE and from sources above. Also, its kinda obvious they're alluding to the Celestial Bureaucracy when they're talking about Ministers. It should be obvious. I never seen anything in D:tF where they talked about Ministers at all. </div> </div> </div>Actually Minister and Ministry does pop up in DtF. In the modern day, Ministers are the Fallen's equivalent to the Kindred's Primogen, the senior council around the Tyrant (the Prince equivalent). So the title is there in the DtF. And not just in the modern sense. In the Rulebook, Pg. 30, during the debates between the Angels over what should be done about Humanity, Belial refers to himself as his fellow Angels as 'ministers of Creation'. And I've spotted a few other instances in the line of Angels or Fallen referring to themselves similarly as Ministers of Creation or Existence.<br /> <br /> Plus the word has been associated in the real world with things Angelic and Demonic. So it's not really a stretch to suggest that it could just as easily refer to Ministers in the Biblical and Angelic sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T18:52:33-07:00","id":1464298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464293#post1464293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bet H5 has really good sales. And you know what they say: \u201cSales are the one true God\u2026\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Define &quot;good.&quot;<br /> <br /> If Paradox sells a lot of copies compared to what Onyx Path usually sells is that good? Well, did we take all the costs involved in wider scale distribution into account? There's a reason why movies aren't financial bombs or successes just based on ticket sales, but ticket sales vs. production costs. Is a movie that costs $50 million to make, distribute, and market, and sells $100 million in tickets better or worse sales than a move that costs $300 million to make, and sells $300 million tickets?<br /> <br /> The first movie made $50 million dollars. The second movie made no money, but sold six times the tickets.<br /> <br /> RPGs are always a shot in the dark for consumers to judge these things, because we get very rough estimates of sales, and no information on production costs, for most big name RPGs (smaller indie companies might be more transparent). <br /> <br /> And, there's also the goals of the company to account for. If Paradox doesn't care about profit, but about the appearance of success, selling a lot of copies even if there is no profit, to help market more profitable aspects of the brand (like future video games), then that also changes the definition of &quot;good,&quot; compared to OPP, which needs profitable RPG sales to survive as a company.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tbh I should admit that one reason I didn\u2019t like HtR is because of the color. </div> </div> </div>O...K...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The books (I never played the game but I did read the PDFs) were the same awful shade of orange as the cheese in vending machine crackers. I hope they don\u2019t repeat the same mistake with H5. Marketing is important. </div> </div> </div>Marketing is more complicated than pleasing one person's opinion on cover color.<br /> <br /> Want to know what the old HtR books did that was important? The popped. Looking at a wall of early 2000s RPGs by just the spines (including other WoD books) it's a see of dark colors, mostly black, some browns, some greens, maybe some reds and purple, and so on. Then there's this vibrant contrasting orange there. Standing out in a crowd is important.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T20:00:14-07:00","id":1464305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually the first of the Ten Thousand Immortals/Imbued may have been there. I had forgotten about this but there was during the War the rise of a new host of warriors on the side of Heaven, referred to as the Malhim. While it's unclear what they were and how they came to be, there are enough hints there for the suggestion that it was the first Immortals/Imbued to be viable.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;May&quot; is very flimsy. And looking it up at a cursory glance, the &quot;Malhim&quot; were likened much more akin to the Garou than anything that had to do with the Imbued. Also again, looking up actual KotE source material, the Ten Thousand Immortals/Wan Xian were an integral force since the Second Age and throughout KotE lore.. not some throwaway new enemy for the Fallen that were just forgotten later on. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also some speculation that the Queen's Angelic Name may have been Ziana, Seraph of the Cycle, leader of the Sixth House, who stayed loyal and has some vague connections to Gaia and the Fera but that's a whole other rabbit hole of vague material across multiple books and lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I wouldn't say its a rabbit hole or really complex at all. Its just one of those moments where DtF flogged through material and just name-dropped anything for shock-trill value, even if it made little sense or just not cared for what lore would be awkwardly hammed around. DtF tried to heavily attribute that Gaia isn't a Celestine at all, but just some Angel who metamorphosed into it and at the (<i>checks tab</i>) same time implying that this Angel, also is the Scarlet Queen... real awkward. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">why wouldn't Lucifer know about the pair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because its just a plothole and to prop up Lucifer's Gary Stu-like status? The Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Queen are radically different in KotE, from what minor name-drops/allusions they are given in DtF. In KotE, the Ebon Dragon and the Scarlet Queen themselves are the highest in the Celestial Bureaucracy, just under APJ, and there is nothing (obviously since it was made way before) about Lucifer or Western-style Angels in KotE lore. Lucifer was not associated or in the Celestial Bureaucracy at all and DtF heavily relies on half, or not most, of the Book of Genesis for its setting; albeit with modifications of course.<br /> <br /> This is completely different from the meta-view of KotE. There is no Cain and Abel, nor Adam and Eve (which are very important plot elements for DtF). Everything is focused on the &quot;Middle-Kingdom&quot; or China, so to speak, while DtF is focused on the Middle-East. KotE heavily draws from Hinduism, Buddhism, and Taoism. DtF heavily draws from Judaism and Christianity. There are completely different from one another. Which pivots into my other point: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if God and the APJ are different beings then you are saying that two different Gods created two different worlds and presumably two different mankinds at the same time and the same place and then... what exactly? Decide that they each get half or something? Does that meant the WoD has two Gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple answer, yes.<br /> <br /> In other threads discussing DtF way back on this site, it was brought up from a user that in Mummy: The Resurrection, there were references that there were in fact multiple gods and they each had their own division of Earth they could influence. Its very ad-hoc, but it can explain the vast discrepancies between the Abrahamic God and August Personage of Jade; as well as the point about lore regarding Horus and the overall Egyptian Pantheon. With Mage alone, there have been confirmed to be multiple gods that exist in the High Umbra. <br /> <br /> And this makes sense for some margin of argument for a unified WoD, without one splat hamfisting everything everything else. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I kind of mixed two things up. The first part of it was the above mentioned God changing/breaking the nature of the world. In the Rulebook it's talked about how during Primordial Earth things were... well different for a lack of a better word. Creationism and Evolution were both correct. That Earth could be made in seven days and a billion years. Adam and Eve were real but also metaphors for early Man evolved from apes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already know about the DtF's &quot;multilayer reality&quot; tidbit. It still has nothing to do with the war, since this was way after. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A big point of DtF is that the Angels whether Fallen or not, don't really know or understand what God's planning or thinking</div> </div> </div> </div>Annnd the entire conflict in the first place, irregardless, were about the rebel Angels who wanted to grant Humanity knowledge and powers, and the ones who remained to the Abrahamic God's dictate that Humanity should be left stagnate. The August Personage of Jade, however, didn't rely on Angels to fight the Yama Kings; it immediately made the the Wan Xian/Ten Thousand Immortals. These are clearly two different entities, with different objectives, and different metaphysical means on how they made their areas of Earth. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But had God not wanted every Angel to leave Earth and never return, how is it that two managed it? The only real answer is that God allowed it or ordered it</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe, just maybe, the people who made DtF just wanted to name-drop anything haphazardly from many other lines out of place, with no meaning other than to forcefully tie-in most WoD with bible fanfiction; than come up with an actual unique creationist origin for WoD? Something akin to Exalted would have been much more superior and original.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T21:00:01-07:00","id":1464307,"title":"","content":"Just saw this thread and got excited for a moment. Then saw immediately that the Imbued are gone?<br /> <br /> Damn it, why do they keep removing everything I enjoyed about the older editions? Was my group just &quot;enjoying things wrong&quot; the whole time? Because it sure seems like we were.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Also why the fuck are they calling this Hunter: the Reckoning 5e if you aren't playing one of the Imbued, the literal character splat of Hunter: the Reckoning, and apparently those guys don't even exist anymore? If there's no Imbued then this game is not a new edition of Hunter: the Reckoning. Full stop. It's a different and new game entirely and one that has nothing to do with Hunter: the Reckoning.<br /> <br /> I'm definitely glad I noticed this thread. HtR is my brother's absolutely favorite RPG of all time. If he'd seen there was a 5th edition he would have bought it in a heartbeat and then started texting me at 3 in the morning asking, &quot;Dude, where's the Edges at? I don't see the Edges.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-18-2021, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T23:17:15-07:00","id":1464316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464307#post1464307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saw this thread and got excited for a moment. Then saw immediately that the Imbued are gone?<br /> <br /> Damn it, why do they keep removing everything I enjoyed about the older editions? Was my group just &amp;quot;enjoying things wrong&amp;quot; the whole time? Because it sure seems like we were.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Also why the fuck are they calling this Hunter: the Reckoning 5e if you aren't playing one of the Imbued, the literal character splat of Hunter: the Reckoning, and apparently those guys don't even exist anymore? If there's no Imbued then this game is not a new edition of Hunter: the Reckoning. Full stop. It's a different and new game entirely and one that has nothing to do with Hunter: the Reckoning.<br /> <br /> I'm definitely glad I noticed this thread. HtR is my brother's absolutely favorite RPG of all time. If he'd seen there was a 5th edition he would have bought it in a heartbeat and then started texting me at 3 in the morning asking, &amp;quot;Dude, where's the Edges at? I don't see the Edges.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks like there are Edges, but they're more an assembly of Numina and elite Backgrounds than the Edges of old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T00:20:33-07:00","id":1464318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464316#post1464316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It looks like there are Edges, but they're more an assembly of Numina and elite Backgrounds than the Edges of old.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it looks like they're going to reuse some of the old names and terms but radically change up the concepts they're linked to, like they did with the name of the game. <br /> <br /> Shame. I thought my disappoint with 5e had reached its zenith and there wasn't anything they could do to disappoint me further, but her we are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T00:45:15-07:00","id":1464334,"title":"","content":"Okay. I think together with the announced <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463829-new-w5-info-from-the-14th-of-october-twitch\">W5 changes</a>, one thing is more and more clear:<br /> <br /> <br /> 5th Edition is something new. Something that drastically changes some old lore and metaplot, introduces CoD mechanisms, and its very own overall flair and mood. They are breaking with a lot of old concepts, old lore, and are not afraid of tossing a lot of new mechanics and things in.<br /> <br /> This is not a bad thing, per se. People have spoken in favor of combining OWoDisms with CoD mechanics into a shiny new package.<br /> <br /> But.<br /> <br /> BUT.<br /> <br /> It is called &quot;5th Edition&quot;.<br /> And that is the problem. Because, if anything, Hunter drives the point home that that's not what it *really* is. Vampire hinted at it, Hunter screams it in your face.<br /> <br /> Despite '5th Ed' being, essentially, in parts a complete overhaul and different as new as CoD was, Paradox/WW are - for some reason - refusing to *actually* separate it from OWoD as something NEW. Something that stands on its own legs, separate and confident in itself.<br /> They are using the established branding and nostalgia and fanbase that comes with the old OWoD to market their new thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> This new thing is directly dismantling the future of the old, cutting off any chances for more official 20th books for their 'old' system. Without there being a real need to handle it that way at all.<br /> \u200bAnd that's what's so horribly frustrating for everyone involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-18-2021, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T02:15:27-07:00","id":1464337,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. If they released a new game called Hunter: the Hunternating, I might buy it. I might play it. I might enjoy it. Instead they're basically shitting all over Hunter: the Reckoning and fans of the game, bringing the name back but giving us something completely different. So fuck that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-18-2021, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T18:40:11-07:00","id":1464440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464298#post1464298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Define &amp;quot;good.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> If Paradox sells a lot of copies compared to what Onyx Path usually sells is that good? Well, did we take all the costs involved in wider scale distribution into account? There's a reason why movies aren't financial bombs or successes just based on ticket sales, but ticket sales vs. production costs. Is a movie that costs $50 million to make, distribute, and market, and sells $100 million in tickets better or worse sales than a move that costs $300 million to make, and sells $300 million tickets?<br /> <br /> The first movie made $50 million dollars. The second movie made no money, but sold six times the tickets.<br /> <br /> RPGs are always a shot in the dark for consumers to judge these things, because we get very rough estimates of sales, and no information on production costs, for most big name RPGs (smaller indie companies might be more transparent). <br /> <br /> And, there's also the goals of the company to account for. If Paradox doesn't care about profit, but about the appearance of success, selling a lot of copies even if there is no profit, to help market more profitable aspects of the brand (like future video games), then that also changes the definition of &amp;quot;good,&amp;quot; compared to OPP, which needs profitable RPG sales to survive as a company.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> O...K...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Marketing is more complicated than pleasing one person's opinion on cover color.<br /> <br /> Want to know what the old HtR books did that was important? The popped. Looking at a wall of early 2000s RPGs by just the spines (including other WoD books) it's a see of dark colors, mostly black, some browns, some greens, maybe some reds and purple, and so on. Then there's this vibrant contrasting orange there. Standing out in a crowd is important.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t know that about how sales work in the RPG industry. Thank you. But I still think the color is one reason the original game didn\u2019t do so well (or so I\u2019ve heard).<br /> <br /> I wanted to like Hunter. I really did. I ordered Nocturnal Moonstruck and Spellbound all in one day and I didn\u2019t like any of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T19:23:07-07:00","id":1464450,"title":"","content":"It's not really unique to RPG sales, even RPG sales reporting being as opaque as it is to the consumers isn't unique. Every industry has similar considerations. Though &quot;luxury&quot; and &quot;niche&quot; industries make the best comparisons to RPGs, as RPGs are both of those things (as in, they are luxury in the sense of being something without direct survival necessities or significant investment rather than luxury-as-demonstration-of-wealth, and niche because it's a small market).<br /> <br /> And I'm not asking you to like Hunter. As a HtR fan, I wouldn't pick the &quot;enemy books&quot; as something to sell the game to someone still uncertain about the games from the core book unless &quot;how do you use the other WoD character types in this?&quot; was an expressed primary source of dislike for the game.<br /> <br /> But here's the thing: the original HtR games did well. It wasn't the best, but for a game introduced just a few years before the cWoD was originally ended, it kept going while others game-line were cancelled (CtD had a huge fan base, and WtO was considered one of the best written games of the WoD, but both were cancelled with poor sales as the reason). It got more gaming books than Demon, Mummy, and Orpheus combined. It got three video games... at the time VtM only got two and none of the rest got any.<br /> <br /> Did it have the lasting impact as some of the others? Nope. But there's still fans playing it to this day, and it actually was a well selling game by the standards of the WoD of time despite all the Internet flame wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T04:43:04-07:00","id":1464501,"title":"","content":"I know nothing about sales in any industry, so I found it interesting. And I didn\u2019t really dislike Hunter that much, but it felt too street level. I wanted more grand conspiracies. Maybe like internal plotting among the Messengers tryna manipulate their Hunter pawns. And more details about the enemies (you know not one clan name was mentioned in Nocturnal?) And yeah I know you\u2019re gonna say \u201cHunter wasn\u2019t that kind of game\u201d but it should\u2019ve been. And I think a lot of people, the kind of casual fans who don\u2019t hang out on this forum cause they\u2019re not hardcore into this stuff, wish it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T04:45:36-07:00","id":1464502,"title":"","content":"Ironically I like V5 BECAUSE it is street level, but it gives you a chance to build up to something bigger, like in Fall of London. Or maybe it\u2019s just the color scheme lol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T05:51:53-07:00","id":1464510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464501#post1464501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know nothing about sales in any industry, so I found it interesting. And I didn\u2019t really dislike Hunter that much, but it felt too street level. I wanted more grand conspiracies. Maybe like internal plotting among the Messengers tryna manipulate their Hunter pawns. And more details about the enemies (you know not one clan name was mentioned in Nocturnal?) And yeah I know you\u2019re gonna say \u201cHunter wasn\u2019t that kind of game\u201d but it should\u2019ve been. And I think a lot of people, the kind of casual fans who don\u2019t hang out on this forum cause they\u2019re not hardcore into this stuff, wish it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might have got there if it had reached a second edition. Perhaps not quite this way, but the conspiracies tend to get bigger and more intricate as the metaplot grows. That was very 90s/00s WW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T07:44:58-07:00","id":1464512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464440#post1464440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I didn\u2019t know that about how sales work in the RPG industry. Thank you. But I still think the color is one reason the original game didn\u2019t do so well (or so I\u2019ve heard).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you'd need to check your sources, the book really looked great on the shelves, and stood out quite nicely. That same color never stopped Deadlands selling quite well. I think the biggest issues here is that Hunter is not Vampire, and there's a different sales standard for anything other than Vampire. Werewolf and Mage were big for RPG's and other lines were niche lines.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T11:52:21-07:00","id":1464526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464501#post1464501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I didn\u2019t really dislike Hunter that much, but it felt too street level. I wanted more grand conspiracies. Maybe like internal plotting among the Messengers tryna manipulate their Hunter pawns. And more details about the enemies (you know not one clan name was mentioned in Nocturnal?) And yeah I know you\u2019re gonna say \u201cHunter wasn\u2019t that kind of game\u201d but it should\u2019ve been.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, they funny thing? The creators of HtR don't entirely disagree with you. The original WW company did. Hunter: Utopia was a book that was supposed to start opening up the Imbued to larger scale stuff as they start to organize and work out a society. However, WW told the HtR folks that Utopia wasn't allowed to have the Imbued &quot;win&quot; so a lot of the book is hypothetical story hooks for what you could do, that has a discordantly pessimistic tone because the editorial team basically didn't want anything from Utopia from becoming part of the metaplot.<br /> <br /> Fall from Grace, Utopia, and Holy War (which is not a book I generally recommend because there's just so much damned cringe in it) are the books that start getting into what happens when the Imbued start to tap into the personal, social, and metaphysical power, and start to rise up from &quot;street level&quot; to more serious contenders in the WoD.<br /> <br /> Though, to manage expectations, the Messengers don't plot. They're effectively mindless (it's not that they're unintelligent, but they lack free will) servants of the Ministers, and there's only two Ministers who have a good working relationship. Demon introduce the idea that part of that is because Lucifer is screwing with things and the Ministers are at least united in an attempt to not let him use the Imbued for his purposes. So there's even some stuff on that level going on as the game goes on and interacts with the other games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I think a lot of people, the kind of casual fans who don\u2019t hang out on this forum cause they\u2019re not hardcore into this stuff, wish it was. </div> </div> </div>Based on what though? The game sold really well. It was forums like this where the game looks divisive and ill-suited to lots of tastes. If anything it's the opposite where casual fans, at least back in the day, liked the game as it was, and it was the hardcore fans online that were arguing about if the game was on the right track.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T15:46:23-07:00","id":1464538,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys. This is really helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T17:16:27-07:00","id":1464542,"title":"","content":"HtR had a lot of blowback on the forums when it first released because of a stunt WW pulled. Basically they had a press release and put up stuff on the website saying that WW had been bought out by a third party. They even went so far as to set up a fake website for the third party, which they had set up to be some weird conspiracy-theory group, and there were notes on that page saying that they planned to discontinue or radically change a lot of the WW products. So you had people honestly believing that WW had been bought out and that there wasn't going to be any more VtM or Mage or Werewolf books or whatever. When WW revealed it was a stunt to generate hype for Hunter the Reckoning you had a vocal group of people who were upset, refused to buy HtR and did their best to shit on the game.<br /> <br /> Then when HtR released it was setting the stage to be linked to Kindred of the East/Exalted and there was more blowback in the playerbase with linking the World of Darkness to a &quot;Dragon Ball Z/anime inspired game&quot; so then the writers started moving to link HtR with Demon instead once that gameline came out. Meanwhile with more casual WW fans who weren't big into the internet community Hunter was fairly popular and successful. I think in the online community the game was more divisive because of the original stunt with HtR annoying fans, and then you had a sort of echo-chamber effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T18:21:04-07:00","id":1464545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">World of Darkness to a &quot;Dragon Ball Z/anime inspired game&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to live in this timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T19:41:08-07:00","id":1464556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464545#post1464545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to live in this timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>You kind of already do, since you can take certain mechanics from Demon Hunter X and KotE and apply them more broadly, so that characters can charge up attacks with a turn by turn expenditure of power that they normally couldn't manage. I suppose you could throw WoD: Combat into that mix, too, since it was basically the bones of &quot;WoD vs. Street Fighter&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which, I have to say, is what I was hoping a Capcom-produced Werewolf game for the PS and Saturn was back in the day. Reality, unfortunately, is weighty and pitiless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T20:09:41-07:00","id":1464560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464501#post1464501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know nothing about sales in any industry, so I found it interesting. And I didn\u2019t really dislike Hunter that much, but it felt too street level. I wanted more grand conspiracies. Maybe like internal plotting among the Messengers tryna manipulate their Hunter pawns. And more details about the enemies (you know not one clan name was mentioned in Nocturnal?) And yeah I know you\u2019re gonna say \u201cHunter wasn\u2019t that kind of game\u201d but it should\u2019ve been. And I think a lot of people, the kind of casual fans who don\u2019t hang out on this forum cause they\u2019re not hardcore into this stuff, wish it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the thing you have to understand with the Imbued is that they are literally the newest splat in-universe. While the breed of Mummy in MtR is also new version of it, some of the new Mummies are actually older Mummy types turned into new ones. So they have individuals that have been around for a while and know things. Orpheus, the last line of WoD even predates the Imbued as the Orpheus Group was conducting projection experiments as far bad as 1996. The Imbued for their part started in 1999 after the Sixth Great Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> In fact, in <i>The Walking Dead</i> book a big plot point of that book was the Messengers guiding a vampire (a Wan Kuei if I remember right) and a risen nicknamed Carpenter to the hunter-net, which should not be possible as the site is being protected from the supernatural eavesdropping, for the purpose of providing the Imbued with information about wraiths, the risen and what happened among the Dead following the 6GM.<br /> <br /> So yeah, the ignorance of the Imbued was a plot point and potentially a game point as there were options to alter the existing supernatural creatures to surprised players, especially WoD vets. Obviously that couldn't stay that way forever but it is a nice feature of the line.<br /> <br /> As for larger groups or factions among the Imbued, it's one of the many things that frustrated me that we never got a H20 as after twenty years, groups and factions like that would have formed among the Imbued and opened up a whole new field to play HtR in. Though I would have it has an option if you're playing in a setting where the Imbuing started back in 1999 while still allowing people to play the more street level stuff and more specifically the early years of the Imbued when things were largely unknown for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464542#post1464542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HtR had a lot of blowback on the forums when it first released because of a stunt WW pulled. Basically they had a press release and put up stuff on the website saying that WW had been bought out by a third party. They even went so far as to set up a fake website for the third party, which they had set up to be some weird conspiracy-theory group, and there were notes on that page saying that they planned to discontinue or radically change a lot of the WW products. So you had people honestly believing that WW had been bought out and that there wasn't going to be any more VtM or Mage or Werewolf books or whatever. When WW revealed it was a stunt to generate hype for Hunter the Reckoning you had a vocal group of people who were upset, refused to buy HtR and did their best to shit on the game.<br /> <br /> Then when HtR released it was setting the stage to be linked to Kindred of the East/Exalted and there was more blowback in the playerbase with linking the World of Darkness to a &quot;Dragon Ball Z/anime inspired game&quot; so then the writers started moving to link HtR with Demon instead once that gameline came out. Meanwhile with more casual WW fans who weren't big into the internet community Hunter was fairly popular and successful. I think in the online community the game was more divisive because of the original stunt with HtR annoying fans, and then you had a sort of echo-chamber effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was a dumb stunt on their part. If they had done that in more recent years... well they would have played into ARGs and the like and could have been a really great way to build excitement for the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T22:43:02-07:00","id":1464563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1463962#post1463962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not a fan of the announcement.<br /> I enjoyed the Imbued and the higher ups are pushing too hard for Chronicles of Darkness 2.0 instead of making World of Darkness 5.0<br /> But, hey, if people out there enjoy it and want to play this version? Then I wish them all the best and to have many long years of playing.<br /> My table? I am not even suggesting the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't it be Chronicles of Darkness 3.0?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T11:12:45-07:00","id":1464600,"title":"","content":"Slot me in with the crowd wondering who the hell this is supposed to be for. I can't see how this works for World fans twice over, and once over for CHronicles fans and new/potential fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T11:52:15-07:00","id":1464610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464600#post1464600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slot me in with the crowd wondering who the hell this is supposed to be for. I can't see how this works for World fans twice over, and once over for CHronicles fans and new/potential fans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same as V5, I suspect - primarily new fans rather than returning ones. Hunter: The Reckoning has a recognizable branding and the hunter side of the World of Darkness is of interest. New fans aren't going to care it's a reboot rather than a remake. Old fans are going to be split between people who liked HtR and are unhappy it's not returning the way they wanted, didn't like HtR and thought it should be this way to begin with back in the day, and those who - like me - liked HtR, would have loved an H20, but are entirely happy to look at H5 on its own merits when we get our hands on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T12:02:40-07:00","id":1464612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464610#post1464610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Same as V5, I suspect - primarily new fans rather than returning ones. Hunter: The Reckoning has a recognizable branding and the hunter side of the World of Darkness is of interest. New fans aren't going to care it's a reboot rather than a remake. Old fans are going to be split between people who liked HtR and are unhappy it's not returning the way they wanted, didn't like HtR and thought it should be this way to begin with back in the day, and those who - like me - liked HtR, would have loved an H20, but are entirely happy to look at H5 on its own merits when we get our hands on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem on new players is that, even with Paradox itself being fairly big and the World of Darkness brand still being a big thing in memory, I can't imagine any avenue for a new player to come into interest of Hunter the Reckoning without running through the bramble of opinions of the older guard.<br /> <br /> And where that was a mixed bag for Vampire and upcoming Werewolf, this sort of at-odds with the fanbase approach makes that less of a bramble and more of Jigsaw trap, and the avenue of new players who might be appealed to without running into that seems so vanishingly small as to be suicidal marketing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T12:12:49-07:00","id":1464614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464612#post1464612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem on new players is that, even with Paradox itself being fairly big and the World of Darkness brand still being a big thing in memory, I can't imagine any avenue for a new player to come into interest of Hunter the Reckoning without running through the bramble of opinions of the older guard.<br /> <br /> And where that was a mixed bag for Vampire and upcoming Werewolf, this sort of at-odds with the fanbase approach makes that less of a bramble and more of Jigsaw trap, and the avenue of new players who might be appealed to without running into that seems so vanishingly small as to be suicidal marketing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect the number of people who will encounter that stuff is fairly low, actually - not that many people browse forums. They'll see the cover of the book in a store and go &quot;Oh neat, vampire hunters in the World of Darkness!&quot; or their Amazon page will propagate a recommendation, or some streamed actual play they watch will pick up the game, etc. And anyone with even basic internet fandom literacy will know that every new edition attracts some level of old guard whining, so of the people who do run into it, how many will care? <br /> <br /> I mean, I was an HtR fan and I honestly don't care about getting into another edition war over a title. It just doesn't matter that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T12:29:55-07:00","id":1464615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464614#post1464614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect the number of people who will encounter that stuff is fairly low, actually - not that many people browse forums. They'll see the cover of the book in a store and go &quot;Oh neat, vampire hunters in the World of Darkness!&quot; or their Amazon page will propagate a recommendation, or some streamed actual play they watch will pick up the game, etc. And anyone with even basic internet fandom literacy will know that every new edition attracts some level of old guard whining, so of the people who do run into it, how many will care?<br /> <br /> I mean, I was an HtR fan and I honestly don't care about getting into another edition war over a title. It just doesn't matter that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can buy a &quot;Oh, Amazon recommendation&quot; or the like, but I don't see anything else being viable. Even disregarding the viability of brick and mortar, specialty game shops are gonna run into the same issue as streaming play sessions-being those are very dependent on the personalities behind the sales pitch (which is inclined to be the old guard, so here's the same Jigsaw trap) where as more mainstream book stores like Barnes and Noble aren't gonna push it particularly well if they push for that audience at all. Even the most neutral news outlet for this sort of stuff is almost bound to have a link from that neutral article to a think piece on the really bizarre decision (nevermind any comments on either of those). What's left over is a trickle.<br /> <br /> I don't particularly have any skin or gain in this chain of events, mind you-but even as someone whose just kind of written off Paradox Wolf's run with World of Darkness and is gonna wait until it's done, this decision is baffling enough it made me want to hear some kind of pretense for the decision, because it's just <i>that far out there</i> as a decision for a franchise that lives (and sometimes kills itself) on brand legacy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I mean, it's baffling enough that even though I know I'm kind of rehashing points HEavy Arms made so much better than I could, I <i>still</i> have to ask those questions again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-20-2021, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T13:45:26-07:00","id":1464634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">People being directed towards World of Darkness when someone asked about Hunter the Vigil in hololive is beginning to make a lot more sense now...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what's this all about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T13:45:43-07:00","id":1464635,"title":"","content":"I don't mind being repetitive. Esp with company.<br /> <br /> I think there's also a lot of underselling of new RPG fans Internet savvy going on. When Justin says, in a Twitch video promoting things, that the Imbued aren't going to be in H5... how many new fans aren't going to just Google what that means? Like go Google &quot;Hunter the Reckoning Imbued.&quot; I'm sure algorithms mean different results, but I get the White Wolf fan wiki, Wikipedia, Reddit, RPG.net, here, TVTropes, and other WoD fan sites. It's not exactly arduous to sate that curiosity.<br /> <br /> I know Justin's Twitter thread on the announcement had people repeating complaints that have been voiced here, and I doubt that's the only place in social media where that's happening (though it's far enough out that it might not matter when H5 is actually released).<br /> <br /> I just don't know young Millenials or Zoomers that by hobby products on brand recognition alone. It's too easy to search for this stuff to find out what it's about, while at the same time most RPGs are small enough that places like this forum actually come up early in searches because there aren't that many places with new content for Search engines to recommend over ten year old fan sites.<br /> <br /> Will they care? No idea. But the idea that they're not going to know just baffles me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T14:33:13-07:00","id":1464642,"title":"","content":"Heck, I'm 35yo and the first thing I do with any new RPG is to search for some opinions. Of course, buying up good reviews is easy, but it also costs and isn't infallible at all.<br /> <br /> But during my absence (my computer broke during the weekend and I only got the piece I needed today) this thread also went through some strange considerations.<br /> <br /> 5th ed is using many bits of style and mechanics from CoD. But it isn't either CoD 3.0 or a mashup in any capacity. Bringing in some influence would be expected, but many changes are neither here or there, but completely new developments. Overall it is indeed a new WoD edition, as different as it may be. And again, this isn't exactly H:tV as this was already Hunters Hunted take.<br /> <br /> Demon wasn't a game meant to wrap up the WoD's metaplot. It is just another game line. And a good one at that, despite not being for everyone's tastes as all the others weren't either. It wasn't severely Abrahamic, either, it was barely more Christian-like than Vampire. It wasn't retconning anything either, just interpreting stuff through its own lenses as every line also did.<br /> <br /> Changeling directly states that every supernatural that's not a Mage is a Prodigal and the world started in the Dreaming, Mage attributes most or all of what exists to originating from the Consensus at some point, except if you get the individual and equally disparate origins relayed by each individual Paradigm. Werewolf had Fera existing for millions of years despite never even hinting at how it worked before human forms, but everything else is just a spirit or spirit-possessed.<br /> <br /> It isn't about knowing everything about everyone, about it sure is fun to <i>pretend</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T16:07:16-07:00","id":1464652,"title":"","content":"On the &quot;Why not Hunters Hunted?&quot; or the more extreme &quot;They're trying to make Reckoning Hunter: the Vigil!&quot; take, I do have a headscratch on that I haven't seen addressed.<br /> <br /> Going with the craziest assessment that they want to make Vigil, but World this time (which I don't buy), and that for whatever reason they don't think the brand name of Hunters Hunted would draw eyes (I'm more open to this one but I still don't buy it)....Okay, they <i>do realize</i> it's not an either/or scenario right? One of the things proven with the Chronicles franchise is that that Noun: the Gerund branding is recognizable and connective while still allowing a permission for different variations of the Noun-based conceit....and it's not a hard skip over to playing around with that in a particular continuity of material.<br /> <br /> Again, accepting the most insane and batshit of arguments that I'm not actively proposing is <i>actually</i> the case...Okay, so you have your Hunter: the Reckoning for the Imbued, your angelic backed hunter with lightsaber toothbrushes*, but you could also have your, I dunno, Hunter: The Collapse or whatever that basically covers what Hunters Hunted did but with a Sexy New Title, or hell, even do a third option that might lean more into the Hunter-Slasher Connection in interesting ways, whatever. I can't imagine it being hard to do something akin to &quot;With Hunter: the Collapse, we're taking the foundation laid out by Hunters Hunted and giving it the respect it deserves by elevating it to a full on gameline, complete with [insert cool things here, including influences from Vigil or whatever].&quot; If you assume that they want to gain acclaim with something in the Hunters Hunted/Vigil, doing something like that lets you have your cake and eat it too, because they you get that, with possibly some added cred for making a &quot;new gameline&quot; or at least elevating something, and you still have room to do your angel-backed actors of zealotry and judgment.<br /> <br /> Or hell, you can do &quot;Hunter: the Reckoning, featuring the Imbued! And Other Types of Hunters!&quot; and just smush Reckoning and Hunters Hunted (and Vigil) together, and then you wouldn't have people wondering why the hell Reckoning <i>doesn't</i> have the gameline's main protagonist/player character in it. <br /> <br /> As I said, I kind of think it's an extreme read and don't necessarily buy it, but again....the decision to rely on the power of a brand name without relying on the content that backed that name feels even weirder to me and I <i>can't</i> think of a good reason to do that. If I didn't want to make the Imbued, I probably would just make a new(/&quot;new&quot;) Hunter and avoid the brand confusion entirely.<br /> <br /> Like, just. No matter how I look at the decision, I kind of can't avoid coming to the conclusion that almost any other decision would have been easier and have less reprecussion.<br /> <br /> *Yes, I am being facetitious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T16:08:42-07:00","id":1464653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was shown a screenshot from someone I trust of a person in a vtuber's chat asking about the game they were running(Hunter the Vigil, though keep in mind it was using some World of Darkness elements) and someone who was apparently in some capacity part of the relevant WoD online presence directed them towards 5e World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> On the discussion of who is the edition for. I really don't know how it will play out for new fans. The places I primarily visit are all concentrations of these fandoms and the only concentrated 5e space I've been in unilaterally just says variants of &quot;These old fans with criticisms of 5e are just toxic.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Calli crossed the streams for her hololive en campaign. I was confused about the combination of material at first, but it seems to be a natural part of WW having made translation guides.<br /> <br /> Though, really, the decision to use sliding difficulty with CoD rules confused me more. It apparently got to be a bit too much, though, since she went back to the fixed tn of 8 after about the second or third tutorial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T17:06:43-07:00","id":1464663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464653#post1464653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calli crossed the streams for her hololive en campaign. I was confused about the combination of material at first, but it seems to be a natural part of WW having made translation guides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give me a short summary of what this actually is? I saw it referenced and linked on reddit and around here, but I got no idea what it is other than anime vtubers doing homebrew Hunter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcane Arts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the &quot;Why not Hunters Hunted?&quot; or the more extreme &quot;They're trying to make Reckoning Hunter: the Vigil!&quot; take, I do have a headscratch on that I haven't seen addressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the key here is that they realised that the framework Vigil is based on is brilliant for any type of hunter game. Heck, I pillage that thing for NBA (and vice versa). They're applying the same approach - broad groups of hunters, varied types of hunters, organizations and assets to help the hunters. It's an excellent way to integrate the monster hunters of Carpenter's Vampire Slayers or the crew from Lost Boys. Instead of the tricks they use in Vigil, they can cover the broad weird powers we've had in multiple books before - DHX's Arsenal, True Faith, Psychic power and so on. It's a great concept that begs to be used in the classic WoD. And I get that logic. I even get why they are using X: The Y - Reckoning is a recognizable line, you can sell the old supplements on DTRPG for some extra money AND there were a couple successful console games.<br /> <br /> What I don't get is deciding to ignore the Imbued, as just ignoring them will cause drama. You'll piss off the fans of HtR, you'll piss off the WoD completionist, and you'll confuse the hell out of the new people once they start delving into the lore, all assuming it's perfectly connected and leads into a bigger whole.<br /> <br /> I could see this working if they have a new Hunter videogame in preparation. They may have called it Reckoning, but the elements it has are downplayed. That way you get people hooked on the new vision and there is a more tangible connection to the new than the old. I mean how can musty old books beat a well marketed computer game?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T18:57:53-07:00","id":1464674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464663#post1464663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> What I don't get is deciding to ignore the Imbued, as just ignoring them will cause drama. You'll piss off the fans of HtR, you'll piss off the WoD completionist, and you'll confuse the hell out of the new people once they start delving into the lore, all assuming it's perfectly connected and leads into a bigger whole.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is the heart of the rest of the post beyond the opening-or rather, more specifically &quot;Why use the Reckoning brand if you're not going to use the Reckoning player character?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'll briefly reiterate &quot;I don't think using a new brand name for a non-Reckoning style of player characteris going to be most jarring thing you can do.&quot;-but honestly, a late addition to that post strikes me as even more relevant, which is &quot;Imbued+other styles of Hunters=Paradox Wolf Reckoning&quot;<br /> <br /> As a point of comparison, over in Chronicles Land, Mummy the Curse's Second Edition made the pitch of not only containing an updated take on the Arisen, but also the inclusion and update of the characters from popular supplement Immortals, since Mummy naturally has a lot of adjacency to that and it neatly deepens Curse's cast. While the actual implementation can be argued about (I don't think anyone walked away going &quot;FUCK YEAH!&quot; from the Immortals in Curse 2nd), the fact that this was one of the most anticipated aspects of Curse Second was an indicator of successful possibilities for adjacent ideas, which would include mushing Reckoning, Hunters Hunted, and Vigil-inspired things together.<br /> <br /> But even if not that, again, Reckoning for angel backed agents, [probably a cool word that has end of the world connotations here] for everything else if for any reason they don't want to use Hunters Hunted. We've gone this long with two Hunter: the [Gerund] style games with relatively little muss, a third is not exactly a deal breaker and leaves open all the other avenues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T21:00:45-07:00","id":1464686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464663#post1464663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't get is deciding to ignore the Imbued.</div> </div> </div> </div>It just occurred to me that they may not <u>ignore</u> the Imbued.<br /> <br /> They may eliminate them in lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T22:13:23-07:00","id":1464692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464612#post1464612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem on new players is that, even with Paradox itself being fairly big and the World of Darkness brand still being a big thing in memory, I can't imagine any avenue for a new player to come into interest of Hunter the Reckoning without running through the bramble of opinions of the older guard.<br /> <br /> And where that was a mixed bag for Vampire and upcoming Werewolf, this sort of at-odds with the fanbase approach makes that less of a bramble and more of Jigsaw trap, and the avenue of new players who might be appealed to without running into that seems so vanishingly small as to be suicidal marketing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but plenty of new people neither know nor care about the opinions of old guard fans (probably more towards the not care side but still).<br /> <br /> More like a sense of indifference<br /> <br /> I\u2019m somewhere in the middle so I straddle the boundary. I can see both sides. I\u2019m hoping H5 will be really good and I\u2019m defo gonna buy it when it comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 10-21-2021, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T22:23:56-07:00","id":1464694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464652#post1464652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the &quot;Why not Hunters Hunted?&quot; or the more extreme &quot;They're trying to make Reckoning Hunter: the Vigil!&quot; take, I do have a headscratch on that I haven't seen addressed.<br /> <br /> Going with the craziest assessment that they want to make Vigil, but World this time (which I don't buy), and that for whatever reason they don't think the brand name of Hunters Hunted would draw eyes (I'm more open to this one but I still don't buy it)....Okay, they <i>do realize</i> it's not an either/or scenario right? One of the things proven with the Chronicles franchise is that that Noun: the Gerund branding is recognizable and connective while still allowing a permission for different variations of the Noun-based conceit....and it's not a hard skip over to playing around with that in a particular continuity of material.<br /> <br /> Again, accepting the most insane and batshit of arguments that I'm not actively proposing is <i>actually</i> the case...Okay, so you have your Hunter: the Reckoning for the Imbued, your angelic backed hunter with lightsaber toothbrushes*, but you could also have your, I dunno, Hunter: The Collapse or whatever that basically covers what Hunters Hunted did but with a Sexy New Title, or hell, even do a third option that might lean more into the Hunter-Slasher Connection in interesting ways, whatever. I can't imagine it being hard to do something akin to &quot;With Hunter: the Collapse, we're taking the foundation laid out by Hunters Hunted and giving it the respect it deserves by elevating it to a full on gameline, complete with [insert cool things here, including influences from Vigil or whatever].&quot; If you assume that they want to gain acclaim with something in the Hunters Hunted/Vigil, doing something like that lets you have your cake and eat it too, because they you get that, with possibly some added cred for making a &quot;new gameline&quot; or at least elevating something, and you still have room to do your angel-backed actors of zealotry and judgment.<br /> <br /> Or hell, you can do &quot;Hunter: the Reckoning, featuring the Imbued! And Other Types of Hunters!&quot; and just smush Reckoning and Hunters Hunted (and Vigil) together, and then you wouldn't have people wondering why the hell Reckoning <i>doesn't</i> have the gameline's main protagonist/player character in it. <br /> <br /> As I said, I kind of think it's an extreme read and don't necessarily buy it, but again....the decision to rely on the power of a brand name without relying on the content that backed that name feels even weirder to me and I <i>can't</i> think of a good reason to do that. If I didn't want to make the Imbued, I probably would just make a new(/&quot;new&quot;) Hunter and avoid the brand confusion entirely.<br /> <br /> Like, just. No matter how I look at the decision, I kind of can't avoid coming to the conclusion that almost any other decision would have been easier and have less reprecussion.<br /> <br /> *Yes, I am being facetitious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, they have people with Marketing degrees and maybe even MBAs who are probably trained in the latest marketing techniques creating these campaigns. I wouldn\u2019t wanna second guess their judgment until poor sales actually proves them wrong.<br /> <br /> I think people should do what they\u2019re specialized in. You don\u2019t ask a lawyer how to fix your car and you don\u2019t ask a mechanic for legal advice. There\u2019s probably something these marketing people know that we\u2019re just not seeing cause we don\u2019t have their academic background or professional experience.<br /> <br /> Yes, technically this is the Appeal to Authority fallacy, but although it\u2019s formally a fallacy, informally it makes a lot of sense. Authorities in their field do have a better chance of being right than the average person on the street.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I\u2019m rambling. I should get to bed. Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 10-21-2021, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T22:35:53-07:00","id":1464696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464663#post1464663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you give me a short summary of what this actually is? I saw it referenced and linked on reddit and around here, but I got no idea what it is other than anime vtubers doing homebrew Hunter?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit behind on following it (there's a prelude for each player's character and several unified group games), but it's essentially just as a I said - vtuber Calliope Mori roped in some of her fellow Hololive EN members to play Vigil with a lot of WoD lore and story elements mixed in. She uses the CoD system more or less entirely by this point, I believe, but you get things like Magadon making an appearance, along with unaccountable one-off weirdness that Vigil likes to use to keep characters on their toes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T23:25:07-07:00","id":1464702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464694#post1464694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, they have people with Marketing degrees and maybe even MBAs who are probably trained in the latest marketing techniques creating these campaigns. I wouldn\u2019t wanna second guess their judgment until poor sales actually proves them wrong.<br /> <br /> I think people should do what they\u2019re specialized in. You don\u2019t ask a lawyer how to fix your car and you don\u2019t ask a mechanic for legal advice. There\u2019s probably something these marketing people know that we\u2019re just not seeing cause we don\u2019t have their academic background or professional experience.<br /> <br /> Yes, technically this is the Appeal to Authority fallacy, but although it\u2019s formally a fallacy, informally it makes a lot of sense. Authorities in their field do have a better chance of being right than the average person on the street.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I\u2019m rambling. I should get to bed. Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly it was a minor for Bachelors, so definitely not a match for an MBA in Marketing, but I'm not exactly the average person on the street either. I have my reasons for being boggled by this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T04:27:56-07:00","id":1464720,"title":"","content":"Degrees are indicators, but it's good to temper expectations. Having an MBA in marketing doesn't mean an individual knows a specific market/product. Someone with 10 years of experience selling video games doesn't instantly know how to sell RPG books. Specialists exist within every field for a reason. The basic skill set a degree indicates a professional has is important, but it doesn't mean they're ready to jump into a new product line right away, or are actually going to know the market for the product better than someone without said degree but a lot of knowledge and experience from first hand experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T04:45:50-07:00","id":1464721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464702#post1464702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly it was a minor for Bachelors, so definitely not a match for an MBA in Marketing, but I'm not exactly the average person on the street either. I have my reasons for being boggled by this.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case I definitely defer to your superior knowledge and experience. Maybe it was a terrible decision on their part. But I\u2019m still (probably) gonna buy it and see how it is. If it\u2019s terrible I won\u2019t buy any of the supplements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T04:51:40-07:00","id":1464723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464720#post1464720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Degrees are indicators, but it's good to temper expectations. Having an MBA in marketing doesn't mean an individual knows a specific market/product. Someone with 10 years of experience selling video games doesn't instantly know how to sell RPG books. Specialists exist within every field for a reason. The basic skill set a degree indicates a professional has is important, but it doesn't mean they're ready to jump into a new product line right away, or are actually going to know the market for the product better than someone without said degree but a lot of knowledge and experience from first hand experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a very good point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T08:29:49-07:00","id":1464740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464686#post1464686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just occurred to me that they may not <u>ignore</u> the Imbued.<br /> <br /> They may eliminate them in lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps they could get &quot;sent to middle east&quot;, Messengers giving them the directions. Ofc some would stay, but we're not going to give rules to play with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T09:10:20-07:00","id":1464750,"title":"","content":"I think the simple answer to why they are doing Hunters like this, rather than the imbued, is that it is directly expanding the world they have already created. I haven't been following V5 that much but from what i've seen the role of mortal hunters in various forms is a significant element, especially with the whole second inquisition thing. Based on that I think it makes far more sense to expand on that idea and focus on mortal hunters than to reboot the imbued hunters that don;t really have a natural place in the world they have built so far. But will agree that given that, and especially knowing how old school players tend to get when you mess with their favorite IP, I wonder whether it would have been better to chose a new title without connection to the OWoD imbued hunters (Hunter: The Avenging, Hunter: the Defending or something like that but much better!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:21:08-07:00","id":1464768,"title":"","content":"To rehash some stuff though:<br /> <br /> 1) The Second Inquisition isn't the subject of H5. Justin said that the large organizations of hunters (aka the types that make up the SI) are seen as antagonists to the characters in H5.<br /> <br /> 2) They're not going to be normal mortals that happen to fight monsters. They're going to have access to powers on some level.<br /> <br /> 3) WoD5 is not supposed to be a different setting, just the future of the setting 15 years later as the new team has decided things have happened. There isn't some &quot;natural&quot; state that the Imbued do or do not fit into. They were part of the setting, and if the WoD5 writers decide that the new setting makes them a bad fit... that was a conscious decision for them to do. Given how vampire focused the WoD5 has been so far, I haven't really seen anything that makes the Imbued inherently &quot;wrong&quot; for things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T11:52:31-07:00","id":1464783,"title":"","content":"Seconding all 3 Heavy Arms said, but also:<br /> <br /> 1.) Second Inquisition is its own book, standalone from HTR5 and a Vampire Supplement<br /> 2.) At least Psychic Powers and True Faith are confirmed as well as things like Arsenal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T15:21:23-07:00","id":1464798,"title":"","content":"I think we have a blueprint for Hunter 2nd edition in <b><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_-_Out_for_Blood\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Masquerade \u2014 Out for Blood</a>. </b>You play a group of mortals who learns about the existence of vampires in a small town and needs to decide how to deal with them. You can meet a seasoned hunter AND the second inquisition (right before the end of the game). The SI tries to use you as bait for vampires while the hunter helps you fight the vampires but then wants you to help with the &quot;war&quot; (which is as desperate as it gets). I think it shows nicely the differences in tone and scope between the various hunter groups. The SI is &quot;the Man&quot; and is not the friend of unalligned hunters, at best it uses them to lure supernaturals in the open. At worst it considers the a liability and deals with them accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T16:00:27-07:00","id":1464805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464740#post1464740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps they could get &quot;sent to middle east&quot;, Messengers giving them the directions. Ofc some would stay, but we're not going to give rules to play with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talking about Imbued in the same breath as the middle east gives me the shakes. Holy War... ugh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T16:42:03-07:00","id":1464808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464805#post1464805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Talking about Imbued in the same breath as the middle east gives me the shakes. Holy War... ugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it wasn't my intention to give any ideas...nor I think they will really go there <i>again</i>.<br /> <br /> But, it's too late for that: The Sabbat too are related to religious iconography, fanatiscism, blood feuds...It's WAS as crass as it gets <i>already</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T18:45:06-07:00","id":1464811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps they could get &quot;sent to middle east&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, it seems that anything these new 5th edition writers don't like, they just shrug them off-screen to the Middle-East. That's exactly what they did to get rid of elders and the Sabbat from VtM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T19:00:56-07:00","id":1464814,"title":"","content":"Honestly at this point, 'being sent to the Middle East' might as well be 5E's 'Put on a Bus'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T02:05:47-07:00","id":1464839,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26996_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26996\" data-vbnamecard=\"26996\">Amethyst</a>, new players may not care about old players' opinions, but they're likely to use it as a starting point to decide before buying, and it will point them out to old material. At this point they'll be forming their own opinions based on the material and Paradox decisions.<br /> <br /> You have already decided that you'll buy the book, good for you. Most of us are cynical and skeptical, but we'll also wait and see, we're just guessing things. But most new players won't start from either assumption and will study the matter before deciding.<br /> <br /> Either way you're not a new player, you're a V5 fan already, that informs a lot of your decision. V5 fans, like you and CTPhipps, already have a good experience with Paradox, so it's not a decision from scratch.<br /> <br /> On the matter of getting rid of the Imbued, I don't think it'll be sending then wherever may be, but really ending the whole Imbuing, with any surviving Imbued either becoming NPCs or losing their powers and joining the other hunters, maybe forming new organizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T03:47:27-07:00","id":1464850,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> that makes sense. Thanks.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not really a serious V5 fan though. I haven\u2019t played the game yet. Just read some of the books and liked the lore. Enough that I\u2019m willing to buy the H5 book and see how it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T03:55:25-07:00","id":1464854,"title":"","content":"I actually prefer V20 it\u2019s what I started out playing but they\u2019re not making any new official V20 books and the company\u2019s transitioning over to V5 and my group is too so it\u2019s like the march of progress you know? Anyway I don\u2019t hate V5 and I really like Fall of London so I\u2019m reasonably happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T08:28:36-07:00","id":1464875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464839#post1464839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;26996&quot;] new players may not care about old players' opinions, but they're likely to use it as a starting point to decide before buying, and it will point them out to old material. At this point they'll be forming their own opinions based on the material and Paradox decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little puzzled by this statement mostly because I think the first part is right i.e. that new players may not care about old player's opinions, and so I don't get why you then say that those same new players are likely to use the the views of the players they don't care about as a starting point. As an old WoD player (mostly Mage and Werewolf and a smidgen of Hunter) I think most old players seem to overestimate the extent to which we are the major market these days for new games. We definitely are the major market for the 20th anniversary line which is entirely geared to a beautifully nostalgic look at these games and these settings. But the new stuff is aimed at new players who are unlikely to be concerned with the long and storied history of the game. My daughter just started playing DnD with school friends and it had absolutely nothing to do with her dear old dad's nostalgic recollections of my campaigns in the 80's and 90's! She's interested in what she's playing with her friends here and now and has no interest whatsoever in what i thought about the DnD edition wars! I think the same is true of WoD and many other games as well as other fandoms (e.g. classic vs new Dr Who)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T09:18:52-07:00","id":1464879,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12792_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12792\" data-vbnamecard=\"12792\">scifirabbi</a>. I like V20 because it\u2019s the game I started playing with, not because I feel any nostalgia for the Nineties. At the same time, I\u2019m also willing and maybe even excited to transition to V5 (we\u2019re finally gonna play over the holiday break).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 10-22-2021, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T10:22:14-07:00","id":1464884,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12792_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12792\" data-vbnamecard=\"12792\">scifirabbi</a>, what I meant is that they'll use whatever we write about to try to understand the material. They don't care about our opinions, but they will seek information.<br /> <br /> When a new player look for info on Hunter and see this thread, it will tell them two important things: that the Imbued existed and that they were removed from the game.<br /> <br /> From this, our opinions on the change will matter little, but the change itself becomes known, and those prospective players may investigate further.<br /> <br /> They'll reach their own conclusions, but our opinions contain information. Now, how will they react to this? Some people don't care that much, but others may get angry at the idea that the game isn't about what the title says. I know people like that.<br /> <br /> Not saying that our opinions are decisive, just that they play a role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T11:18:16-07:00","id":1464891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464884#post1464884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> what I meant is that they'll use whatever we write about to try to understand the material. They don't care about our opinions, but they will seek information.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I will say that while I am happy to see what they do and personally not too bothered that they will not be continuing with the Imbued, I do think its a pity that there is no H20 for the imbued. For me that's what the purpose is of the 20th Anniversary line, to provide a gaming experience based on the full history of those games for those of us who have been playing them for over 20 years. So while I am happy to see what H5 will do and feel that it doesn't need to be a continuation of the old H:tR, it is unfortunate that the fans of the Imbued hunters don't get to have a full 20th anniversary treatment of that game. But that's life I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T13:39:25-07:00","id":1464905,"title":"","content":"Also, I\u2019m really excited to see how hunters in H5 interact with the Second Inquisition. I feel like they\u2019re gonna set up a divide kinda like in V5, with the new hunters being the Anarchs and the SI being the Camarilla. What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T14:25:11-07:00","id":1464912,"title":"","content":"That certainly seems to be the dynamic they're hinting at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T15:32:35-07:00","id":1464919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464814#post1464814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly at this point, 'being sent to the Middle East' might as well be 5E's 'Put on a Bus'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until they have to make a book on anywhere in the ME, in which case they will say that everyone went back home... (^VVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T22:32:23-07:00","id":1464970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464783#post1464783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seconding all 3 Heavy Arms said, but also:<br /> <br /> 2.) At least Psychic Powers and True Faith are confirmed as well as things like Arsenal</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't expecting crossover with DC but I guess an addict is good fit for WoD and arrows are good for staking vampirs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T04:01:36-07:00","id":1464994,"title":"","content":"I think older players do play a role in bringing newbies into the hobby. I've brought over a dozen people into RPGs over the years, all of them with VTM.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, though, they all just play D&amp;D if I'm not there, as it's the only game their casual gamer friends recognise and care about. It takes more experienced gamers to get them to try other things.<br /> <br /> So while things like Stranger Things and Community have given RPGs a coolness factor that draws in people without any prior knowledge, they're not going too deep into the hobby without recommendations from more experienced gamers.<br /> <br /> I think it's also like fiction. Books require more investment of time and effort than films, so people tend to be more cautious in buying a book than they are in buying a film. They look around and ask for second opinions. That's where the experienced players come in.<br /> <br /> It's hard to know, though, because the industry isn't very transparent so there's not a lot of data to base these things on. We also don't know if the net of new players minus old players is an increase or a decrease, or whether it even makes more profit rather than acting as an expensive PR strategy for the video and mobile games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T08:43:18-07:00","id":1465014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464905#post1464905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I\u2019m really excited to see how hunters in H5 interact with the Second Inquisition. I feel like they\u2019re gonna set up a divide kinda like in V5, with the new hunters being the Anarchs and the SI being the Camarilla. What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>It will be a bit less antagonistic at first. The SI wants to use unaffilated hunters and cares very little for their survival. In their eyes they are expendable and lack the training, self discipline and upbringing to make full fledged agents (some factions of the SI might have different views on this though, I guess the Society of Leopold might want to convert hunters for example, but they wouldn't be true operatives) but they have value as they help lure the monsters in the open. The moment the hunters realize they are being used at bait their relationship with the SI could (should) change drammatically.<br /> Also, in &quot;Out for Blood&quot; you can meet an experienced hunter... she's been in prison for killing ghouls and is pretty fanatical in her views (only the hunt matters...), these are other themes for hunter games. Can you be a &quot;part time hunter&quot;? How does the law deal with you killing vampires when vampires officially do not exist (and can use the law against you...)? Are you content with defending your little corner of the world or do you want to killa ll monsters? What are you willing to do, whant compromises will you take in order to suceed? Are all &quot;monsters&quot; monsters or some of them may deserve mercy? And so on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T08:26:27-07:00","id":1465406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/first-look-at-the-new-edition-of-hunter-the-reckoning\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/first-look-at-the-new-edition-of-hunter-the-reckoning\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/first-look-at-the-new-edition-of-hunter-the-reckoning\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/first-look-at-the-new-edition-of-hunter-the-reckoning </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is the mentioned preview of Ht:R V","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T12:08:15-07:00","id":1465429,"title":"","content":"I'm really interested in the Drive, Desperation and Creed mechanics, it really seems to use the whole hope and its antithesis as part of the game, like Hunger was made material in V5. It reminds me of the Stress mechanics of Alien RPG, which is awesome.<br /> <br /> I'm a tad bit sad that Hunter will be practically cells and have no bigger organization, but I didn't like that whole shtick of Recoking with the Hunter's blog and &quot;HunterNet&quot; site either. But it doesn't seem like something too hard to employ by houserule or simple statement. <br /> Looks like it will be something between Hunters Hunted and the Reckoning, but it won't be as similar to Hunter the Vigil as I thought. But it might be that they are making a very basic setting to really permit it to be taken anywhere from there, and I agree with the approach. Better to have a solid base that covers the low-level side of things, then having a game that tries to go through all levels and scales. I'll be on the lookout for more on this game, but it looks promising. <br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah, we were all taken by surprise by it. Almost out of the blue. XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T15:34:56-07:00","id":1465444,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, my personal play style with HtR was to ignore the Imbued and play up Bystanders from the Player's Guide; so this abandonment of the Imbued in the new edition, while quite surprising, is also not a problem for me. <br /> <br /> I'm curious if the new edition's Drives and Creeds well align with the first edition's Virtues and Creeds? I hope so; I actually enjoyed that part of the original game. But I won't mind the Edges being reworked as something a bit more Endowment-like. <br /> <br /> I've generally been underwhelmed by V5; but then, Vampire has never been a gameline that particularly interested me. H5, on the other hand, may well be something I end up picking up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T21:47:46-07:00","id":1465476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\">