r","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T21:21:05-07:00","id":1466605,"title":"","content":"Semi-serious thought experienced today regarding axing of the Imbued: Does this mean that the Solar Exalted are going away too? (^VVVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T23:51:51-08:00","id":1467158,"title":"","content":"Golden Race in Dead Magic may refer to western ancestor imbued/Solar/Wan Xian, etc. <br /> <br /> To be honest global wan gui maybe more reasonable if you consider HtR/DtF/Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T10:12:38-08:00","id":1467266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1467158#post1467158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Golden Race in Dead Magic may refer to western ancestor imbued/Solar/Wan Xian, etc.<br /> <br /> To be honest global wan gui maybe more reasonable if you consider HtR/DtF/Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't seem like that's what we're getting, though, since the Hungry Dead were axed completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T03:06:58-08:00","id":1473519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karthak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464023#post1464023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First they do some weird shit with Vampire, then they shoot Gaia in the head, and now they've removed the Reckoning part from Hunters: The Reckoning (more like Hunters: The Gelded now)? What in the name of the Dark Father are the writers smoking!?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good games weed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T04:17:01-08:00","id":1473521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1464839#post1464839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the matter of getting rid of the Imbued, I don't think it'll be sending then wherever may be, but really ending the whole Imbuing, with any surviving Imbued either becoming NPCs or losing their powers and joining the other hunters, maybe forming new organizations.</div> </div> </div> </div>And from what I've read about it, all of the necessary game systems to reintroduce the Imbued are already there: what 1e called Virtues appear to be called Drives now, and Edges appear to be more like HtV's Endowments, in that their organizing principle is <i>not</i> the Creeds (which <i>are</i> still a thing), but appear to be more of an extension of how the Numina are organized (we explicitly have Psychic Phenomena and True Faith among H5's Edges). But even with those changes, the basic skeleton is already there: Conviction, Drives, Edges, and Creeds. <br /> <br /> What appears to be missing is the lore, where the hunters are the Chosen of the Messengers and Imbued with Edges that echo their Creeds, in a last-ditch effort to stave off the end of the world. That could <i>easily</i> be reintroduced as a type of Edges (call them Imbuements) which are granted by mysterious supernatural benefactors and <i>are</i> organized by Creed; and things like the Sight and Hunter's Code could be recast as effects of the first Imbuement that everyone with Imbuements gets. No other new game systems would be needed beyond what H5 is already providing. <br /> <br /> The only thing lost is the \u201cimminent end of the world\u201d aspect; as monteparnas suggests here, it may be that there <i>were</i> Imbued for a time, around the end of the last millennium; but when the world failed to end, their benefactors essentially said \u201coops; we didn't need to do that after all\u201d and stopped Imbuing hunters. Reintroducing the Imbued would then theoretically involve justifying the Messengers returning and taking up the practice again. In short, they'd need to be recast in a way that makes sense without the \u201clatter days metaplot\u201d that dominated the World of Darkness from 1999\u20132003. <br /> <br /> But even if they were to be brought back, I'm fine with them no longer being central to the game. As I said in my first post to this thread, my personal play style for HtR was to go with Bystanders (and then only because of the game benefits of Bystander-style Conviction and access to a handful of Merits designed to help them maintain agency in the face of Delirium/the Fog/the Mists); the \u201cBuffy the Vampire Slayer\u201d vibe was never my thing. I liked the Conviction/Virtues/Creeds stuff, and regretted that Bystanders didn't tap into any of that. I'd be okay with the Imbued being reintroduced as one option among many, for those who like them; but I really like how it looks like this will make all of the things I liked about the original HtR available to me without forcing me to take on all of the things I <i>didn't</i> like. <br /> <br /> BTW, is there any news on how this is progressing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-29-2022, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T09:37:31-08:00","id":1473531,"title":"","content":"I don't remember we getting anything else other than those blogs on the official WoD website about Hunter, and things have been quiet for all the end of 2021 and all this January of 2022. I don't know when more will be revealed. The V5 Inquisition book is scheduled for March (at least the Renegade site tells us so, but the Sabbat book didn't arrive at the release date written at the site so...). It seems there is no rush, and even though that is good, I kind of miss getting the hype and antecipation with each new info they put out. Things have been quiet from Paradox's WoD studios for a while. Last thing I remember was that free surprise New Year's chronicle for V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T15:36:24-08:00","id":1473544,"title":"","content":"It wasn't really a surprise, Renegade had announced there was something coming for New Year's.<br /> The Inquisition book was originally scheduled for December, being postponed alongside the Sabbat, due to shipping delays, initially to late January, and postponed again now to March, for the same reasons. The SI books are apparently stuck in shipping as far as we know.<br /> <br /> As for Hunter News, It's odd that there has been little news regarding it, considering the writing was finished months ago.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T19:16:17-08:00","id":1473624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1473544#post1473544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">,,,<br /> As for Hunter News, It's odd that there has been little news regarding it, considering the writing was finished months ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. WoD/Renegade news concerning books has pretty much followed the pattern of announcement of the book and then we don't hear about it again until they're ready to put it on sale. I wouldn't expect to hear any news until the book is ready for pre-sale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T13:12:40-08:00","id":1473853,"title":"","content":"What's funny to me is the idea that W5 is such a... <i>delicate </i>product that they'll grab what might be HH, a small dependent companion piece, and give it a full WoD title in that &quot;Kind of Person: the Event&quot; style to make it seem like they're doing something big and aren't totally lost with what to write for W5 beyond title and credits. <br /> <br /> (I mean, I don't entirely blame them, Werewolf is a minefield)<br /> I never played HTR, but I don't think mysterious gods empowering people to blast supernaturals really fits the faux progressive narrative, so I'm not suprised it's cut, though I am dissapointed. <br /> <br /> HH is a dope game with a dope title. I don't see the need to drag HTR down. Like if I wanted to watch a Batman film and they faked out and gave me a Superman movie, i'd be annoyed, even though I like Superman more. If they told me Batman no longer exists and he's just like Superman now, I'd be quite upset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T13:26:04-08:00","id":1473855,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superman:_Speeding_Bullets\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6c/SupermanSpeedingBullets.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> Oh, I don't know; a Superman movie masquerading as a Batman movie could be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-02-2022, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T16:12:23-08:00","id":1474451,"title":"","content":"The whole premise of the post revised gamelines is that the End Times events really happened but with the twist that they didn't really destroy the world, just changed it. In the case of HtR, looking at what happened in the End Times book could be a good exercise to understand why the imbued might not be around anymore and what we are dealing with a different breed of hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T12:38:03-08:00","id":1474509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474451#post1474451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole premise of the post revised gamelines is that the End Times events really happened but with the twist that they didn't really destroy the world, just changed it. In the case of HtR, looking at what happened in the End Times book could be a good exercise to understand why the imbued might not be around anymore and what we are dealing with a different breed of hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explaining isn't the point, they actually can do that quite easily. But they can just as easily have the Imbued around and explain that. So it is a decision to not have them, and people is upset with this decision. For now, since we still don't know what form exactly the game will take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T13:12:14-08:00","id":1474512,"title":"","content":"Agreed. To me, there's a very simple explanation for them no longer being around: the world <i>didn't</i> end, and the existential crisis has passed. Sure, there's still some danger that matters will worsen and disaster will once again loom; but that's only a <i>possibility</i>. So the Heralds and Messengers withdrew the Imbuing. <br /> <br /> Just how important was it that the hunters were Imbued by Messengers with Creed-based superpowers? From the preview, it looks like you literally have <i>everything else</i> that made HtR what it was: humans from ordinary backgrounds fighting monsters and getting in over their heads; Conviction; <s>Virtues</s>Drives; Creeds; and Edges. In 1e, the Messengers played a role in the Imbuing; but after that, they were entirely hands-off. The Imbued we're left entirely in the dark and on their own in terms of what the Imbuing was and what they were supposed to do. So exactly how is the game any different if they're in the dark and on their own because there <i>are</i> no Messengers empowering them? <br /> <br /> Frankly, the only thing from 1e that hasn't been confirmed for 5e that I'll miss if they don't show up in some form of another were the \u201cagency-preserving powers\u201d: the ability for hunters to ignore the likes of the Delirium and the Mists; the ability to continue to think rationally even when other mortals would be supernaturally compelled to behave irrationally. I don't need Cleave, or the Sight, or the Code, or the supernaturally shielded Hunter-net; just keep my hunter from becoming a lunatic the moment a shapeshifting beastman appears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T15:25:00-08:00","id":1474525,"title":"","content":"I am sure this has been brought up before but....V5 is supposed to be a mix of Masquerade and Requiem.<br /> I feel they are now trying to make Reckoning to be a cross between it and Vigil.<br /> <br /> I will get it when it comes out to see it and to see if I was right or proven absolutely wrong.<br /> I pray it is the latter but I have my doubts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T16:03:47-08:00","id":1474530,"title":"","content":"I have no doubt that the X5 lines are all borrowing ideas from the Chronicles of Darkness. However, my suspicion with H5 is that there's more to it than that. Phil Brucato mentioned that back in 1999, when WW was designing Hunter: the Reckoning, one of the disappointments he had with it was that he envisioned it as a book about ordinary people dealing with the discovery that the world was supernatural, and wanted it to focus more on that aspect; but the bulk of the developers went straight to \u201cwhat kinds of powers should they have?\u201d<br /> <br /> If the folks at ParaWolf are more like Brucato in sentiment than the original design team for HtR, it would make sense that they're attempting to de-emphasize the \u201cImbued with power to fight the supernatural\u201d side of it. <br /> <br /> If that's true, the parallels between H5 and HtV, to the extent that they exist, are more of a coincidence than a direct borrowing. Well, maybe not \u201ccoincidence\u201d; more like, if you're making a game about ordinary people hunting monsters, it's hard <i>not</i> to have parallels to HtV: you'd have to actively work to <i>avoid</i> them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T19:39:19-08:00","id":1474543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474512#post1474512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, the only thing from 1e that hasn't been confirmed for 5e that I'll miss if they don't show up in some form of another were the \u201cagency-preserving powers\u201d: the ability for hunters to ignore the likes of the Delirium and the Mists; the ability to continue to think rationally even when other mortals would be supernaturally compelled to behave irrationally. I don't need Cleave, or the Sight, or the Code, or the supernaturally shielded Hunter-net; just keep my hunter from becoming a lunatic the moment a shapeshifting beastman appears.</div> </div> </div> </div>That heavily depends on the other gamelines and not Hunter though. We don't know how Delirium will be in W5 and C5 is still a far away dream .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T20:39:38-08:00","id":1474546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474525#post1474525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sure this has been brought up before but....</div> </div> </div> </div>It has, repeatedly, and I'm half intrigued half upset with this nonsensical notion that everything wrong with V5 came from it borrowing from Requiem.<br /> <br /> But on topic, this isn't relevant for Hunter at all anyway. Reckoning was the outlier in having a structure of powers like the supernatural splats do for Hunters, instead or assuming ordinary people and adding the option of a handful of minor powers. This second approach wasn't invented by Vigil, it was already in Hunters Hunted, so it is as old as hunters in WoD.<br /> <br /> Without the Imbued there's little to add in terms of themes and tropes to the whole idea. Not that in any way invalidates a core book for them, it is just that there's no sense in saying it is copying this or that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T22:26:52-08:00","id":1474547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474509#post1474509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Explaining isn't the point, they actually can do that quite easily. But they can just as easily have the Imbued around and explain that. So it is a decision to not have them, and people is upset with this decision. For now, since we still don't know what form exactly the game will take.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they had just called it Hunters: the Hunting or whatever and then just ignored the existence of Hunter: the Reckoning and acted as though it had never existed in the newer 5E metaverse, that would have been fine. HtR never had a particularly major impact on the other gamelines, so it would have been easy enough to ignore. But calling it Hunter: the Reckoning while also saying that Hunter: the Reckoning doesn't exist just sort of feels like a slap in the face to people who enjoyed playing Hunter: the Reckoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T09:37:07-08:00","id":1474570,"title":"","content":"lot of people getting slapped in the face in WoD 5th edition it will seem","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T12:49:45-08:00","id":1474579,"title":"","content":"Honestly... the whole &quot;slap in the face&quot; thing would be more tolerable if WoD 5e was actually, well, ground breaking in any way, shape, or form. If WoD 5e was the next Apocalypse World that would be leading to a whole new decade of mainstream game design by showing true success with a unique remixing of old ideas into a coherently new package? I could take some slaps to the face.<br /> <br /> But WoD 5e is a nostalgia brand that's trying to be relevant in contemporary culture. That's by no means impossible to pull off, but nostalgia brands can't run away from the sources of that nostalgia. Nothing in it is revolutionizing TTRPGs; hell none of its social commentary is actually new (more disappointing for the Gen X/old Millenial crowd to see how little the world's changed). So I'm getting slapped in the face for no reason I can comprehend besides someone feeling like it would be cool to slap me in the face, instead of getting slapped in the face to snap out of my current headspace and see something in a new meaningful light.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T18:01:22-08:00","id":1474592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474546#post1474546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has, repeatedly, and I'm half intrigued half upset with this nonsensical notion that everything wrong with V5 came from it borrowing from Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm half intrigued and half upset about this thing <i>happening</i>.<br /> <br /> On one hand, it does make sense to take ideas from both - Heck, it's not <i>too </i>controversial to say that the newer mechanics of NWoD are in some ways better.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand, Why did it had to be like <u>this</u>?:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ... if you're making a game about ordinary people hunting monsters, it's hard <i>not</i> to have parallels to HtV: you'd have to actively work to <i>avoid</i> them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it shouln't be hard to imagine why this sort of move would be both &quot;a slap on the face&quot; and an easy add on the list of &quot;everything wrong with 5th ed came from it borrowing from NWoD&quot;...<br /> <br /> ...because, even if the &quot;conspiracy theory&quot; it's nonsensical, <i>it seems to be the result</i> <i>anyway</i>. Isn't it?...maybe it won't be but for now it sure sounds like it.<br /> <br /> It makes me wonder what would be if they worked actively to avoid the comparison. Perhaps it's not a bad idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-13-2022, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T03:02:14-08:00","id":1474606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474592#post1474592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...because, even if the &quot;conspiracy theory&quot; it's nonsensical, <i>it seems to be the result</i> <i>anyway</i>. Isn't it?...maybe it won't be but for now it sure sounds like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They borrowed a lot of mechanics from VtR, but they also made a lot of their own things. More than that, I saw much more complains about lore than mechanics, and they borrowed no lore from VtR in a meaningful way. You can draw comparisons, but not more than you can draw between VtR and VtM anyways.<br /> <br /> It is hard to not draw parallels between H5 and HtV because this is the simplest, most obvious concept possible. So much so that it is actually Hunters Hunted and I challenge you to point a single concept from Vigil that was not already in HH.<br /> <br /> At the end the parallel is obvious only because people are actively trying to make it, and no amount of work on their part will avoid the comparison, a comparison that helps nothing in understanding what really went wrong as it just reduces it to &quot;is wrong because they're borrowing from that other game&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T04:31:25-08:00","id":1474609,"title":"","content":"There was a lot of complaint about mechanics borrowed from Requiem: Myself and a lot of people complained about Touchstones, it was arguably the most polemical thing other than the Tremere lore and Hunger (it was also complained that it wasn't borrowed <i>rigth</i>). There was also the lore aspects of the Camarilla being sligthly more like Invictus than it already was, or the Elders being presented as less of an element (as per the Basic, not the supplements). Perhaps all of these weren't treated as &quot;the horror&quot;, and IF i'm calling it a &quot;conspiracy theory&quot; it's because I would agree that the similarities are coincidental, and not <i>necessarily </i>a bad thing - still, the comparison it's natural to draw which brings us to the real problem of this thread.<br /> <br /> <b>It's easy to draw comparisons between HtV, HH and H5 - what's harder it's to draw a paralel between HtR 5th and<u> Hunter the Reckoning</u>.</b><br /> <br /> It would have been super easy to avoid the comparison, they just had to make an actual HtR 5e. The concepts are so different that one would be hard press to talk about <i>requiemizing </i>BUT they didn't do that now, did they?, <i>what they did it's to replace the concept for a different one that's easy to compare with HtV</i><br /> <br /> Way to add wood to the fire.<br /> <br /> Moreover, while HH and HtV may be similar, they're not the only way to tackle the concept of &quot;human v.s monsters&quot; \u00bfdo you really can't imagine other way to organize a human vs. monsters game that's not a general popurry of different archetypes of hunters - some of which have supernatural powers, some who don't, some are organized, some aren't?. The whole problem it's that they went with the same concept. If that concept was already in HH that's simply deflecting the point, it's not <i>solving </i>it<br /> <br /> Don't blame the public: We're not the &quot;active&quot; force here, we're just *reacting* to what's being presented in the most natural and obvious way possible. If it's wrong it's wrong, but you can't blame us for seeing what's clearly there to be seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-14-2022, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T05:13:36-08:00","id":1474611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474609#post1474609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't blame the public</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not. Not in this sense.<br /> <br /> You said nothing at all that I don't agree and said myself earlier, give or take some details.<br /> <br /> My exact phrasing that you commented upon was about the comparison with Requiem and not that the problems don't exist or don't have to be addressed. So what, I can't be upset with people making a shitty comparison that <u><i>also</i></u> solves nothing?<br /> <br /> Quite the contrary, this comparison by itself is just deflecting the point, as the similarities with other lines aren't the actual problem and the comparison just creates undue resentment against something that is <u><b>not</b></u> the source of the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T05:57:30-08:00","id":1474615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474609#post1474609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>It's easy to draw comparisons between HtV, HH and H5 - what's harder it's to draw a paralel between HtR 5th and<u> Hunter the Reckoning</u>.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that hard to do. I've been doing it throughout this thread, in fact. You still have the same basic structure to the game: Conviction, Creeds, <s>Virtues</s>Drives, and Edges; the playstyle is still the same: hunters on their own, fighting against monsters. H5 <i>doesn't</i> include playing as members of a hunter organization, just as HtR didn't (the mention of hunter orgs in the preview makes a point that they're antagonists by default); it's just that their existence is being addressed in the core book instead of a supplement. The only things missing are the Messengers (who almost never made any impact on the game in HtR outside of the hunter's backstory) and supernatural Edges organized mostly by <s>Virtue</s>Drive. <br /> <br /> And for all we know, H5 <i>will</i> still address the \u201cBuffy the Vampire Slayer\u201d flavor of play that some HtR fans enjoyed. We haven't yet seen what all of the Edges are, and it won't surprise me if the likes of Cleave shows up somewhere. So even <i>that</i> parallel may yet remain. It's just not the central focus of the game anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T14:58:27-08:00","id":1474651,"title":"","content":"I need a bit more than names to say that. The protagonists of HtR weren't just &quot;hunters on their own, fighting against monsters&quot; - that could easily be describing the first chapters of HH, but you can't play HtR with HH: Imbued were a splat of their own, really, one designed to figth the supernatural. As distinct from other humans as Mages are<br /> <br /> What you call Agency Powers was an <i>important </i>part of that - <i>perhaps the most important</i>. One of the other main characteristics of the Hunters was that they received hints and clues about the supernatural in everyday objects like road signs and newspapers. I remember that was one of the sellpoints of the book back in the day. They weren't just &quot;hunters&quot;, they were this people that was being guided by misterious, almost surrealist, powers. <i>They were true &quot;chosen ones&quot;.</i> How many hunters from HH can say that?<br /> <br /> It didn't had organizations, but it had the potential of having them - see, actually having Hunter organizations could still be a &quot;HtR new edition&quot; because such were on the making. It was a possible future of the lore and could be a metaplot update. It was one of the &quot;goals&quot; of the setting. I'm sure many old fans would have wanted to see see how that evolved.<br /> <br /> The Core of HtR is...what was in the Core. I don't need to know what the Messengers are and whatnot, but If I don't get at least that short piece of content that originaly depicted The Imbued as their own thing with their own short and powerful story, how can it be HtR 5e?.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My exact phrasing that you commented upon was about the comparison with Requiem and not that the problems don't exist or don't have to be addressed. So what, I can't be upset with people making a shitty comparison that <u><i>also</i></u> solves nothing?<br /> <br /> Quite the contrary, this comparison by itself is just deflecting the point, as the similarities with other lines aren't the actual problem and the comparison just creates undue resentment against something that is <u><b>not</b></u> the source of the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't love the comparison, but that doesn't change that it's eerily easy to make:<br /> <br /> &quot;Not having Imbued&quot;, and having &quot;a Hunter gameline that's a lot like HH&quot; it's how CoD rolls. Isn't it?. I think that's how Vigil was first described to me back in the day.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a coincidence, with Phill disappointment and all that, but it's becoming harder not to see a trend here.<br /> <br /> I mean, what's next?, justifying why it's not inspired in CoD, and totally coherent with Demon, to have God being a machine. :P There's a lot of fiction where God it's a machine! , a MtA Paradigm even!.:P .<br /> <br /> Would you become a &quot;believer&quot; if that happened? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-14-2022, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T19:32:10-08:00","id":1474682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474651#post1474651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need a bit more than names to say that. The protagonists of HtR weren't just &quot;hunters on their own, fighting against monsters&quot; - that could easily be describing the first chapters of HH, but you can't play HtR with HH: Imbued were a splat of their own, really, one designed to figth the supernatural. As distinct from other humans as Mages are<br /> <br /> What you call Agency Powers was an <i>important </i>part of that - <i>perhaps the most important</i>. One of the other main characteristics of the Hunters was that they received hints and clues about the supernatural in everyday objects like road signs and newspapers. I remember that was one of the sellpoints of the book back in the day. They weren't just &quot;hunters&quot;, they were this people that was being guided by misterious, almost surrealist, powers. <i>They were true &quot;chosen ones&quot;.</i> How many hunters from HH can say that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, is too early to say for certain that H5 will rule out the \u201cBuffy the Vampire Slayer\u201d playstyle. All we know for certain is that it won't be the central focus of the game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474651#post1474651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It didn't had organizations, but it had the potential of having them - see, actually having Hunter organizations could still be a &quot;HtR new edition&quot; because such were on the making. It was a possible future of the lore and could be a metaplot update. It was one of the &quot;goals&quot; of the setting. I'm sure many old fans would have wanted to see see how that evolved.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you'd be okay if H5 borrowed the \u201ccompacts and conspiracies\u201d concept from HtV? So would I; but then, I've never pushed the notion that there's anything inherently wrong with X20 lines borrowing from the Chronicles of Darkness. It all depends on how it's done. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474651#post1474651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Core of HtR is...what was in the Core. I don't need to know what the Messengers are and whatnot, but If I don't get at least that short piece of content that originaly depicted The Imbued as their own thing with their own short and powerful story, how can it be HtR 5e?</div> </div> </div> </div> To be pedantic for a moment, it can't ever be 5e, because there has yet to be even a 2e, let alone a 3e or a 4e. But with that out of the way: let's say that it <i>does</i> turn out that H5's history section talks about how the Imbued appeared briefly around the turn of the century, made a big splash, and then petered out, either dying or losing their powers, and they're no longer around today. Would it then be okay as you see it to call this Hunter the Reckoning? Or will it only work for you if H5 supports playing Buffy? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474651#post1474651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't love the comparison, but that doesn't change that it's eerily easy to make:<br /> <br /> &quot;Not having Imbued&quot;, and having &quot;a Hunter gameline that's a lot like HH&quot; it's how CoD rolls. Isn't it?. I think that's how Vigil was first described to me back in the day.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a coincidence, with Phil disappointment and all that, but it's becoming harder not to see a trend here.<br /> <br /> I mean, what's next?, justifying why it's not inspired in CoD, and totally coherent with Demon, to have God being a machine. :P There's a lot of fiction where God it's a machine! , a MtA Paradigm even!.:P .<br /> <br /> Would you become a &quot;believer&quot; if that happened? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that \u201chunter\u201d was associated with the HH stuff for far longer than it was ever associated with the Imbued: 1992 until 1999, including an entire \u201cYear of the Hunter\u201d in 1996 where nearly every gameline got into the act of describing the mostly ordinary mortals who hunted that gameline's kind. HtV merely returned to that original formula; it's HtR's Imbued who are the odd man out here \u2014 the Deviation* from the norm, of you will. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">* Inside joke, as I consider the best match for the Imbued in the Chronicles of Darkness to be Deviant, not Hunter. And that's not a particularly good match, either.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-14-2022, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T20:05:09-08:00","id":1474695,"title":"","content":"How are we still repeating these same things....<br /> <br /> In general, I think you're taking things too far <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> and I generally feel like we're more on the same page than not (at least with the Hunter stuff). Dataweaver and monteparnas aren't wrong in their push back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474682#post1474682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I said, is too early to say for certain that H5 will rule out the \u201cBuffy the Vampire Slayer\u201d playstyle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you stop that?<br /> <br /> I don't want &quot;Buffy the Vampire Slayer&quot; playstyle. I don't even know what that's supposed to mean. Buffy is HH or HtV, not HtR. Buffy is part of an ongoing conspiracy where the Watchers train and support the Slayer to combat demons that's been in place for centuries. That's not Imbued. That's the WoD Arcanum mixed with the CofD's Lucifuge (not worried about a spoiler on how the Slayers were created).<br /> <br /> I want the Imbued playstyle. It's its own thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you'd be okay if H5 borrowed the \u201ccompacts and conspiracies\u201d concept from HtV? </div> </div> </div>HtR had it's own ideas of growing Hunter organizations from the initial cells of PCs long before HtV happened. H5 doesn't need to borrow that, even if it probably will since it's not using the Imbued and those organizations were built around the specifics of the Imbued.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would it then be okay as you see it to call this Hunter the Reckoning? </div> </div> </div>No. HtR is about the Imbued. Trying HtR as a blip in the wider concept of hunters in the WoD should mean the book is called something other than Reckoning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The difference is that \u201chunter\u201d was associated with the HH stuff for far longer than it was ever associated with the Imbued: 1992 until 1999, including an entire \u201cYear of the Hunter\u201d in 1996 where nearly every gameline got into the act of describing the mostly ordinary mortals who hunted that gameline's kind. HtV merely returned to that original formula; it's HtR's Imbued who are the odd man out here \u2014 the Deviation* from the norm, of you will. </div> </div> </div>So? HH includes vampires that hunt other vampires. That's not part of HtV.<br /> <br /> Aleph's overstating things, yes, but your pushback is going too far in the other direction to actually get at the core of the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T21:42:03-08:00","id":1474701,"title":"","content":"Sorry; the Buffy bit was over the line. I do get what the original HtR playstyle is like; and aside from a handful of agency preserving Merits from the Bystanders section of the Player's Guide, it's not really my thing. But I shouldn't have taken it that far. <br /> <br /> Also, \u201cHH style\u201d is perhaps the wrong way to phrase it. More like \u201cYear of the Hunter\u201d style, except that the Year of the Hunter books focused mostly on hunter organizations (the Inquisition, government agencies, the Arcanum, various ghost hunter factions) rather than individuals. When HtR was first announced, that's what a lot of us were looking for: regular people who were made aware of the supernatural threats around them and decided to do something about it. The Imbued, being supernaturally empowered to the last of them, were <i>not</i> what we were looking for. <br /> <br /> What I've been seeing of H5 so far is a lot closer to what I wanted to see the first time around. If they could incorporate something like the aforementioned Bystander traits (HPG pp.51\u201352, 56\u201360), I'd have everything I want from the original game. The rest of it was, as I see it, merely an attempt to help sell the then-brand-new Exalted game by planting hints that the Imbued were somehow the former Solar Exalted reborn into the modern world. That required the Imbued to be more than just ordinary people who had been alerted to the presence of the supernatural; it required them to be supernatural beings themselves. Because so were the Exalted. <br /> <br /> That said, I would not object if each Creed were given an optional Edge that brings the HtR Edges into H5 \u2014 optional, so that those of us who prefer something more like the HH style don't end up having to house-rule the game to get rid of them. That, combined with the Bystander traits, would allow for the Imbued style of gameplay for those who want it. I <i>do</i> hope that they include something like that in H5; I could even get behind the notion that the Messengers are still around, bringing monsters to peoples' attention but no longer Imbuing them, and the \u201cBystander\u201d traits can arise as a result of that. Just as long as encountering monsters on your own is also an option for becoming a Hunter. <br /> <br /> But (other than the Bystander traits, particularly Hardened Spirit, Resistant to Supernatural Fear, and Resistant to Mind Control; the agency-preserving traits) I also won't be disappointed if the Imbued are not there. <br /> <br /> Or there's another option: do True Faith as the H5 version of the Imbued, with Virtues stacked on top of the Drives in a manner similar to how Dark Ages: Inquisitor replaced True Faith with a set of Superior Virtues, and those Virtue dots entitling you to Creed-based powers based on 1e's Edges. The idea here is that throughout history, the Messengers have <i>always</i> been around, empowering mortals with sufficient Drive and Religious Devotion (HPG p.97) with divine guidance and assistance; and that has traditionally been represented in the game by the True Faith mechanics. But when the Reckoning happened, they \u201cbroke protocol\u201d and extended the scope of their empowerments, resulting in them Imbuing individuals who <i>wouldn't</i> have qualified for it before, when only the faithful were Imbued. After the crisis passed, they mostly went back to their old MO. As such, most of the remaining Imbued are true believers (in <i>some</i> sort of higher power; not necessarily the Christian God), though a few outliers still exist. <br /> <br /> There: you get your Imbued, complete with a place within the new structure of the game, and I get my mortal Hunter. Heck, I might even find some interest in <i>playing</i> this version of the Imbued.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-15-2022, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T03:25:26-08:00","id":1474717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474701#post1474701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry; the Buffy bit was over the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is it over the line?<br /> <br /> The problem is that it's what Tier 3 mixed splat HtV looks like. The Slayers have an Endowment that grants them superhuman physicals. The Watchers and Witches have an Endowment that lets them access supernatural Merits. A few full supernaturals decided to ally with the group. Xander has a weird unique Endowment that drastically increases his Skill dots as the plot demands (this isn't even some meta thing that keeps him relevant, one episode he got turned into a GI Joe style soldier and even after that ended, he's shown to have retained and refined skills he had access do from that experience). The Initiative is a joint operation between TFV and the Cheiron group practically on the nose.<br /> <br /> Buffy is HH with a bunch of Numina users and loner supernaturals from different backgrounds coming together. Buffy is high level HtV.<br /> <br /> Buffy, despite Joss Whedon, was popular, and people want to play that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> HtR wasn't that though.<br /> <br /> [quote...it's not really my thing.[/quote]<br /> <br /> Nobody's asking for you to change your mind on this. Just respect that the people for whom HtR is their thing don't want their thing being removed from a new edition of HtR because Paradox doesn't seem to want to actually make a new edition of HtR, but wants the HtR branding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When HtR was first announced, that's what a lot of us were looking for: regular people who were made aware of the supernatural threats around them and decided to do something about it. The Imbued, being supernaturally empowered to the last of them, were <i>not</i> what we were looking for. </div> </div> </div>And what does that have to do with a new edition of HtR not being what HtR turned out to be?<br /> <br /> The fact that H5 is more your speed doesn't address why it should be called HtR if it's not going to be what HtR was about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rest of it was, as I see it, merely an attempt to help sell the then-brand-new Exalted game by planting hints that the Imbued were somehow the former Solar Exalted reborn into the modern world. </div> </div> </div>People that actually wrote for the books have repeatedly refuted this nonsense. The Exalted-WoD connections were (1) not just in HtR and (2) turned into Easter Eggs before anything besides a single ad campaign went to print.<br /> <br /> If you believe this, then you must believe that <b>all of Revised</b> was a giant ad for Exalted: VtM Revised was about selling Abyssals, WtA Revised Lunars, etc. because there's just as many Easter eggs in all the other game lines as their are in HtR, and they matter just as much to being able to enjoy those games independent of Exalted.<br /> <br /> If you think it sounds crazy that Mage Revised was merely an attempt to sell Sidereal Exalted by planting hints that the Awakened were somehow the former Sidereal Exalted reborn through the ages (as they were never imprisoned like the Solars were)? Guess what. There's as much evidence of that being the case as the Imbued were supposed to be the Solars revived.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it required them to be supernatural beings themselves. </div> </div> </div>Why is it required that so many of the HH/YotH splats are supernatural beings themselves? They're practically all Numina users of some stripe (assuming their not full supernatural splats like the Children of Osiris).<br /> <br /> Why is it required that there's a whole group of HtV splats that are defined by being having access to supernatural powers instead of hunting with mundane weapons and smarts?<br /> <br /> Because they need to actually stand a chance against what's out there in their settings. Just like the Imbued have powers that give them a chance against the supernatural monsters they fight.<br /> <br /> One of the seeming never ending frustrations with ever talking about HH vs. HtR is this insipid idea that HH/YotH is about &quot;mundane mortals that totally aren't supernaturals,&quot; but HtR is about the Imbued, who are &quot;true supernaturals.&quot; Even though it's complete bullshit.<br /> <br /> HH/YotH/etc. Where the Vatican's D&amp;D-Cleric special ops teams, Psychic power used government agents, sorcery wielding members of a mysterious organization with dark secrets that studies the supernatural, Qi powered anime kung-fu monster hunters, and cyborgs all take on the nasties of the WoD are the books that aren't about &quot;supernatural beings themselves.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I would not object if each Creed were given an optional Edge that brings the HtR Edges into H5 \u2014 optional, so that those of us who prefer something more like the HH style don't end up having to house-rule the game to get rid of them. </div> </div> </div>What does that even mean?<br /> <br /> &quot;It's fine if H5 has characters that can study mystic martial arts to punch supernaturals for aggravated damage, but if the ability to channel conviction to the hunt into mundane weapons so they do more damage isn't regulated to optional rules, the game will be ruined.&quot;<br /> <br /> That seems a very odd hill to fight on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That, combined with the Bystander traits, would allow for the Imbued style of gameplay for those who want it. </div> </div> </div>No. HtR with a proper clean up would allow the Imbued style of play I want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or there's another option: do True Faith as the H5 version of the Imbued.. </div> </div> </div>No. That's not the Imbued, that's a half measure that lets people that don't like the Imbued feel like they're through the fans of the Imbued a bone while they forget that we're humans and bones don't actually do us much good.<br /> <br /> For all that you seem to say that you understand what the Imbued playstyle is... you really don't do a good job of showing it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T06:06:28-08:00","id":1474730,"title":"","content":"Okay, could you knock that off, please? I began my last post with an apology for going too far, and your response basically ignored that and proceeded to attack me. Please, at the very least accept the apology in the spirit in which it was intended, and then respond to the rest of the post with that in mind.<br /> <br /> As for the rest of my post, I was trying to find common ground. Could you please at least read it with that in mind, instead of just assuming that I'm continuing to attack you and your preferences?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-15-2022, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T06:47:29-08:00","id":1474734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474695#post1474695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are we still repeating these same things....<br /> In general, I think you're taking things too far Aleph and I generally feel like we're more on the same page than not (at least with the Hunter stuff). Dataweaver and monteparnas aren't wrong in their push back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're rigth.<br /> <br /> I got angry at the argument of HtR5e being similar to HtV because both are similar to HH. That's a non argument on so many levels...But it ultimately doesn't matter, it's a side thing as monteparnas said ( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>: sorry for the derisive tone before, It was uncalled for. But I will keep bringing this up, if it keeps happening).<br /> <br /> Hopefully we're going to see the potential to make Imbued with the rules, and they're just killed in metaplot. Not a real fix but better than nothing and, I think, best we can hope for at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-15-2022, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T13:36:28-08:00","id":1474756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474730#post1474730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I began my last post with an apology for going too far, and your response basically ignored that and proceeded to attack me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're standing on my foot, and instead of getting off my foot, you're apologizing that my drink got spilled. Starting with apologizing for something that isn't the pressing complaint isn't a good apology that will get a positive response.<br /> <br /> I never said anything about calling HtR &quot;Buffy play style&quot; as something that was &quot;over the top,&quot; so why are you expecting me to care about you apologizing for that being over the top instead of, say, apologizing for it being completely misplaced, or a complete misrepresentation of HH, YotH, DHX, HtR, and Buffy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Please, at the very least accept the apology in the spirit in which it was intended, and then respond to the rest of the post with that in mind. </div> </div> </div>I can't read your mind to know your true intent. I'm not accepting your non-apology because I don't feel any desire to do so, nor is trying some public shaming effort going to change my feelings on that going to go anywhere. If you want to try again with an apology that actually follows the basic principles of a baseline apology, I'll respond to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the rest of my post, I was trying to find common ground. Could you please at least read it with that in mind, instead of just assuming that I'm continuing to attack you and your preferences? </div> </div> </div>monteparnas (on page 4) and ArcaneArts (on page 7) already posted good common ground solutions; even if impractical because Paradox isn't doing them.<br /> <br /> The problem is simple. There's no common ground for old school HtR fans where a new edition of HtR doesn't have the Imbued as core characters. The common ground would be expanding HtR to have more core coverage of non-Imbued hunters (as monteparnas suggested, essentially, playable Bystanders as playable Ghouls, and low key mortal hunters as Thin-bloods to cover similar ground as V5). Anything that involves the Imbued getting cut, sidelined, or reworked into something radically different than before isn't common ground; it's telling the Imbued fans to get lost.<br /> <br /> I believe your intentions are good. But if you want me to stop acting like you're taking a massive shit on a game I love? Stop taking a massive shit on it by telling me how compromises you'd like should be satisfactory to me despite me not getting the game I want. The fact that I really to believe your intentions are good is making it worse, because I am at my wits end trying to figure out how your intentions are coming out so tremendously opposite in result in a way that's still not purposeful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T18:43:56-08:00","id":1474769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474734#post1474734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">( <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>: sorry for the derisive tone before, It was uncalled for. But I will keep bringing this up, if it keeps happening).</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense taken, relax. My problem is actually the same, just coming from another perspective on the matter.<br /> <br /> Despite never being a fan of HtR myself I fully recognize the problem: as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, the problem isn't if H5 is similar to this or that, but that HtR is about the Imbued. Period. The problem is making H5 not about the Imbued.<br /> <br /> If the line were to be called Hunters Hunted 5th edition, Reckoning fans would still and rightfully be asking for a new HtR, but this whole conversation would be entirely different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474701#post1474701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I've been seeing of H5 so far is a lot closer to what I wanted to see the first time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, me too, but that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> Whatever we wanted to see when HtR came, it ended up being something else, <b><u>and this something has its fans. A lot of them.</u></b> Do you think it right to use the brand to make what we wanted instead of what the actual fans of the old HtR wanted? Especially when it is easy to incorporate our desired style in a line with the Imbued and us just ignore them, while excising the Imbued is basically a a stone wall on the path of anyone wanting to play them, in the official setting.<br /> <br /> I never liked HtR, yet it existing never stopped me from using Hunters as I actually like in my games, whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Did I felt that there was little support for my preferred play style? Certainly, and I will be glad to find it in this new game. But this support in no way demands the Imbued to not exist. This isn't a fair exchange, not at all.<br /> <br /> And saying that having similar powers and whatnot is enough to cover for the lack of the Imbued is like saying that Masquerade can be extinguished because Book of the Wyrm has enough rules to cover Vampires as fomorians or that Apocalypse may be dropped if we have a Revenant family with custom Protean powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T08:31:48-08:00","id":1474902,"title":"","content":"Hunter in proofing stage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1494359139493023747?s=21\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1494359139493023747?s=21\" target=\"_blank\"> Post Not Found - X | 404 Error </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1494359139493023747?s=21\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1494359139493023747?s=21 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The post you're looking for could not be found or may have been deleted. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T11:04:33-08:00","id":1474997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1474902#post1474902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter in proofing stage.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1494359139493023747?s=21\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/...493023747?s=21</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Boyah! It's coming out soon! <br /> <br /> New 5th edition WoD releases always make me excited. I really wanna see how they make Hunters now, and how the setting of them is presented. And with some luck there will be more in-depth mechanics for things other games may use (or not).<br /> I'm eager to see how the Drive, Despair and Creed system works together in the game, cuz it really seems like a fun dynamic. We will just have to wait to play it out.<br /> <br /> Second Inquisition orgs won't be the only thing that comes knocking","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T13:26:14-08:00","id":1475005,"title":"","content":"Just throwing my two cents in here<br /> I completely understand why many will miss the Imbued,they are insanely cool. But I'm looking forward to by anyways","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T16:04:22-08:00","id":1475806,"title":"","content":"Well....the cover is shite.<br /> <br /> Not that that has any bearing on the contents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T16:21:06-08:00","id":1475809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Origin