Hunter in my opinion. <br /> I mean... it reminded me of any photo of an Irish folk band in all respect to them.<br /> I still expect an awesome game","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T22:04:16-08:00","id":1475825,"title":"","content":"The cover reminds of something you would see on a political campaign flyer. Which...yeah that does not seem like an appropriate vibe to Hunter.<br /> <br /> That being said for the rest of the art: no, it's not all photos like V5 corebook was. And back to two column layout instead of three. So there's that at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T16:49:31-08:00","id":1475864,"title":"","content":"One one hand, I never really understand putting promo material behind an account. Like... you want people to see promo material to get them into your site... you don't lock it behind making an account just to see what your free previews are.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it means I'm not looking it over yet and getting annoyed at it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T00:01:00-08:00","id":1475882,"title":"","content":"I saw the art preview before and this cover is very disappointing in comparison. Sadly, people *do* judge a book by its cover.<br /> <br /> Where is the preview? Is there a link?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T00:17:37-08:00","id":1475883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1475882#post1475882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw the art preview before and this cover is very disappointing in comparison. Sadly, people *do* judge a book by its cover.<br /> <br /> Where is the preview? Is there a link?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its on the World of Darkness site, but you need an account to see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T03:07:06-08:00","id":1475888,"title":"","content":"I usually try to be constructive but that cover.....<br /> <br /> It looks like the billboard ad for a mediocre 'gritty' (depressing) bbc drama no one will remember in a year of it wrapping up......who Greenlit that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 03-06-2022, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T03:21:54-08:00","id":1475890,"title":"","content":"It's here, BTW: <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/hunter-the-reckoning-5th-edition-preview\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news...dition-preview</a><br /> <br /> As mentioned above, an account is needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T08:58:22-08:00","id":1475900,"title":"","content":"Not going to make an account just to look the preview, until the cover is publicly released I'll remain free of awfulness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T10:04:20-08:00","id":1475908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1475864#post1475864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One one hand, I never really understand putting promo material behind an account. Like... you want people to see promo material to get them into your site... you don't lock it behind making an account just to see what your free previews are.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it means I'm not looking it over yet and getting annoyed at it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1475900#post1475900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not going to make an account just to look the preview, until the cover is publicly released I'll remain free of awfulness.</div> </div> </div> </div>TBF, it's not like you have to pay anything to start up an account. It's a minor annoyance in the grand scheme of things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T10:34:16-08:00","id":1475914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1475908#post1475908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TBF, it's not like you have to pay anything to start up an account. It's a minor annoyance in the grand scheme of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>An annoyance I'm not willing to go through for an even minor benefit. It doesn't really matters if it costs something or not beyond time and patience when even that seems too much for little payoff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T13:44:15-08:00","id":1475932,"title":"","content":"It's a minor annoyance with not pay off for me. I'm sure, within a week, someone will host it somewhere else without the need for an account. That might be piracy, but it would be piracy of a free document that's meant to be an advertisement for an upcoming for-profit item. That says a lot of things about Paradox, and about Internet IP piracy, none of which is really &quot;good.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm a customer. Their job is to convince me to buy their products. That's already a very high bar I'm not sure they could reach if they wanted to for me personally, but there's plenty of people between &quot;I buy everything WoD 5 sight unseen&quot; and &quot;I don't buy anything WoD 5 period.&quot; Adding annoyances just annoys potential customers, and encourages and more insular fandom of those &quot;in&quot; that get all the free stuff right away, and those &quot;out&quot; that have to wait for, again a free promo pdf, to get to them in some form.<br /> <br /> This is advertising 101 level shit. You make sure promo material is accessible as possible first, so people make accounts for more stuff (like buying directly from your online store instead of other places so you get a bigger cut of the sales) once you hook them in. You don't gate promos behind annoyances, or people will skip it for something else/wait for when they don't need to do that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T18:33:37-08:00","id":1475957,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I did sign up for an account for a previous giveaway/promo (I forgot what it was) and then I got so many emails for merch and such that I had to mark their stuff as spam and unsubscribed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T18:47:42-08:00","id":1475959,"title":"","content":"Even if that wasn't the case for Paradox's accounts... it's true enough on the Internet people don't like to sign up to get something free because they think there's going to be a catch; like the above mention spam.<br /> <br /> I know people that get annoyed at Onyx Path for the sheer amount of tweets/emails/etc. that happen just through the way their Kickstarter notifications are setup.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T00:12:40-08:00","id":1475970,"title":"","content":"I don't mind OPP emails because they're all about RPGs, and usually the ones I want to play. The Renegade ones are a bit more annoying because they're about so much more. And I'm really not interested in Power Rangers.<br /> <br /> You could probably sign up, get the PDF and then delete your account or change your contact settings.<br /> <br /> That said, it does seem odd to gate the promo behind a login. Bonus material, maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T00:13:54-08:00","id":1475971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1475932#post1475932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a minor annoyance with not pay off for me. I'm sure, within a week, someone will host it somewhere else without the need for an account. That might be piracy, but it would be piracy of a free document that's meant to be an advertisement for an upcoming for-profit item. That says a lot of things about Paradox, and about Internet IP piracy, none of which is really &quot;good.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm a customer. Their job is to convince me to buy their products. That's already a very high bar I'm not sure they could reach if they wanted to for me personally, but there's plenty of people between &quot;I buy everything WoD 5 sight unseen&quot; and &quot;I don't buy anything WoD 5 period.&quot; Adding annoyances just annoys potential customers, and encourages and more insular fandom of those &quot;in&quot; that get all the free stuff right away, and those &quot;out&quot; that have to wait for, again a free promo pdf, to get to them in some form.<br /> <br /> This is advertising 101 level shit. You make sure promo material is accessible as possible first, so people make accounts for more stuff (like buying directly from your online store instead of other places so you get a bigger cut of the sales) once you hook them in. You don't gate promos behind annoyances, or people will skip it for something else/wait for when they don't need to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's specially stupid here is doing that with the freaking <i>cover</i>.<br /> <br /> It is the quintessential promo/public material about your book, showing it around isn't even considered piracy because it is meant to be known and seen. Giving away the cover and then putting the subscription wall between it and the preview content would make more sense by orders of magnitude even if it was still a bad decision.<br /> <br /> No, I'm not interested in subscribing and the offer doesn't interest me nearly enough. Talking shit about it on a forum is actually more fun than going after it when I can just wait to see it for free <b>if I still even remember the matter</b> when it comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T02:21:34-08:00","id":1475978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1475971#post1475971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's specially stupid here is doing that with the freaking <i>cover</i>.<br /> <br /> It is the quintessential promo/public material about your book, showing it around isn't even considered piracy because it is meant to be known and seen. Giving away the cover and then putting the subscription wall between it and the preview content would make more sense by orders of magnitude even if it was still a bad decision.<br /> <br /> No, I'm not interested in subscribing and the offer doesn't interest me nearly enough. Talking shit about it on a forum is actually more fun than going after it when I can just wait to see it for free <b>if I still even remember the matter</b> when it comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not missing much on the cover front (ETA: pun unintentional). Someone said it looks like a 90s album cover, and I agree. It could be The Cranberries or The Cardigans!<br /> <br /> They should take one of the pieces of art from inside and just slap it on the cover instead. It would take someone half an hour to do and job's a good'un. The other art we've seen so far looks really good, and is better and more consistent than the V5 core rulebook. <br /> <br /> I'm not quite sure why there's such a mismatch between the cover and interior art. The latter is really evocative and would do more to sell the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 03-07-2022, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T22:07:04-08:00","id":1476028,"title":"","content":"OK, I watched a YouTube review of the preview... is it really only like 10 pages (intro, the Inquisitive, the sample Beast Whisper Edge, and La Celestina)?<br /> <br /> I also really hope for the sake of fans that they listen to everyone decrying that cover art and fix it soon because... yeesh.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-07T23:23:38-08:00","id":1476029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1475932#post1475932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a minor annoyance with not pay off for me. I'm sure, within a week, someone will host it somewhere else without the need for an account. That might be piracy, but it would be piracy of a free document that's meant to be an advertisement for an upcoming for-profit item. That says a lot of things about Paradox, and about Internet IP piracy, none of which is really &amp;quot;good.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I'm a customer. Their job is to convince me to buy their products. That's already a very high bar I'm not sure they could reach if they wanted to for me personally, but there's plenty of people between &amp;quot;I buy everything WoD 5 sight unseen&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;I don't buy anything WoD 5 period.&amp;quot; Adding annoyances just annoys potential customers, and encourages and more insular fandom of those &amp;quot;in&amp;quot; that get all the free stuff right away, and those &amp;quot;out&amp;quot; that have to wait for, again a free promo pdf, to get to them in some form.<br /> <br /> This is advertising 101 level shit. You make sure promo material is accessible as possible first, so people make accounts for more stuff (like buying directly from your online store instead of other places so you get a bigger cut of the sales) once you hook them in. You don't gate promos behind annoyances, or people will skip it for something else/wait for when they don't need to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair, giving free content in exchange for an email is exactly advertising 101: it's the easiest and most basic form of Lead Generation. <br /> <br /> BTW, WOD-as-a-company evidently doesn't make much use of remarketing and retargeting tools, and doesn't spam promotionspromotions. I think their direct marketing behaviour is very respectful of their customers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T02:43:28-08:00","id":1476035,"title":"","content":"As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5291\" data-vbnamecard=\"5291\">adambeyoncelowe</a> pointed out, you use bonus content for that, not promotional content meant to get people interested in your product in the first place. If signing up got people a free Loresheet or monster write-up for Hunter that's only going to be given away via a Paradox account? That's how you get people to give away an email address.<br /> <br /> There's no appeal to:<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, we've got a new game.&quot;<br /> &quot;What's it about?&quot;<br /> &quot;Create an account and find out!&quot;<br /> <br /> There's no way you don't lose more people because it twinges their Internet red flags than you'd get by tempting people by putting an advertisement behind an account sign up.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, we've got a new game, check out this preview pdf!&quot;<br /> &quot;That's neat.&quot;<br /> &quot;Cool, if you sign up for an account, you'll get updates and a free monster write-up exclusive to people with accounts.&quot;<br /> <br /> That? That's going to get more people to make accounts than didn't, and if used well should generate more than enough sales to cover the costs of a two-page monster write-up and a 1/8 page art piece a few times over.<br /> <br /> La Celestina looked interesting enough, that I'd consider converting her to HtR 1e or HtV. If there's a freebie monster I could get with just an email? If people said it was as cool as La Celestina I could see myself making an account to get it legit instead of waiting to pause a YouTube video to read the text as it flashes by because the reviewer was showing off the art. I might never play H5, but a good bestiary that has lots of neat antagonists is something that would actually have value to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T06:13:18-08:00","id":1476043,"title":"","content":"Internet red flags are serious stuff. It doesn't matter how they actually use your e-mail after sign-up, it matters my personal history with this to inform my decision <b>before </b>I can even know how they actually behave. I'm not going to sign up to see it for myself and decide if I should sign up.<br /> <br /> And again, there's the mere inconvenience attached to it. It doesn't matter how minor it is, it is there and I'll judge if it seems worth it. Put the way they did it simply doesn't. The very material that could convince me otherwise is hidden, so it isn't convincing me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T11:45:35-08:00","id":1476056,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/blob:https://web.whatsapp.com/aaedfa8c-f409-4f01-8f88-3c1e815ac754\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> they changed it<br /> <br /> I don't likee bullying devs into changing their project. But I gotta say it is much better","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T13:59:06-08:00","id":1476062,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://twitter.com/worldofdarkness/status/1501279189432942595\" target=\"_blank\">Link to the new cover</a>, I really like it now.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call it bullying though, people just gave feedback, even if a bit derisive at times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","user":"SetiteFriend","date":".  fixed the order 03-08-2022, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T15:49:55-08:00","id":1476066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1476062#post1476062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://twitter.com/worldofdarkness/status/1501279189432942595\" target=\"_blank\">Link to the new cover</a>, I really like it now.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call it bullying though, people just gave feedback, even if a bit derisive at times.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yes, I agree","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T16:01:59-08:00","id":1476068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1476062#post1476062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://twitter.com/worldofdarkness/status/1501279189432942595\" target=\"_blank\">Link to the new cover</a>, I really like it now.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call it bullying though, people just gave feedback, even if a bit derisive at times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, feedback is feedback. Kind of like the Sonic movie this one (the first trailer was atrocious), but they did wanted to see reactions and they did saw reactions.<br /> <br /> Not personally a fan of the Heavy Gun Badass style, but it sure is good!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T16:18:59-08:00","id":1476069,"title":"","content":"I mean it's certainly better. Its pretty bland but I'm not embarissed looking at it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-08T17:49:19-08:00","id":1476073,"title":"","content":"The new cover at least better informs a gameline that's supposed to be about playing monster hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T04:48:10-07:00","id":1481910,"title":"","content":"Well damn, I got excited to see they were doing new H:tR (I'm behind on the news, y'see).<br /> Then reading that the Imbued were being dumped for what's really just a HH update? Well colour me confused. Why even call it Reckoning?<br /> <br /> Then we spot JA's petty little fingers all over it, and everything makes sense (right down to the name, a very deliberate message to fans of H:tR that they're not wanted in this town).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/651-throne","name":"Throne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T05:43:09-07:00","id":1482142,"title":"","content":"I'm umming and ahhhing. I like the visuals. I don't like the generic terminology as much (the Driven sounds more passive than the Imbued), but it's not a deal-breaker. If they explicitly and easily allowed Imbued to be a part of the game, instead of just retconning them, I'd be happy. <br /> <br /> One thing that has weirdly rubbed me the wrong way is the sidebox in the new preview that likens 'the Reckoning' to terms used for modern social justice movements. I think it's because I always find WW lexicons full of frivolous (if fun) language that's deliciously style over substance. But it seems cynical to link 'the Reckoning' to #MeToo or #BLM. It's trivialising and commercialising.<br /> <br /> 'The Reckoning' doesn't need to be an IC term. And it definitely doesn't need to create an equivalence between fantastical vampire killing and civil rights movements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T10:35:40-07:00","id":1482170,"title":"","content":"It's also ironic, because there was something of an undercurrent in HtR1e of the whole thing being somewhat \u201cright-wing militia\u201d in tone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T11:19:14-07:00","id":1482179,"title":"","content":"On one side, the &quot;right-wing militia&quot; feel was taken by the SI. But I too think the social reference is being taken too far.<br /> <br /> The two hunter general &quot;types&quot; are basically becoming a too direct and Manichean allegory with very little of the moral nuance that characterize the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T05:11:34-07:00","id":1483302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1482170#post1482170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also ironic, because there was something of an undercurrent in HtR1e of the whole thing being somewhat \u201cright-wing militia\u201d in tone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was intentional. It was supposed to have the feel of playing one of those paranoid conspiracy theorists, but the conspiracies were real and the paranoia was warranted. It hasn't aged well since now the idea of vampires drinking the blood of children and pretending to be politicians is no longer a some weird fringe theory but becoming more and more centralized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T06:13:26-07:00","id":1483306,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure that the \u201cvampires drinking the blood of children\u201d thing is still very much viewed as \u201cwacko fringe\u201d stuff. But yeah, ideas such as \u201cthe government has been subverted by a shadow government\u201d have gained traction in recent years.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure that that's a valid reason for Hunter the Reckoning to go to the other extreme, though.<br /> <br /> Though it might explain the absence of the Imbued. While The Messengers were not described as angels, the parallels between the Imbuing and the \u201cGod told me she was demon-possessed!\u201d stereotype of the religious right are hard to miss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-07-2022, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T12:29:18-07:00","id":1483325,"title":"","content":"I would argue that the increased traction of formerly &quot;fringe&quot; (they've haven't really been all that fringe for decades) conspiracy theory based thinking is all the more reason for a Reckoning game to lean into those elements of the game. Exploring without glorifying how good people (and &quot;good&quot; people) get sucked into violent extremist movements is as relevant as ever as a topic; and having the fictional barrier between reality and a game has always been a tool the WoD uses to do so for any number of topics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T12:38:32-07:00","id":1483326,"title":"","content":"Werewolf also gets a fair bit of that for angles that involve rooting out and fighting corruption. Seems like crossover is usually not too many posts away from someone comparing Garou to religious extremists and the like for killing characters from someone's favorite non-Werewolf game, much like with H:tR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T18:20:52-07:00","id":1483351,"title":"","content":"I'm a WtA fan, and I call the Garou religious zealots all the time in threads that aren't about crossover at all.<br /> <br /> While we still don't know exactly what W5 is going to look like, there is already something to say about not doing the SI as PCs because WtA already plays with the idea of being an extremist that's part of an ongoing and intergenerational dogmatic institution. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T07:44:51-07:00","id":1483463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483325#post1483325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that the increased traction of formerly &amp;quot;fringe&amp;quot; (they've haven't really been all that fringe for decades) conspiracy theory based thinking is all the more reason for a Reckoning game to lean into those elements of the game. Exploring without glorifying how good people (and &amp;quot;good&amp;quot; people) get sucked into violent extremist movements is as relevant as ever as a topic; and having the fictional barrier between reality and a game has always been a tool the WoD uses to do so for any number of topics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I said something similar on RPG.net. It's way more relevant now, than ever, to explore the impact of online echo chambers, radicalisation, propaganda, dehumanisation and conspiracy theories. I know people who've been swept up by this sort of stuff (don't we all now?).<br /> <br /> And you have the added bonus that while all the pre-HTR games were about 'playing the monster', H5 could've been about 'playing the monster' (when you don't realise you're the monster)'. I love that potential.<br /> <br /> At what point does a supernaturally empowered imbued person become just as bad as the monsters they hunt? HTR1e touched on that, and H5 could've mined this to create plenty of conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T08:01:43-07:00","id":1483464,"title":"","content":"So the book is in, and the responses seem mixed to negative on RPG.net. A lot of people are pointing out that by scrubbing the imbued, it's turned a WoD game (the selling point is usually the depth of the setting and lore) into a very generic game with some hangover legacy ideas that don't fit the idea of entirely mundane hunters.<br /> <br /> There are three loosely supernatural Edges, so it's clear that these are mostly the Xanders of the world, not the Buffys or Willows.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, the Driven have Drive but there isn't an in-game reason why they have this, why it isn't magic or divine intervention, and why no one else gets it. Hunters with the orgs specifically don't get Drive (though there may be some who do, it's clearly shown this is an exception). <br /> <br /> If Drive is entirely mundane, then in theory, a dedicated teacher should also be able to access Drive. If Drive is supposed to be some sort of Fate-style metacurrency, then it should be open to all character types in the WoD, not weirdly gated for independent hunters only.<br /> <br /> There's also more of the iffy 'monsters are the cause of real world ills' without any critical reflection of this. One of the examples I saw was particularly distasteful but I won't go into more details here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T09:45:01-07:00","id":1483474,"title":"","content":"For some unknown reason it seems to have Wolverine as Werewolf antagonist, to the point that the description itself draws paralells to that. Was that really necessary? Also Orpheus are antagonists which was unexpected. It seems tha the Orgs are all meant as antagonists for baseline Hunters and I assume they will get fleshed out in supplements?<br /> <br /> For the curious old factions are SAD, Orpheus, Society of Leopold, Arcanum<br /> <br /> In general, the orgs and the sample monsters seem interesting, these writeups have a very &quot;Night Horrors&quot; feel to them with multiple scenario hooks and how to run and use them in game. There's also a gunmage that hunts Hunters ? :P<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T10:32:44-07:00","id":1483481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483474#post1483474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some unknown reason it seems to have Wolverine as Werewolf antagonist, to the point that the description itself draws paralells to that. Was that really necessary? Also Orpheus are antagonists which was unexpected. It seems tha the Orgs are all meant as antagonists for baseline Hunters and I assume they will get fleshed out in supplements?<br /> <br /> For the curious old factions are SAD, Orpheus, Society of Leopold, Arcanum<br /> <br /> In general, the orgs and the sample monsters seem interesting, these writeups have a very &quot;Night Horrors&quot; feel to them with multiple scenario hooks and how to run and use them in game. There's also a gunmage that hunts Hunters ? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>How black and white does it feel to you? The excerpts I've seen seem to paint things quite clearly as 'we're the virtuous, conspiracy-theorist vigilantes and they're the evil cabal running the world'. <br /> <br /> I'm hoping that's just a side effect of things out of context. Do they unpick this presentation at all?<br /> <br /> What are character options like? A few people have said there aren't too many on RPG.net and that the monster building rules are a bit on the light side?<br /> <br /> Are the Edges any good? I'm gold they tend to be more like Advantages than Numina? Is there any support for playing OG imbued, or do you have to DIY it all yourself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T10:38:16-07:00","id":1483484,"title":"","content":"Going through the book a bit more now. The new Hunters seem very light on powers, to the point that even characters from Vigil seem vastly more tricked out than these folks. Also, they seem to have a Drive which gives them mechanical benefits and narrative hooks to lean into, but cannot seem to agree if it's a good thing or a bad thing. In general, this seems to be the book if you want to play baseline humans, as most of the tricks you can get are pretty barebones and easy not to integrate.<br /> <br /> The hunter organisations mentioned as &quot;Orgs&quot; are distinct from the Hunters as &quot;inferior&quot; due to lacking Drives and being in service to something other than the hunt, and it seems a bit... weird? Why writeup 10 factions of hunters and then say they all suck only you and your ragtag group are worth anything and are doing this right. I thought at first that this was a way to introduce them as patrons and allies, but it seems that any faction that is in the hunting job is compromised and untrustworthy and should be avoided by right minded hunters?<br /> <br /> While I really like the Night Horrors vibe of the monster chapter, it feels like they cut out a lot of preamble and general info about the monsters and the actual mechanics to build your own are rather simplistic and barely adequatw, especially compared to Vigil and NBA.<br /> <br /> Speaking of NBA, the layout and fonts makes me think of it a lot, but it's gone back to two consistant two columns. Actually the book looks like a proper well thought out and laid out RPG book with a pretty consistant art style. It's so much easier on the eyes than V5.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T10:43:01-07:00","id":1483486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483481#post1483481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How black and white does it feel to you? The excerpts I've seen seem to paint things quite clearly as 'we're the virtuous, conspiracy-theorist vigilantes and they're the evil cabal running the world'.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping that's just a side effect of things out of context. Do they unpick this presentation at all?<br /> <br /> What are character options like? A few people have said there aren't too many on RPG.net and that the monster building rules are a bit on the light side?<br /> <br /> Are the Edges any good? I'm gold they tend to be more like Advantages than Numina? Is there any support for playing OG imbued, or do you have to DIY it all yourself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, sorry, I just picked it up and went through it quickly (I'll confess that I really was looking for W5 info more than anything else first, then I just started going back and forth)<br /> <br /> Will look into it more and can get back to you. But as I said in my 2nd post, the presentation of the Orgs is rather adversarial and &quot;these guys are messing with things they shouldn't&quot; and the text seems to advocate them as the inferior hunter, one right minded hunters (PC's) shouldn't associate with.<br /> <br /> Edit: I mean this is the preamble on the Orgs, and it's really not a good vibe.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/5hvfACk.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":".  Edit: Orgs 06-09-2022, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T10:52:45-07:00","id":1483487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483484#post1483484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going through the book a bit more now. The new Hunters seem very light on powers, to the point that even characters from Vigil seem vastly more tricked out than these folks. Also, they seem to have a Drive which gives them mechanical benefits and narrative hooks to lean into, but cannot seem to agree if it's a good thing or a bad thing. In general, this seems to be the book if you want to play baseline humans, as most of the tricks you can get are pretty barebones and easy not to integrate.<br /> <br /> The hunter organisations mentioned as &amp;quot;Orgs&amp;quot; are distinct from the Hunters as &amp;quot;inferior&amp;quot; due to lacking Drives and being in service to something other than the hunt, and it seems a bit... weird? Why writeup 10 factions of hunters and then say they all suck only you and your ragtag group are worth anything and are doing this right. I thought at first that this was a way to introduce them as patrons and allies, but it seems that any faction that is in the hunting job is compromised and untrustworthy and should be avoided by right minded hunters?<br /> <br /> While I really like the Night Horrors vibe of the monster chapter, it feels like they cut out a lot of preamble and general info about the monsters and the actual mechanics to build your own are rather simplistic and barely adequatw, especially compared to Vigil and NBA.<br /> <br /> Speaking of NBA, the layout and fonts makes me think of it a lot, but it's gone back to two consistant two columns. Actually the book looks like a proper well thought out and laid out RPG book with a pretty consistant art style. It's so much easier on the eyes than V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sigh. So it's basically the nWoD/CoD core rulebook for mortals, but without the versatility?<br /> <br /> Alternate pitch: Drive can be the result of magic, faith, aliens, mad science, mutations, genetics, long-lost supernatural heritage. This is your origin. Origin opens up powers, tech and special tricks. You also have a creed, which is how you approach hunting and what role you take in the party.<br /> <br /> In this presentation, the Society of Leopold, the Arcanum, the Second Inquisition, mediums, psychics, hedge mages, the Shih and the imbued could all be played out of the core rulebook.<br /> <br /> Come up with a unified system for all of that, with some neat bolt-ons based on origin, and you'd be onto a winner. Your cell could be comprised of Buffy (imbued), Willow (hedge mage), Giles (Arcanum) and Xander (mere mortal), and you'd have no problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T11:40:18-07:00","id":1483499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483486#post1483486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh, sorry, I just picked it up and went through it quickly (I'll confess that I really was looking for W5 info more than anything else first, then I just started going back and forth)<br /> <br /> Will look into it more and can get back to you. But as I said in my 2nd post, the presentation of the Orgs is rather adversarial and &amp;quot;these guys are messing with things they shouldn't&amp;quot; and the text seems to advocate them as the inferior hunter, one right minded hunters (PC's) shouldn't associate with.<br /> <br /> Edit: I mean this is the preamble on the Orgs, and it's really not a good vibe.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/5hvfACk.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. As I expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T15:21:21-07:00","id":1483523,"title":"","content":"So in other words, H5 is about what I expected, a blander version of HtV with the HtR label pasted onto it. I wish I could say I was surprised but that's what non-OPP 5E material has conditioned me to expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T17:51:16-07:00","id":1483532,"title":"","content":"I wasn't expecting super powers and magic-wielding awesome hunters, I wanted a game as dirty streets as it could, with any superstuff like magic and tech being optional or debatable, and that is what I got and I really liked it. If there was something I would add would be Cell tactics or examples of cells, but other than that the game delivered. <br /> <br /> Hunter feeling like they are different and are better than &quot;the Establishment&quot; and &quot;the Man&quot; is pretty much in-tone with the feel the hunters have, it's a game about having enough and putting your hand on the wheel. Even if that sounds a tad bit overrebellious at times, it doesn't actually sounds far off. Although it is weird how Hunters seem so ancap, I don't think they would have Drives and Edges like that if they weren't like this, they would have the power of orgs, which I think are a nice playstyle too, and not actually too hard to adapt. But an unprobeable supplement would be nicer of course.<br /> <br /> The Monsters traits for me are better than trying to translate to Edges or things like their multitude of powers, besides, they are more a problem by their surroundings and assets rather than their direct reactions. The urban legend and occult danger were well shown in the example monsters, but what I mainly got from all this is that the Monster are the end goal in the middle of a lot of obstacles and shortcuts. Other hunters and monsters, cops, orgs, the cell itself and its own personal problems and dilemmas, all of this should make the game, otherwise it would be pretty straightforward research, investigation, observation and intervention. <br /> <br /> <br /> I really liked the Despair and Danger calibrations, and was hoping for more of it since the Fallen London notoriety counter for the SI, that was expanded in the Second Inquisiton supplement. More games should have these game-wide counters so that choices and consequences always have an easy go-to in game for the ST, which gives concrete chokes and releases in the tension. <br /> <br /> The Storyteller's part is also very robust, giving plenty of advice, molds and teachings on building the story to be played. I actually want to play and not only ST this game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T18:13:52-07:00","id":1483540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483474#post1483474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some unknown reason it seems to have Wolverine as Werewolf antagonist, to the point that the description itself draws paralells to that. Was that really necessary? Also Orpheus are antagonists which was unexpected. It seems tha the Orgs are all meant as antagonists for baseline Hunters and I assume they will get fleshed out in supplements?<br /> <br /> For the curious old factions are SAD, Orpheus, Society of Leopold, Arcanum<br /> <br /> In general, the orgs and the sample monsters seem interesting, these writeups have a very &quot;Night Horrors&quot; feel to them with multiple scenario hooks and how to run and use them in game. There's also a gunmage that hunts Hunters ? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they drop any hints at what tribe Sniktbub is supposed to be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T18:38:59-07:00","id":1483542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483523#post1483523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in other words, H5 is about what I expected, a blander version of HtV with the HtR label pasted onto it. I wish I could say I was surprised but that's what non-OPP 5E material has conditioned me to expect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not by any means.<br /> <br /> HtV is meant to support PCs from Compacts and Conspiracies, its equivalent for the Orgs, and they have all the benefits of street-level Cells plus some (at the cost of loyalty and all that). It has a strong theme of obsession and its dangers, with conflicts with Hunters that become as monstrous as the monsters not being uncommon.<br /> <br /> It reminds me much more of a watered down version of Hunters Hunted, as in that book most &quot;hunter&quot; organizations are dubious, but even then it isn't nearly as black-and-white as that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483532#post1483532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't expecting super powers and magic-wielding awesome hunters, I wanted a game as dirty streets as it could, with any superstuff like magic and tech being optional or debatable, and that is what I got and I really liked it. If there was something I would add would be Cell tactics or examples of cells, but other than that the game delivered.<br /> <br /> Hunter feeling like they are different and are better than &quot;the Establishment&quot; and &quot;the Man&quot; is pretty much in-tone with the feel the hunters have, it's a game about having enough and putting your hand on the wheel. Even if that sounds a tad bit overrebellious at times, it doesn't actually sounds far off. Although it is weird how Hunters seem so ancap, I don't think they would have Drives and Edges like that if they weren't like this, they would have the power of orgs, which I think are a nice playstyle too, and not actually too hard to adapt. But an unprobeable supplement would be nicer of course.<br /> <br /> The Monsters traits for me are better than trying to translate to Edges or things like their multitude of powers, besides, they are more a problem by their surroundings and assets rather than their direct reactions. The urban legend and occult danger were well shown in the example monsters, but what I mainly got from all this is that the Monster are the end goal in the middle of a lot of obstacles and shortcuts. Other hunters and monsters, cops, orgs, the cell itself and its own personal problems and dilemmas, all of this should make the game, otherwise it would be pretty straightforward research, investigation, observation and intervention.<br /> <br /> <br /> I really liked the Despair and Danger calibrations, and was hoping for more of it since the Fallen London notoriety counter for the SI, that was expanded in the Second Inquisiton supplement. More games should have these game-wide counters so that choices and consequences always have an easy go-to in game for the ST, which gives concrete chokes and releases in the tension.<br /> <br /> The Storyteller's part is also very robust, giving plenty of advice, molds and teachings on building the story to be played. I actually want to play and not only ST this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with &quot;superpowers&quot; is two fold. One side has been debated already, it is more about the Imbued and the title than about a good game of Hunters needing it. But the other side is about those Orgs, specially those that come from earlier editions. The Arcanum and the Society of Leopold in particular are all about &quot;superpowers&quot;. They're defined by it. What makes the SoL dangerous isn't just the humongous body of knowledge they have on vampires, but also about their Faith and how they learned to weaponize it against Kindred and other monsters. The Arcanum is all about studying the supernatural and borrowing its powers for the sake of it, being possibly the biggest collection of Ghouls, sorcerers and Numina in general not at the hands of any Splat.<br /> <br /> So, adding to that that making Orgs a mechanically inferior option right away is at least weird, I'd expect that any book with those organization would have a fair number of options that represent their trade. It isn't a deal breaker to me, specially because they can get a supplement that addresses that, but it is clearly a flaw.<br /> <br /> For Hunters being better than &quot;The Man&quot;... I don't know if this should be at the forefront. WoD has previously always been about the world being dark regardless of the supernatural, not because of it. They're actually morally nuanced entities that can only have corrupt societies because the world itself is a corrupting place, and most evils in this dark world are completely human evils. That already puts the Hunt under a complicated spotlight because the players know for a fact that not every <b>Monster</b> is, indeed, a monster.<br /> <br /> And on top of that, no trope is more ubiquitous to Hunter stories within and without the World of Darkness than obsession turning a monster hunter into a monster in all but name (and powers, maybe), that you can't commit to such a life without the risk of loosing sight to the simple fact that the ends don't justify the means. And while there are organizations that fall into this category (in WoD the SoL is a prime example), the archetypal hunters-turned-monsters are either cells or loners.<br /> <br /> I still have to read the book by myself, and it seems there are some gems in there. I personally like the street-level style of play for most games, despite disagreeing that the game should be restricted to that even in the core alone just because that's <i>my</i> style. But overall the complaint that the game is too black-and-white seems to hold water, and that's really bad imo, even more when the main Good Guys are basically Conspiracy Theorists putting their hands on guns to actually use them against the institutions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T01:48:47-07:00","id":1483563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483499#post1483499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you. As I expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's worse is how it's even reinforced with other language in the book. There's a part of the book about building relationships with other groups. This is how they write examples <i>&quot;Whether an inspiring member of the creed one looks up to or a particularly duplicitous rival in the branch office of one of the orgs, Hunters aren\u2019t alone in the night. &quot; </i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483540#post1483540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do they drop any hints at what tribe Sniktbub is supposed to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not really. He seems to be a Ronin Ragabash that feels the hunters are out of their depth and is willing to help them while looking cool, aloof and disparaging about their prowess. Also whenever he changes to wolfman form he flips out and murders anyone around him indiscriminatley. He is also of Cheyenne ancestry and seems to be a Ronin because he believed that anyone white on american soil is evil and hate of hieararchy got him tossed him out of werewolf society (nuWendigo? Uktena?).<br /> <br /> <br /> I've been looking more into the book<br /> <br /> The Creeds are very crappy splats with no identity. There is Enterpreneurial, Faithful, Inquisitive, Martial and Underground. They are essentially methodologies you use to hunt and your backstory that use old HtR Creed names as sobriquets. Their only mechanical hook is what situation they get their desperation dice in - i.e. religious creed gets it against the supernatural, militant in combat, investigative in data gathering.<br /> <br /> Now what are the Desperation dice? The game has two public counters - Desperation and Danger. Danger represents how much you have pissed off the authorities and/or your quarry and results in higher difficulties and more opposition. Desperation represents how bad things are going for the hunters. The worse things are for the hunters the more Desperation there is. Now Desperation is ranked from 1-5 and any Hunters (again they insist on the capitalisation as opposed to the ordinary hunters) with a Drive and a Creed can choose to use the desperation dice in any field where their creed specialty applies.<br /> <br /> Desperation dice can never be rerolled, each <b>1</b> causes horrible consequences and/or raises Danger. 10's give a potential critical win, which seems to only be an extra margin of success. I got no idea what &quot;potential&quot; means here, I assume they mean you need double 0's? But why call it out specifically for desperation dice?<br /> <br /> Powers! (Edges)<ul><li>Assets are Arsenal, Fleet, Library, Ordnance</li> <li>Aptitudes are tricks your character has - Beast Whisperer (petmaker), Drone Jockey, Jury Rigging and Global Access (Hack the Planet)</li> <li>Endowments are the actual powers - Sense the unnatural, Thwart the Unnatural (ignore powers) and Repel the Unnatural (use cross to drive of vampires) and Artifact (1 bonus die to certain skill)</li> </ul><br /> In general, the whole section is very sparse. For some reason explosives are separate from &quot;Arsenal&quot; as &quot;Ordnance&quot;. Edges can be customized with perks that improve their effects in certain contexts. All of them require activation rolls and most of them have <b>Difficulty 4</b> to even activate properly. Some of them are downright going to cause issues in the future, I'd like to especially single out Global Access - <i>&quot; ...the Hunter can gain access to any kind of data on any subject or person, in any conceivable system&quot;</i> as something that's gonna be hilarious to interpret once Magic, Spirits and Hypertech exist in this setting. Drone Jockey seems very easy to abuse if you load up on perks and get multiple users (simply due to how action economy works in WoD).<br /> <br /> I still don't get why &quot;Drive&quot; is so special for the Hunters and why it makes them different from other humans beyond marking them as protagonists. For something they spend A LOT of wordcount on to make special, it doesn't really seem so in everything I've seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T05:36:13-07:00","id":1483576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483563#post1483563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's worse is how it's even reinforced with other language in the book. There's a part of the book about building relationships with other groups. This is how they write examples <i>&amp;quot;Whether an inspiring member of the creed one looks up to or a particularly duplicitous rival in the branch office of one of the orgs, Hunters aren\u2019t alone in the night. &amp;quot; </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, not really. He seems to be a Ronin Ragabash that feels the hunters are out of their depth and is willing to help them while looking cool, aloof and disparaging about their prowess. Also whenever he changes to wolfman form he flips out and murders anyone around him indiscriminatley. He is also of Cheyenne ancestry and seems to be a Ronin because he believed that anyone white on american soil is evil and hate of hieararchy got him tossed him out of werewolf society (nuWendigo? Uktena?).<br /> <br /> <br /> I've been looking more into the book<br /> <br /> The Creeds are very crappy splats with no identity. There is Enterpreneurial, Faithful, Inquisitive, Martial and Underground. They are essentially methodologies you use to hunt and your backstory that use old HtR Creed names as sobriquets. Their only mechanical hook is what situation they get their desperation dice in - i.e. religious creed gets it against the supernatural, militant in combat, investigative in data gathering.<br /> <br /> Now what are the Desperation dice? The game has two public counters - Desperation and Danger. Danger represents how much you have pissed off the authorities and/or your quarry and results in higher difficulties and more opposition. Desperation represents how bad things are going for the hunters. The worse things are for the hunters the more Desperation there is. Now Desperation is ranked from 1-5 and any Hunters (again they insist on the capitalisation as opposed to the ordinary hunters) with a Drive and a Creed can choose to use the desperation dice in any field where their creed specialty applies.<br /> <br /> Desperation dice can never be rerolled, each <b>1</b> causes horrible consequences and/or raises Danger. 10's give a potential critical win, which seems to only be an extra margin of success. I got no idea what &amp;quot;potential&amp;quot; means here, I assume they mean you need double 0's? But why call it out specifically for desperation dice?<br /> <br /> Powers! (Edges)<ul><li>Assets are Arsenal, Fleet, Library, Ordnance</li> <li>Aptitudes are tricks your character has - Beast Whisperer (petmaker), Drone Jockey, Jury Rigging and Global Access (Hack the Planet)</li> <li>Endowments are the actual powers - Sense the unnatural, Thwart the Unnatural (ignore powers) and Repel the Unnatural (use cross to drive of vampires) and Artifact (1 bonus die to certain skill)</li> </ul><br /> In general, the whole section is very sparse. For some reason explosives are separate from &amp;quot;Arsenal&amp;quot; as &amp;quot;Ordnance&amp;quot;. Edges can be customized with perks that improve their effects in certain contexts. All of them require activation rolls and most of them have <b>Difficulty 4</b> to even activate properly. Some of them are downright going to cause issues in the future, I'd like to especially single out Global Access - <i>&amp;quot; ...the Hunter can gain access to any kind of data on any subject or person, in any conceivable system&amp;quot;</i> as something that's gonna be hilarious to interpret once Magic, Spirits and Hypertech exist in this setting. Drone Jockey seems very easy to abuse if you load up on perks and get multiple users (simply due to how action economy works in WoD).<br /> <br /> I still don't get why &amp;quot;Drive&amp;quot; is so special for the Hunters and why it makes them different from other humans beyond marking them as protagonists. For something they spend A LOT of wordcount on to make special, it doesn't really seem so in everything I've seen.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds so bland. I am still interested in Desperation and Danger, and how we might use those to fix my problems with Hunger, but the other stuff sounds so generic. And I wish they'd stop making everything Difficulty 4 (i.e., 8 dice needed!). Difficulty 3 is probably too high as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T06:36:18-07:00","id":1483578,"title":"","content":"Doesn't sound bad, really more or less what I was expecting, but I still wish they hadn't called it Hunter the Reckoning or had included Imbued as an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T09:31:14-07:00","id":1483612,"title":"","content":"Just so that it doesn't sound it's all horrible forever, I'd like to share some thoughts on the design. It's Black, Grey and Orange on White, and it looks really striking, most of the art is actually drawn and not photography and its highly evocative, to the point that it feels like a better take on what CoD looks like. It's clear they had a decent layout person for this with their head straight on, and the book looks really nice, I think that on paper it might really be a stunner.<br /> <br /> Also it offers us glories as this absolute madlad who is someone I never knew I wanted to play before, illustration for &quot;Physical Specimen&quot; archetype:<br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/HOkgA46.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Now beyond the visual I have some new thoughts about the core conceit of the game. I'm not sure the authors were on the same page or were actually coordinating on what they were making here. The framework for playing a group of low powered monster hunters driven together by necessity and sticking together through brotherhood is there, and the game should be able to work.<br /> <br /> However, the way that Drive is written and presented is utterly inconsistent and painfully artificial. On one hand it's something that differentiates hunters and Hunters, but is defined as a need and drive of humans to fight the horrors in the night. It's clearly something special, but wherever they can they downplay it. This comes to the fore quite well with the Factions (I am not going to use the term &quot;Orgs&quot; as its dumb) where it insists that the hunters of the factions are neither Hunters, nor Driven. Which for some factions and characters makes sense, but a lot of the archetypes those factions represent are about people willing to do whatever needs to be done to deal with the dark. Quite a few of their front line people and probably even the leadership has to have true believers to survive and keep things going in the World of Darkness. Yet they are not Driven, they never become Driven and they are not true Hunters.<br /> <br /> Add to this the fact that the game itself cannot really decide what this Drive is, one one hand it's presented as getting things done that need doing while fighting monsters, on the other it fully supports characters that just want to study monsters or even become monsters! It's not helped by the fact that there is 2.5 pages of text about drives, and none of it actually explains what they are beyond a shorthand for &quot;These are the protagonists&quot;. Worse yet, it actively tells us that Drive and Creed are NOT in game terms, they are distinctly out of game terms to help us out, but nowhere does it actually bother to tell us as the ST's and the players what they are and couches the terms in fluffy language and presents them as is.<br /> <br /> Worse yet, it implies that Drives are permanent, and that once your eyes are open there is no going back, yet it doesn't address this. Heck, it even rather inconsistently claims that you can finish your Hunt, and by finishing your Hunt you can go back to your life as it was once before. Alas, the game doesn't really care about the idea that you're playing a zealot willing to do anything to hunt down the monsters, you do get touchstones, but there is no impact of your Drive on your interpersonal relationships beyond what your ST devises for you.<br /> <br /> You can temporarily lose your Drive, when you roll despair on your dice. So what happens then? Nothing. You lose your special dice until you perform an act of atonement, and honestly practically all of these acts of atonement are things that your character would do anyway if they had that drive! They don't even insist you need to act irrationally towards that goal. No you just need to do something that's pretty much in character for your Drive. The book example itself for Curiosity is &quot;Get New Information&quot;.<br /> <br /> It even goes so far to say that people who pick up arms to fight the supernatural for a moment (the average horror movie protagonist) are not Driven and never will be as long as they didn't turn into a full time monster hunter as a consequence of that encounter. If Drive is something everyone can have, would it not make more sense that it can come and go as narrative demands it?<br /> <br /> In essence, I love the idea of Desperation Dice for these character, but I hate the whole way the Drives are set up around it. I honestly cannot believe that 20 people are listed as authors, editors and consultants and not a single one of them noticed how disjointed this whole concept is!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 06-10-2022, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T09:46:06-07:00","id":1483613,"title":"","content":"Ever hear the saying \u201ctoo many cooks spoil the broth\u201d? I have no problem believing that a book with 20 authors, editors, and consultants feels disjointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T09:58:44-07:00","id":1483614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483613#post1483613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ever hear the saying \u201ctoo many cooks spoil the broth\u201d? I have no problem believing that a book with 20 authors, editors, and consultants feels disjointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did I even think. I was just getting frustrated by the end of my critique that noone actually read this as a whole and noticed it was a mess.<br /> But you're probably right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T13:12:18-07:00","id":1483641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483612#post1483612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also it offers us glories as this absolute madlad who is someone I never knew I wanted to play before, illustration for &quot;Physical Specimen&quot; archetype:</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any additional context given for the character illustrated there... or is he just standing there with no explanation of who he his and how he got to be that way?<br /> <br /> Like, I understand why people that don't know the meaning behind most of what he's wearing is can just enjoy the cool feel of the character but to me he's visual gibberish. That could actually be good if he's a character with a story that tells us how he became...that... or really bad if it's gibberish because the artist doesn't know why that's the case.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T13:42:27-07:00","id":1483649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483641#post1483641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there any additional context given for the character illustrated there... or is he just standing there with no explanation of who he his and how he got to be that way?<br /> <br /> Like, I understand why people that don't know the meaning behind most of what he's wearing is can just enjoy the cool feel of the character but to me he's visual gibberish. That could actually be good if he's a character with a story that tells us how he became...that... or really bad if it's gibberish because the artist doesn't know why that's the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ouch. Now you're making me feel bad for liking the idea of a asskicking Rabbi and not knowing enough how it should be portrayed.. I'd love to hear more about the errors so I can learn something useful for the future. There is zero context to the character. Each Creed has a couple of sample character types, and this is most likely the splat illustration for the &quot;Physical Specimen&quot; subtype. I thought just the name was silly but the idea was cool. Really sorry to hear it's that bad.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T14:46:38-07:00","id":1483651,"title":"","content":"OK, so, part of this is that he's not a rabbi, because he's saying that with his clothing.<br /> <br /> Ultra-orthodox Jews have a very strict dress code, but like all people, there's a desire to dress in a fashion the help express things about themselves. As such, very small details have huge meanings; making them very hard to understand to outsides but bright as day to people that &quot;speak&quot; the coded messages.<br /> <br /> So, to break down what the man in that picture is saying with how he dresses (to get this out ahead of time, he's coded as an Ashkenazic Jew, some of these things have entirely different meanings for ultra-orthodox Jews of other traditions) :<br /> <br /> 1) His hat is saying that &quot;God loves Queers and Hates straights,&quot; and he wants to break into religious services just wearing that hat, carrying a pride flag, and scandalizing everyone with his nudity. The style of hat indicates he has strong reform minded sympathies (the shape of the hat, the length of the brim, and how this relates to the length of his hair are a complicated thing to decode precisely), and he has color on it. Color is a <b>huge</b> no-no here. Ultra-orthodox men are not allow to have any colors besides black or natural (leather/fur) on the external surfaces of their clothing. The lining of the hat could have color, but a band of color around the outside? That is super iconoclastic, rebellious, and so on. The only way that could be worse among that community is if it was red (which would be declaring himself a sex worker). To try to put this in perspective, a band of dark grey cloth that might be black if the lighting was different would result in months of gossip about a man.<br /> <br /> 2) He's wearing a theologian/academic's glasses. This is a statement that he's done at least the equivalent of a university level education in private Jewish schools with the religious training on top of any secular studies he's done (again, there's some implications based on his hair since it denotes a middle-aged man, not a current student), and has made a commitment to on going religious study for life even if that coincides with other things like a job and a family.<br /> <br /> 3) He has a well trimmed but long beard, high quality watch, and a nice vest. This indicates he is neither a practicing rabbi or a laborer. These are signs of someone that's a professional in a business or high-skilled low manual labor area. He is putting in the effort to balance signifying his success, wealth, and secular status, without bragging or boasting. That particular cut of beard is also favored in some groups because it can be tucked into a fully buttoned collar to stand out less when meeting with people of other groups; again indicating a businessman of some sort. A person that does manual labor (even things like cooking or delicate work) would trim to a shorter length so their beard doesn't get in things, and a rabbi would be pressured into a less &quot;stylish&quot; and more natural beard precisely to show he is not concerned with matters where adapting his presentation to be less &quot;Jewish&quot; would be important.<br /> <br /> 4) His talit katan (the fringed undershirt) is a very weird choice. That style is generally one that you'd only wear on the most important days of your life. It's like wearing a high end designer tuxedo to the gym, or even a priceless family heirloom. But it's also ripped, while his chest is exposed (huge no-no there as well), and we can see scars that would have ripped the garment (traditionally a talit katan goes all the way up to at least your collar bone). This is a sign of severe mental trauma and unresolved grief. This looks like he was attacked by a monster on his wedding day or something similar, and instead of seeking help and undergoing the traditional Jewish mourning rituals is still wearing the signs of his trauma out in the open for everyone to see. Despite the fact that the scars are well healed now, he's still wearing a ripped shirt (a sign of mourning). So he's basically begging people to have him committed because he's trying to commit suicide by monster hunting.<br /> <br /> 5) The pants and boots are completely unacceptable dress unless required by active military duty. From the waist down, he's a soldier in the middle of a war, while walking around with a sledgehammer. Given he's not wearing complimentary clothing above his waist, this is a very conflicted message. If he was in a literal war-zone, he'd be wearing other things elsewhere. In the context of Hunter, you can only really see this as a declaration that the world is a warzone and he's looking for a fight. A military background could explain his physicality though.<br /> <br /> So... yeah. That's a lot of stuff that is a really mixed bag.<br /> <br /> However, don't feel bad because I think, esp. if you put some character thought into #4 and #5 there, there could be a superb story here. You could do a lot with how the Drive has caused him to lose touch with his religious community, pushing his Touchstones away with a toxic mix of grief, combat training, and severe psychological damage, and only these little cues to express to people how much trouble he's really in failing because to most people that can read them he looks like a psycho ready to murder anyone that gets close to him.<br /> <br /> It's just... disappointing to hear the book just tossed in &quot;lets make a physical Jew&quot; that checks off a bunch of &quot;token&quot; boxes while trying to be subversive by making him physically intimidating and powerful instead of nebbish; only to fail because they didn't give people the context needed to understand it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T15:38:34-07:00","id":1483653,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Thanks for that. Planning to save that and lookup some of the terms you've used for later reference. I feel you have put way more thought in this, and that the art prompt was much simpler than the details you go into. There's a lot of hooks to go from your recontextualisation, but the 4+5 would make a pretty interesting character.<br /> <br /> Essentially they've used orthodox Jew tropes with zero context? I assume that their Diversity consultancy agency listed in the credits didn't really bother with this. It does make me wonder about some of the other characters...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T15:50:49-07:00","id":1483654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483523#post1483523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in other words, H5 is about what I expected, a blander version of HtV with the HtR label pasted onto it. I wish I could say I was surprised but that's what non-OPP 5E material has conditioned me to expect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> H5 is kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T16:33:58-07:00","id":1483658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483653#post1483653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad to help, and I hope you future research results in some fun characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel you have put way more thought in this, and that the art prompt was much simpler than the details you go into. </div> </div> </div>It's kind of a lot of thought and kinda of not? While I didn't grow up in an orthodox community, I grew up in a diverse enough Jewish community that I regularly interacted with orthodox Jews of different groups and the thinking becomes background stuff. I've internalized a lot of these rules because it was just part of growing up in the community I did. The artwork in question mostly hit me because it's jarring (again, that can be good, jarring can say a lot that is good for the art).<br /> <br /> I'm conflicted a bit in how far I want to assume about the art prompt here. More specifically, I feel like I should reserve my frustrations with the writing not doing anything to compliment the art, because I struggle with the idea that an artist accidentally managed to include so many of those details. Without other evidence, I'd prefer to assume the artist got a prompt, and did some research, and actually made a picture that was trying to tell a real story (maybe not the exact one I walked away with, but at least something similar). As I hope I'm not overstating, I really see a lot of potential in that piece if people know what it means, so it's hard for me to think it wasn't purposeful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Essentially they've used orthodox Jew tropes with zero context? I assume that their Diversity consultancy agency listed in the credits didn't really bother with this. It does make me wonder about some of the other characters... </div> </div> </div>It does seem to be the case that they didn't contextualize this image. I don't have the pdf so I can't really comment on anything more than what others are posting. <br /> <br /> Like, it's not offensive to me even if disappointing, and most diversity consultants are trying to weed out offensive and problematic stuff before they get to focus down on these kinds of details (plus realistically speaking people that &quot;speak&quot; ultra-orthodox Jewish dress coding in detail is a very small number of people compared to a lot of other groups for a diversity consulted to know about).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T17:25:22-07:00","id":1483663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483658#post1483658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm conflicted a bit in how far I want to assume about the art prompt here. More specifically, I feel like I should reserve my frustrations with the writing not doing anything to compliment the art, because I struggle with the idea that an artist accidentally managed to include so many of those details. Without other evidence, I'd prefer to assume the artist got a prompt, and did some research, and actually made a picture that was trying to tell a real story (maybe not the exact one I walked away with, but at least something similar). As I hope I'm not overstating, I really see a lot of potential in that piece if people know what it means, so it's hard for me to think it wasn't purposeful.<br /> <br /> It does seem to be the case that they didn't contextualize this image. I don't have the pdf so I can't really comment on anything more than what others are posting.</div> </div> </div> </div>So each Creed consists of a 4 page writeup, including Personality, Tactics, Dangers and Suggested Traits. It finishes off with Archetypes, which are quick character concepts maybe a paragraph long to show off typical characters of a creed. There is one splat illustration per Creed, and one full page photo manipulated piece. The illustration we're discussing seems to refer to the &quot;Physical Specimen&quot; Archetype for the Faithful. The other Archetypes are Apostate (I drink blood to do God's good work of killing vampires), Death's Brink Convert (I was dead were it not for my Faith) and Absolver (I will give you absolution for your sins before I kill you). In general, the art is left out of context. There are some characters that do appear multiple times in the art, but they are related to two short adventures for the Hunters (kinda like the Mari and Albrecht comic).<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/J4Iz1Er.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T18:07:09-07:00","id":1483666,"title":"","content":"I see.<br /> <br /> I remain a bit conflict on the prompt here. I know Jews that have moved from more metropolitan areas to live in isolated ultra-orthodox communities rather than try to manage their faith and secular life when the rest of the world doesn't feel like your faith matters much. Even as someone that wasn't raised and hasn't embrace orthodoxy, I miss living in a community where the idea of Friday night being a spiritual time where people wouldn't expect you to be available if you wanted to start Shabbat in a way that resonated for you, and there were enough Jews of various persuasions that major Jewish holidays were days employers treated as normal days to see a lot of people taking off. I've had to make personal compromises to my circumstances around things like that. So that description of, &quot;devoted themselves to a remote religious community in hopes of finding personal balance,&quot; resonates with me both as a personal matter and something I've seen happen.<br /> <br /> In the WoD, the idea that those communities are easily subverted by the supernatural is also easy for me to buy. Pre-V5 there was a whole minor Mage Craft that worked to claim isolated Jewish communities as their own turf. <br /> <br /> I'm still left with the feeling that all the pieces of a good use of an unexpected cultural example are there, but it just needs a little push to build up some context that links that general write-up to the very specific image there. I can envision how this character came about in an authentic way... but it's something I know way more about than most people do. It just feels like it needed to follow up that passage about the &quot;general&quot; and then give a more specific example that linked to the image to have worked better. And really, it seems better in genera to mix general write-ups with a few example executions, not just this one passage and image combo.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-10T20:56:53-07:00","id":1483685,"title":"","content":"I do think in the end the combination of the text and the image, with the adequate context for it you provided, does prompt very interesting and powerful stories. He struggled and went to an Orthodox community to find balance, he faced trauma and now is on the Hunt.<br /> <br /> But adding the cues with the text we also know he's still a theologian, not just a madman. He broke with orthodoxy, but is still a thinker whose physical preparedness is an extension of his theological views and practices. More than that, I get from it that however strange the coding of his clothes can be, they're thoroughly deliberate. He wants to say what he says, it is an intentional message.<br /> <br /> Elaborating in the details and the whys seems a lot of fun. And I do agree that no matter how little context the text gave, the artist most likely knew what they were doing, at least to a reasonable extent. It is just too much of a coincidence (otherwise the code would just be gibberish of the kind that makes it too obvious they didn't know anything about what they were doing).<br /> <br /> EDIT: I always find it curious that you can't formalize a request to have your religion's holidays in the US. Around here it is law, while many holidays here are Catholic, by formalizing a request you're entitled to have your religion's rules recognized and followed through, with distinct paid leaves or shifts if needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 06-11-2022, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T00:41:06-07:00","id":1483699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483685#post1483685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But adding the cues with the text we also know he's still a theologian, not just a madman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Asmodai called him a madlad, not a madman, which is a slang term for someone that tends to do physically dangerous things out of excitement or humor; though usually associated with men acting immature rather than &quot;normal&quot; youthful roughhousing.<br /> <br /> Which, at least IME, is actually fairly common in the ultra-orthodox Jewish communities. For young men, they have grown up in a highly regimented culture, were physical activity is one of the few outlets of both personal independence and pent up emotional stress. One of my school friends probably had ADHD (wasn't diagnosed), and soccer was pretty much how he coped to get out daily emotional issues. Looking back on it as an adult, it's kinda of painful to know we didn't really recognize those pleas to get one more point in before lunch was over - even though we clearly didn't have time for more - was because he needed it to help with a day that was just going shitty.<br /> <br /> There's a very &quot;boys will be boys&quot; attitude, and that they'll grow out of it, but plenty take way too long to (if they ever completely do), so nobody really thinks much about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He wants to say what he says, it is an intentional message. </div> </div> </div>And an interesting mix of conscious messaging and subconscious implications. A lot of the more overt statements tend to indicate a lot of unexamined deeper set issues that are still being communicated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: I always find it curious that you can't formalize a request to have your religion's holidays in the US. Around here it is law, while many holidays here are Catholic, by formalizing a request you're entitled to have your religion's rules recognized and followed through, with distinct paid leaves or shifts if needed. </div> </div> </div>The simple answer is... the whole &quot;50 states&quot; thing. Each state has it's own rules, and the federal government has rules where the state rules don't apply. Even within the same state, things depend where you live. I went to high school and university in the same state where I live now... but in two places that couldn't be more different in how these issues get treated. <br /> <br /> And while I acknowledge there is a risk of getting trapped in this mode of thinking and never standing up for smaller reforms, there are so many bigger issues to solve than making sure I get 3-5 more vacation days a year than I do because I'm spending them on religious days where my Christian coworkers don't have to do that. I can't bring myself to fight for a few days of paid holiday leave when my country doesn't guarantee paid parental leave for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-11T11:06:15-07:00","id":1483729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483699#post1483699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asmodai called him a madlad, not a madman</div> </div> </div> </div>I used madman to mean that he may <i>seem</i> as completely taken by emotion and trauma and, as you said, &quot;he looks like a psycho ready to murder anyone that gets close to him&quot;, but in reality he's far more in control and sending this message on purpose.<br /> <br /> But I didn't knew what exactly was a madlad and that really helps a lot, although this isn't so much how he reads to me now. It could have been in his past, though. And I agree that there's a lot of subconscious messaging there, but I personally felt that it is fitting to imagine it had a lot of deliberation on the decisions, which doesn't take out the subconscious part, but re-contextualize it a lot.<br /> <br /> For the paid leave thing... yeah, I get your point. I wouldn't completely agree because I tend to dislike this argument of more pressing matters for the reason you acknowledged already, plus it frequently being used to invalidate issues in the first place. But it is certainly true that there are easier and more pressing fights. It was just something that took me by surprise a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T15:38:52-07:00","id":1483819,"title":"","content":"Why is there so much stuff about the Philippines in the new Hunter book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T16:35:52-07:00","id":1483822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483819#post1483819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is there so much stuff about the Philippines in the new Hunter book?</div> </div> </div> </div>one of the writers was from there,i liked it quite a bit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T16:43:12-07:00","id":1483824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483819#post1483819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is there so much stuff about the Philippines in the new Hunter book?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have all kinds of funky monsters and an authoritarian leaning regime that can be fought as well as the monsters of the night. Sounds like a good match while giving something to other parts of the world. That's something WoD had always been lacking, and I'm glad they gave it to a local writer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T20:52:57-07:00","id":1483844,"title":"","content":"While I doubt it had that much sway on things, there was also a brief splash by the Trese animated adaptation on Netflix last year that helped show off some of the unexplored aspects of Filipino culture that works really well for urban fantasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T07:52:25-07:00","id":1483869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483824#post1483824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They have all kinds of funky monsters and an authoritarian leaning regime that can be fought as well as the monsters of the night. Sounds like a good match while giving something to other parts of the world. That's something WoD had always been lacking, and I'm glad they gave it to a local writer.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense. Very cool. I learned more about Filipinx culture from reading H:tR than I ever learned in high school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T09:33:16-07:00","id":1483993,"title":"","content":"It looks like I'm in the minority here, but I actually like it. I'm okay with removing the imbued from the equation, though I suspect that later supplements will probably either add options, or at least explain what happened. This feels more like your average, on the street Hunters who are tired of being prey to the supernatural.<br /> <br /> The Desperation mechanic can potentially be pretty strong, even making Hunters equivalent to your average Vampire in that they can potentially have fairly large dice pools as long as what they are doing ties in to their Drive.<br /> <br /> I do have some complaints; the Edges, Aptitudes, and Endowments seems a little bare...I think there should be more options. Out of the box, you are a little limited with customizability. I was really hoping they would expand on the combat system; in the act of trying to simplify combat for Vampire 5E, I think they made the system a little too simple. The lore was minimal; I think it would have benefited to add a little more about what has been happening in the past 20 years.<br /> <br /> But those are minor quibbles. Overall, I like what they've done. I enjoy the section on Storyteller tips and how to build the episodic stories in the vein of the Supernatural series. The artwork wasn't too terrible, and it wasn't unnecessary (I'm looking at you, Vampire 5e with your 15 pages of fashion pictures).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","name":"Raunalyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T10:04:23-07:00","id":1484002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raunalyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483993#post1483993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The artwork wasn't too terrible, and it wasn't unnecessary (I'm looking at you, Vampire 5e with your 15 pages of fashion pictures).</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not so much of a minority in the sense that the art is really getting a lot of positive comments, I want to see more of it (exchange rates will keep me from buying this book for a long time or forever).<br /> <br /> But there's no need to say it is better than V5 core. I don't think we'll have something that awful anytime soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T11:56:52-07:00","id":1484017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484002#post1484002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there's no need to say it is better than V5 core. I don't think we'll have something that awful anytime soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of it in the core book was amazing...there was just SO MUCH of it. They could have easily cut 50% of the artwork, or reduce it to half/quarter pages and added lore.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","name":"Raunalyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-14T12:26:10-07:00","id":1484026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raunalyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484017#post1484017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of it in the core book was amazing...there was just SO MUCH of it. They could have easily cut 50% of the artwork, or reduce it to half/quarter pages and added lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't classify any of it as amazing, at least in context. Some were good pieces of art, but in the wrong place imo. And not because of being photo-shoots, either, although in the end most people think it was it and most books started to avoid photo-shoots.<br /> <br /> And I definitely agree that they went too far with the number of art pieces. Maybe it was intentional precisely because they didn't had enough text to make for the desired number of pages, maybe it was just them thinking more art would make the book look better. At the end of the day the art contributed a lot to the negative views of the book and nothing to help with the theme and mood of Masquerade even V5-style. It just seemed as mostly a Goth-themed fashion-week magazine and a little as any other magazine, really. They're either too &quot;good-looking&quot;, too obviously taking poses, or just look like stock images.<br /> <br /> But then again, it is hard to miss the spot so hard. And understandable why they thought it would be a good idea (out of context most of them are, indeed, good-looking). I just think it became too low of a bar, and as I said, it seems that Hunter's art is <u><b>really</b></u> good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T03:37:48-07:00","id":1484345,"title":"","content":"So let's start with some art before I continue talking about Hunter the Reckoning and specifically the Antagonists section.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/w2zqwNy.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/ru1jGtR.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/rs4DoJg.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/QPQr5xM.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So yes, the art in this really feels striking and more like WoD than anything in the V5 books.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T05:36:54-07:00","id":1484349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484345#post1484345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So let's start with some art before I continue talking about Hunter the Reckoning and specifically the Antagonists section.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/w2zqwNy.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/ru1jGtR.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/rs4DoJg.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/QPQr5xM.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So yes, the art in this really feels striking and more like WoD than anything in the V5 books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The art also feels like HTR1e toned down to a more realistic level. It's still action movie level, but it's not Arnold Schwarzenegger action movie level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T07:11:22-07:00","id":1484352,"title":"","content":"So the Antagonist section. Oh Boy. I have some deeply conflicted emotions about it, because the authors (again) didn't think it through. The format is essentially Night Horrors with an in character section telling tall tales, followed by stats, goals and objectives, how to use it in stories, encounters and additional complications. And honestly, I like most of them, and all of them are good enough to just lift up from the book and use in any game for a session and some for even whole campaigns!<br /> <br /> However, there are some caveats.<ul><li>Each of the core antagonists is described in a single paragraph that's completely useless and generally countermanded by a description of the individual monsters (i.e. hunters don't encounter anything but lone werewolves, yet are shown in the art and in a writeup of another antagonist as fighting and hunting packs)</li> <li>the critters presented are quite a far stretch from your usual WoD fare, I honestly prefer that, I like the weird and quirky and the fact that I could drop them into any chronicle, but it's rather offbrand for the whole &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; spiel</li> <li>there is very little context given - they like to use words like &quot;The Establishment Vampires&quot;, &quot;The Blood Cult Vampires&quot;, werewolf packs, powerful ancestor ghosts, a dissolved ghostly bureaucracy and technomagic yet nothing in the text or anywhere else explains this. This ends up quite disjointed when comboed with the prior two points</li> <li>the tools for make your own critter are very simplistic, just a few generic powers mostly mapping to prominent vampiric discipline powers with a dicepool of X resisted by Y, a more robust system would have been nice but this is functional.</li> <li>All the in character stories are presented by either people in other hunter cells, orgs or even confessions of victims, and they consistantly present a much more cosmopolitan, interconnected and communicating world of Hunters, that the book and its storytelling section don't! It talks a lot about how rare the Hunters are, how special the PC's are for banding together and gives no context for this larger society that shares stories and tales. I'd love to know more about it as it would make a more interesting setting, but it would imply that groups banding together is good, and remember Orgs are BAD!</li> <li>Occasionally they speak of redemption and helping people out, but it's clearly presented as a throwaway because all presented characters it mentions are seen as actually backfiring on the PC's</li> <li>There is little special and magical about the Mages, they just get very very high dicepools for things they are good at. It's like Revised on steroids</li> <li>There are two settings quite clearly detailed here - North Mexico/American South + Phillipines, but neither has any further information or context outside the geographical ties for the critters</li> <li>out of 15 presented threats I feel that it's a very unfortunate implication that 10 of them are strictly coded as People of Color specifically in text and the rest are simply unspecified.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Vampires:</b><ul><li>a fire breathing, fire commanding Mexican human trafficker with a whole organisation, looking to make more of himself and to fuck over the Camarilla</li> <li>a constructed being made by a serial killer (explicitly said not to be a vampire) that hunts people in a small Mexican town</li> <li>A well connected Filipino secret society of cannibals led by an inner circle of Vampires that seeks to feed on the flesh of the &quot;God Children&quot; and has pet Hunters</li> </ul><br /> <b>Werewolves</b><ul><li>crazed old lupus driven from his hunting grounds and playing the Leatherface role</li> <li>sarcastic trickster loner that looks like and acts like wolverine and who is so much better than the Hunters at hunting</li> </ul><br /> <b>Mages</b><ul><li>a gun nut hunter of Hunters who has a bag of endless guns and wants to teach the Hunters a lesson for being xenophobic assholes</li> <li>a guy with high arcane that keeps houses in which he gently manipulates tenants to kill their loved ones to serve his dark masters</li> <li>a magic van owned by a group of Coyotes whose back opens into a strange dimension that carries people elsewhere and who might get eaten or changed by things in the strange dimension</li> </ul><br /> <b>Ghosts</b><ul><li>A haunted outhouse where a kid who died in the pit below kills people who enter it by drowning them in shit (yes, sigh)</li> <li>A serial killer victim Filipino girl who takes rides with stranger and eats their health and willpower</li> <li>a haunted mall built on the mass graves of Filipino victims of Japanese atrocities now eats people and enslaves their souls</li> <li>a slaver captain who torched his human cargo and now hunts anyone tied to the descendants of companies and cities of the slave traders</li> </ul><br /> <b>Fair Folk and Strange Things</b><ul><li>a fair folk that keeps falling in love and then painting his targets into paintings for his gallery replacing them with fetches</li> <li>a monstrous thing in a coat that collects eyes from its victims and adds them to its body</li> <li>a pair of books - one that makes anyone who reads it obsessed with learning more about monsters through vivisection and obsessive collecting until they move on to humans and themselves and another that cures you as long as you remove a body part</li> </ul><br /> So yes, all in all there's interesting stuff here that's well presented and useful to start running immediately. However, as a whole it doesn't seem to be sure what it wants to be. I for one will definitely treat this as inspiration, but would advise against anyone reading anything into the other WoD games going from what is presented here..<br /> <br /> <br /> Off to run a game, but planning to read the Orgs next <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T10:08:45-07:00","id":1484370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484349#post1484349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The art also feels like HTR1e toned down to a more realistic level. It's still action movie level, but it's not Arnold Schwarzenegger action movie level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overall I like the style and quality more than most WoD art before V20. With a few exceptions, WoD books tended to have a few gems and a lot of crap. In-theme and on the right mood crap, but still crap. V5 core had very well done pieces that got the theme completely wrong and ruined the mood, which is unarguably worse, but still had more quality than most classic WoD.<br /> <br /> Usually the art only really got better by the middle to end of Revised. Which is to say, overall this here seems really nice and above average for WoD in general, not just V5, it is really good!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484352#post1484352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the critters presented are quite a far stretch from your usual WoD fare, I honestly prefer that, I like the weird and quirky and the fact that I could drop them into any chronicle, but it's rather offbrand for the whole &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; spiel</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it kind of works from the perspective of serving well for an ST that has all the cores. The problem seems to be less that they don't work with other lines, since Hunters are supposed to usually be unaware of most details about monster societies, and more that the books may feel incomplete if you're going to only buy this one. And I fully embrace the idea that a core book must be a standalone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T13:02:57-07:00","id":1484379,"title":"","content":"The quality of the art is a massive step up, but I struggle with the actual subject matter. H5 is supposed to be a toned down gritty street level game compared to 1e, where most Hunters don't have powers, just guts, specialized skills picked up the hard way, and a lot of luck.<br /> <br /> Is Muslim-coded woman leaping off a crashed motorcycle ready to cut something off-panel in half with her scimitar a fantastic piece of art? Sure. But it doesn't seem to be any better at being in tone with the game than bland Liefeld-equse Hunter #5 jumping through a window and blasting away with a gun. Maybe it's the limitations of what I see getting posted here and elsewhere, but H5's art quality going up a ton doesn't seem to have actually stepped away from presenting Hunters as badasses going toe-to-toe with monsters instead of desperate normal folks trying to do their best with extremely limited options.<br /> --------------<br /> <br /> Also, something I've seen posted elsewhere: why the hell are so many rolls in H5 difficulty 4? It feels like the designers forgot the tone of their own game and back-filled it in by making your ability to bring awesome weapons to a fight contingent on a roll so it can fail sometimes and you forget your signature weapon at home this time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T13:42:41-07:00","id":1484383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484379#post1484379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's the limitations of what I see getting posted here and elsewhere, but H5's art quality going up a ton doesn't seem to have actually stepped away from presenting Hunters as badasses going toe-to-toe with monsters instead of desperate normal folks trying to do their best with extremely limited options.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, indeed. First thing I thought when looking at the last pieces posted is that those folks sure love their swords. And it does seem like those hunters actually hold on their own in a direct fight more often than they should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T15:10:17-07:00","id":1484389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484370#post1484370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it kind of works from the perspective of serving well for an ST that has all the cores. The problem seems to be less that they don't work with other lines, since Hunters are supposed to usually be unaware of most details about monster societies, and more that the books may feel incomplete if you're going to only buy this one. And I fully embrace the idea that a core book must be a standalone.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the weird thing. I don't think this game works well with others. It's designed to be standalone and it intentionally bypasses all the themes and ideas of V5. It's going to work best on its own (possibly with more monster supplements), and I find the whole approach strange due to all the &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; hubub they made.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484379#post1484379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The quality of the art is a massive step up, but I struggle with the actual subject matter. H5 is supposed to be a toned down gritty street level game compared to 1e, where most Hunters don't have powers, just guts, specialized skills picked up the hard way, and a lot of luck.<br /> <br /> Is Muslim-coded woman leaping off a crashed motorcycle ready to cut something off-panel in half with her scimitar a fantastic piece of art? Sure. But it doesn't seem to be any better at being in tone with the game than bland Liefeld-equse Hunter #5 jumping through a window and blasting away with a gun. Maybe it's the limitations of what I see getting posted here and elsewhere, but H5's art quality going up a ton doesn't seem to have actually stepped away from presenting Hunters as badasses going toe-to-toe with monsters instead of desperate normal folks trying to do their best with extremely limited options.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is indeed correct. The art is good, but it shows off bigger badasses doing more individually than the game claims they should do.<br /> <br /> Heck one of the pieces of art actually shows a group of hunters surprised by a pack of three werewolves winning!<br /> <br /> They also use a trick with sequential images showing small stories with the same characters, the headscarf wearing woman is a part of a gang of hunters rushing on their motorcycles to hunt some kind of a psionic horror or flying vampire culminating in this image. It was nice to see that they used that method, but I fully agree that the game is not really consistant with what it says and shows.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484379#post1484379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, something I've seen posted elsewhere: why the hell are so many rolls in H5 difficulty 4? It feels like the designers forgot the tone of their own game and back-filled it in by making your ability to bring awesome weapons to a fight contingent on a roll so it can fail sometimes and you forget your signature weapon at home this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was me in one of the past posts, most of the Edges require 4 successes to activate and there is even a sidebar that says you should be using your Drive Dice to make sure they are activated. This applies to even the indirect/support edges which you're probably want to use before Desperation has started rising. Why? I got no idea.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T15:46:07-07:00","id":1484392,"title":"","content":"Two house rules I suggested on RPG.net for a book I've never even read (though reading V5 helped because I know the basic math of the system):<br /> <br /> 1) Edge rolls should be difficulty 1 and scale with your successes; with the caveat that the ST can cap the maximum level you can hit based on the situation. So if you're rolling for Fleet, 1 success gets you a beat up clunker, 2 successes a decent common vehicle or an OK specialist vehicle, etc. Something I thought of between then and now, is you can offer success-at-cost by reducing a Perk on a fail instead of getting nothing.<br /> <br /> 2) Edge rolls should happen when dramatically appropriate based on your character's personal concept of the Edge rather than things like defaulting to the start of scenes to see if you have them for the scene (which as noted on RPG.net means back-to-back scenes can get weird since <b>knowledge</b> can technically disappear between scenes the way Library is written). If your character has a high-tech experimental metallurgy based silver sword that's supposed to be way more functional in combat than normal silver in their personal Arsenal, it makes way more sense to roll after a fight to see if your sword broke than it does to roll to see if you could to bring it in the first place. If they rely on someone else for their specialist gear, rolling ahead of time is more appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T00:59:25-07:00","id":1484418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484392#post1484392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two house rules I suggested on RPG.net for a book I've never even read (though reading V5 helped because I know the basic math of the system):<br /> <br /> 1) Edge rolls should be difficulty 1 and scale with your successes; with the caveat that the ST can cap the maximum level you can hit based on the situation. So if you're rolling for Fleet, 1 success gets you a beat up clunker, 2 successes a decent common vehicle or an OK specialist vehicle, etc. Something I thought of between then and now, is you can offer success-at-cost by reducing a Perk on a fail instead of getting nothing.<br /> <br /> 2) Edge rolls should happen when dramatically appropriate based on your character's personal concept of the Edge rather than things like defaulting to the start of scenes to see if you have them for the scene (which as noted on RPG.net means back-to-back scenes can get weird since <b>knowledge</b> can technically disappear between scenes the way Library is written). If your character has a high-tech experimental metallurgy based silver sword that's supposed to be way more functional in combat than normal silver in their personal Arsenal, it makes way more sense to roll after a fight to see if your sword broke than it does to roll to see if you could to bring it in the first place. If they rely on someone else for their specialist gear, rolling ahead of time is more appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm stealing these rules if I ever pick this up.<br /> <br /> The monsters seem interesting (though a lot exist in 'exotic third-world slums', which is a trope they should move away from), though it seems with few rules for making more. They're quite different to the standard splats in the WoD, which is okay, but yeah, isn't really One World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T04:08:27-07:00","id":1484419,"title":"","content":"I have less issues with the Philippines section, esp. since IIRC it was written by someone of the appropriate background. It would be really weird of the monsters in the Philippines weren't... well.. reflective of the local people there.<br /> <br /> The idea of then also using the US/Mexico border as the other major example was a questionable choice in the first place, and then to have so much of it focus the bad stuff on the Mexico side of things pushed it over the edge into &quot;ick.&quot; It's not doing much good on highlighting the real issues there, and it's not doing much to explore the supernatural weirdness of the WoD. They have all of the US, Canada, and Europe to pick something a little less used, get some local flair with some unique monsters, and still leave room for some of the more traditional WoD critters presented in unique variation ways.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T10:34:10-07:00","id":1484431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484418#post1484418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(though a lot exist in 'exotic third-world slums', which is a trope they should move away from),</div> </div> </div> </div>That's infuriating, even more when it is well known that the US has a lot of social problems and slums below even third world standards (&quot;Cancer Alley&quot; is a fantastic example of something that would hardly fly legally anywhere else, and even illegally wouldn't on most poor countries), if they even had some commentary to make.<br /> <br /> And since they hadn't, heck, just go with more cosmopolitan places where people will set games more easily than &quot;lets form a cell of everyday people and <i>fly to Mexico</i>&quot;. What's that for, fight monsters and go to the dentist in one go? Not to say that the &quot;Alien Fear&quot; vibe is really cringe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T12:19:05-07:00","id":1484435,"title":"","content":"Or, they could have taken a place like El Paso and Juarez, or San Diego and Tijuana, and highlighted how cosmopolitan those border cities really are. Playing up Mexican Coyote smugglers and Mexican drug cartels is such low hanging fruit compared to the vast amount of other things that are happening in those cities. These are places defined by how cultures mix and mingle despite a line being drawn between them on a map.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T13:02:09-07:00","id":1484439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484435#post1484435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, they could have taken a place like El Paso and Juarez, or San Diego and Tijuana, and highlighted how cosmopolitan those border cities really are. Playing up Mexican Coyote smugglers and Mexican drug cartels is such low hanging fruit compared to the vast amount of other things that are happening in those cities. These are places defined by how cultures mix and mingle despite a line being drawn between them on a map.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting, but also already in what I meant with cosmopolitan places. They could have done big, cosmopolitan cities all around the world instead of the whole &quot;exotic slum&quot; approach, since it is easier to do by yourself with internet research without local input making as much of a difference.<br /> <br /> But it still does some, so staying in the US would generally be a good idea if they didn't want to hire more foreigners than the Filipino author they got. And if they did, then there could be more varied approaches.<br /> <br /> One thing I would like to see is how frequently border areas, despite intense rivalry or even hostility between sides of the border, are so frequently more similar to each other than to the rest of their own side, at least in some aspects (and sometimes in everything).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T11:30:28-07:00","id":1484629,"title":"","content":"Regarding the whole misfortunate presentation of wicked Mexicans and Philipino, I don't think this was intentional by the authors. Just as the whole reading of the cells as rightwing antiathoritarians is not the intent of the writers. There are places where they strain to make Hunters heroes and people who care enough about the world to fight for the good things in it.<br /> <br /> I think it would have been great if they introduced small gazzeteers into the book and actually given us two settings to use instead of presenting things like this. If we focus on the games where protagonists are the locals and show what's there worth fighting for and how much they have to be proud of their homes it stops being as awkward and gain substance. Sure, popularity of the Narcos shows must be inspirational for folks, but if we focus on what's cool in Mexico and how badass the Mexicans can be I'm pretty sure it would make for a good game, one that could even handle the whole tendency of oWoD to only ever write about Americas and utterly mess up the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> If I went in that direction, I'd like to build up some organisations of Hunters in Mexico, people you can have rivalries with, share tall tales with and ask for help when things really go to hell. These folks have been living in this World for a long time, and there must be people in the know. I'd focus on just one of the states - one near US is not a bad choice due to cultural blending, and the problem &quot;how do we Hunt someone who just ran into USA&quot; sounds like loads of fun - its history, culture and architecture. The mannequin vampire is a good start of directly tying monsters into places, but not all places need to be filled with monsters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484392#post1484392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two house rules I suggested on RPG.net for a book I've never even read (though reading V5 helped because I know the basic math of the system):<br /> <br /> 1) Edge rolls should be difficulty 1 and scale with your successes; with the caveat that the ST can cap the maximum level you can hit based on the situation. So if you're rolling for Fleet, 1 success gets you a beat up clunker, 2 successes a decent common vehicle or an OK specialist vehicle, etc. Something I thought of between then and now, is you can offer success-at-cost by reducing a Perk on a fail instead of getting nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both houserules are fun, but I'd like to point out that the Edges in the book are already setup like your suggestion 1. Just starting at diff 4.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T12:02:57-07:00","id":1484633,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't have the exact text, so I phrased it whole... the big problem is still that it starts at diff 4 (though my impression wasn't that getting 5+ successes on Asset checks scaled like that, while Aptitude and Endowment checks did).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T12:14:51-07:00","id":1484637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484633#post1484633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I don't have the exact text, so I phrased it whole... the big problem is still that it starts at diff 4 (though my impression wasn't that getting 5+ successes on Asset checks scaled like that, while Aptitude and Endowment checks did).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no, you're correct. I was critiquing their design choice. There are some that don't need a roll at all, or a very simple roll, but all the ones that are at Diff 4 have extra effects and are better if you can get more hits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T23:03:07-07:00","id":1484671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484637#post1484637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, no, you're correct. I was critiquing their design choice. There are some that don't need a roll at all, or a very simple roll, but all the ones that are at Diff 4 have extra effects and are better if you can get more hits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Difficulty 4 is just too high for this game. Difficulty 2 should be standard (equivalent to the old difficulty 6) and difficulty 3 should be challenging (equivalent to the old difficulty 7) with difficulty 4 kept for things that are quite difficult (old difficulty 8).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T23:31:09-07:00","id":1484673,"title":"","content":"The problem with setting the difficulty in the new system is that it also puts a huge amount of stress on auto-succeeding and/or taking half. The risks of failure/complicated rolls generally outweigh the potential bonus successes from critical hits. If you set the difficulty to what a lot of us would probably want to see, and keep the stress on not rolling, you lose any reason to roll unless the ST makes you roll; which runs the risk of causing tension between ST and player because it makes it feel like calling for rolls as trying to bring up chances for the dice to screw the player rather than exciting unknown outcomes.<br /> <br /> Decreasing the difficulties only really pays off if you also have a more roll happy play style contrary to the advice in the books. V5 and H5 both putting the difficulty fairly high means taking half isn't enough, and the system, not the ST, is making things dangerous.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T01:15:51-07:00","id":1484950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1484673#post1484673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with setting the difficulty in the new system is that it also puts a huge amount of stress on auto-succeeding and/or taking half. The risks of failure/complicated rolls generally outweigh the potential bonus successes from critical hits. If you set the difficulty to what a lot of us would probably want to see, and keep the stress on not rolling, you lose any reason to roll unless the ST makes you roll; which runs the risk of causing tension between ST and player because it makes it feel like calling for rolls as trying to bring up chances for the dice to screw the player rather than exciting unknown outcomes.<br /> <br /> Decreasing the difficulties only really pays off if you also have a more roll happy play style contrary to the advice in the books. V5 and H5 both putting the difficulty fairly high means taking half isn't enough, and the system, not the ST, is making things dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. There are lots of interconnected problems, which makes tweaking V5 a big task, even for small changes. You're usually better off tweaking V20, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T02:38:11-07:00","id":1484952,"title":"","content":"One of these days I really need to clear off enough other things off my plate to get the energy to do a full fan conversion of the WoD to the Storypath system to make it the action-horror game it really is,and leave the &quot;grittier&quot; approach to the CofD. I've been tweaking the old rules long enough that I'd rather start with something that's already doing way better with a lot of the base mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T01:15:49-07:00","id":1485461,"title":"","content":"It all seems a little quiet about this game now. Has anyone seen any reviews? I'm curious to know, as well, how sales are doing? Are people picking this book up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T02:01:15-07:00","id":1485464,"title":"","content":"Honestly theres not enough to it for much discussion. Theres only about 20 pages worth of actual game mechanics in the 220+ page book and most of the background lore stuff, sparse though it is has already been covered in V5 books. Theres a bunch of fairly generic ST and chronicle building advice but again that has already been covered in other books.<br /> <br /> Mostly the book comes across as kind of unfinished and kinda seems like they just couldn't be bothered commiting to anything and constantly fall back on telling you to just ' do it yourself'.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T05:29:39-07:00","id":1485489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1485464#post1485464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly theres not enough to it for much discussion. Theres only about 20 pages worth of actual game mechanics in the 220+ page book and most of the background lore stuff, sparse though it is has already been covered in V5 books. Theres a bunch of fairly generic ST and chronicle building advice but again that has already been covered in other books.<br /> <br /> Mostly the book comes across as kind of unfinished and kinda seems like they just couldn't be bothered commiting to anything and constantly fall back on telling you to just ' do it yourself'.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The responses I've seen online mostly seem to be of interest, quickly changed to a hard nope when the new premise is laid out. There's a say-nothing review in ScreenRant (which is known for its churnalism and clickbait headlines, so I wouldn't expect much from them anyway), and a few YouTube reviews, but it's like tumbleweed otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T09:23:01-07:00","id":1485512,"title":"","content":"I mean, this is basically what a lot of us predicted?<br /> <br /> It's not tapping into the HH fanbase because &quot;orgs are the bad guys.&quot;<br /> It's not tapping into the Imbued fanbase because &quot;the Driven are normal everyday people no matter what, including Edges, and if they have more than a whiff of supernatural power they can't be Driven.&quot;<br /> It's not tapping into the Vigil fanbase because, &quot;we have a very specific vision of the Driven and we'll talk about how varied they can be, but never actually support that.&quot;<br /> It's not tapping into the broader RPG fan-base because monster hunting is not special on its own. Monster hunting is the default RPG stance with lots and lots of games that do it in every conceivable style. What made the WoD/CofD monster hunters special in the wider RPG spectrum was their reflection on the original subversion of playing the monsters defending against the hunters. The Driven can't have Loresheets though, because they're not allowed to connect to the WoD (aka what makes a WoD Hunter game special in the first place).<br /> <br /> H5 is basically putting everything on fans new to things with V5 that aren't put off by any incongruity with past products (even if H5 itself calls attention to said issues), and trying to replicate the early WoD success of appealing to people that barely realize there are RPGs besides D&amp;D in the hopes of getting them into Hunter before they find out about all the competition out there.<br /> <br /> We'll have to wait and see how that pans out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T15:45:35-07:00","id":1485554,"title":"","content":"I think we also may be misjudging its impact. The book is still not in general distribution. If you've been following it from the start you can get it on the Renegade website, but it hasn't trickled out to normal distribution channels yet. So most people that have it are people who knew about it and were keeping an eye out in it in advance - that most likely being us, with our perspectives and expectations of the game, as well as the knowledge of what else is there.<br /> <br /> The general audience still hasn't had a chance to really get into this and give their own feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T17:58:29-07:00","id":1485579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1485554#post1485554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general audience still hasn't had a chance to really get into this and give their own feedback.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but the general commentators that V5 caters to had. If they're not nearly as loud as they are about V5 stuff, something's very off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T00:18:42-07:00","id":1485607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1485512#post1485512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, this is basically what a lot of us predicted?<br /> <br /> It's not tapping into the HH fanbase because &amp;quot;orgs are the bad guys.&amp;quot;<br /> It's not tapping into the Imbued fanbase because &amp;quot;the Driven are normal everyday people no matter what, including Edges, and if they have more than a whiff of supernatural power they can't be Driven.&amp;quot;<br /> It's not tapping into the Vigil fanbase because, &amp;quot;we have a very specific vision of the Driven and we'll talk about how varied they can be, but never actually support that.&amp;quot;<br /> It's not tapping into the broader RPG fan-base because monster hunting is not special on its own. Monster hunting is the default RPG stance with lots and lots of games that do it in every conceivable style. What made the WoD/CofD monster hunters special in the wider RPG spectrum was their reflection on the original subversion of playing the monsters defending against the hunters. The Driven can't have Loresheets though, because they're not allowed to connect to the WoD (aka what makes a WoD Hunter game special in the first place).<br /> <br /> H5 is basically putting everything on fans new to things with V5 that aren't put off by any incongruity with past products (even if H5 itself calls attention to said issues), and trying to replicate the early WoD success of appealing to people that barely realize there are RPGs besides D&amp;D in the hopes of getting them into Hunter before they find out about all the competition out there.<br /> <br /> We'll have to wait and see how that pans out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It seems like a flop so far. But I was overlooking the distribution thing, so I am perhaps being too rash. It may sweep the board in a few months' time. Then again...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T01:18:56-07:00","id":1485612,"title":"","content":"I think it is worth noting that it <b>is</b> available to general audiences. It's not being marketed to general audiences yet, because you have to preorder it to get the early PDF release. But anyone that wants it can get it.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the whole point of getting your PDF out to people that are, effectively, buying the game sight unseen, is that those are the people that are going to generate the most initial hype. The people getting copies now are the people that are going to be the first run of podcasts, AP streams, and convention plays of the game. The vast majority of people that haven't gotten it are either waiting for what the people getting now think, or aren't following this at all. The &quot;wait and see what the people willing to preorder it think&quot; crowd doesn't seem to be that impressed, because the &quot;got it preorder&quot; crowd doesn't seem to be that impressed (and the few largely positive people on it I've seen aren't really doing a lot to defend why it's worth getting in the wider context of its competition). So, yes, there is going to be a point where getting it is much easier because Paradox is doing traditional distribution on top of digital marketing so there's going to be a lot of people not following stuff on line that are going to see it in a store or whatnot and some of them are going to buy it. But (esp. with the whole global economy doing shitty thing) a large portion of those people are still going to pop online to see what the buzz is... and no buzz is bad for the way Paradox is setting things up. H5 doesn't need to do V5 numbers, but it definitely needs to do better than what Onyx Path books do in a Kickstarter to avoid Paradox reconsidering how they're approaching the TT books part of the WoD.<br /> <br /> The impact to be judging here is that the period of when the preorder PDF back to when it ships to general distribution is when you build up all the hype so that general distribution leads to general sales. However much V5 is not my thing, it has lots of fans. It has diehard fans from the first alpha playtest that were ready to get everyone they could to start playing V5 once it dropped. V5 was all over geek related news sites leading up to its release. We are not in the era of people discovering books in physical stores as the primary way people get into new games (if we ever were, since word of mouth has always been a huge part of RPG marketing). So yes, I think it's far to be skeptical of the general distribution reversing things, because the success of that correlates strongly to having a significant hype for the current stage of the book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-02T14:32:41-07:00","id":1485651,"title":"","content":"Well I was hoping for a silver lining. We have zero insight into sales for V5 and H5, and I'd somhow like to know that they understand that H5 is a better product than V5, even if what it is, is messy. But, I'm not really sure how much they even care or who their audience is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T09:11:24-07:00","id":1485694,"title":"","content":"Game stores should be getting in their physical copies starting this week, barring delivery problems and the holiday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T13:06:12-07:00","id":1485711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1485694#post1485694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Game stores should be getting in their physical copies starting this week, barring delivery problems and the holiday.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean eventual holiday, as there's no holiday for everyone around the world this week.<br /> <br /> Curiously, though, beyond a local holiday in the US, this week will be <b>Kupala Night</b> across Slavic countries, including Russia, which means it will be indeed a religious holiday for hundreds of millions across the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T22:00:30-07:00","id":1486082,"title":"","content":"Here's a review: <a href=\"https://www.enworld.org/threads/a-review-of-the-new-hunter-the-reckoning.689512/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.enworld.org/threads/a-re...koning.689512/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T16:01:44-07:00","id":1486242,"title":"","content":"I see they're keeping touchstones. Hopefully they've refined and cleaned them up a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T16:38:27-07:00","id":1486243,"title":"","content":"Cleaned up is hard to measure because Hunter doesn't have anything that Touchstones really do. Like, it's cleaner, because there's nothing to mess up. It's a good thing that WoD5 seems to understand that Touchstones shouldn't be exactly the same for each splat, but the CofD also knew to sometimes just drop stuff if it doesn't fit. Not every CofD game has Touchstones, because they don't have a role in every CofD game, even if a lot of them do and they get implemented in many ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T02:42:08-07:00","id":1486267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1486243#post1486243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cleaned up is hard to measure because Hunter doesn't have anything that Touchstones really do. Like, it's cleaner, because there's nothing to mess up. It's a good thing that WoD5 seems to understand that Touchstones shouldn't be exactly the same for each splat, but the CofD also knew to sometimes just drop stuff if it doesn't fit. Not every CofD game has Touchstones, because they don't have a role in every CofD game, even if a lot of them do and they get implemented in many ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly this is quite correct. Touchstones are there, but they don't interact with Drive in any way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T03:15:29-07:00","id":1486268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1486243#post1486243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cleaned up is hard to measure because Hunter doesn't have anything that Touchstones really do. Like, it's cleaner, because there's nothing to mess up. It's a good thing that WoD5 seems to understand that Touchstones shouldn't be exactly the same for each splat, but the CofD also knew to sometimes just drop stuff if it doesn't fit. Not every CofD game has Touchstones, because they don't have a role in every CofD game, even if a lot of them do and they get implemented in many ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts on v5 touchstones were good idea that needed polish. Abstract and non human touchstones should have been present and it should have been more of an asset than liability. I can see touchstones being a struggle with hunters since they're already human outside of an threat of them becoming some sort of disconected pyscho killer ala punisher on a bad day and even that's ultimatly a human if not particularly relatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-12-2022, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T11:23:46-07:00","id":1486297,"title":"","content":"That, as Asmodai pointed out, did not get addressed. H5 has Touchstones and Chronicle Tenets, but they have no mechanical aspect to make them fulfill a role. Touchstones are supposed to do for Hunters what you say (keep them from going all Punisher style psychotic), but there's no rules to enforce it. You're just supposed to make an NPC for your Hunter that keeps them &quot;grounded,&quot; with no system backup on how that looks. They're still living humans. Chronicle Tenets likewise no longer plug into anything. It's just a framework for making sure the ST and players are on the same page about the tone of the game by turning some basic ideas on that into a list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T05:57:27-07:00","id":1486609,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting one, Kotaku is a mainstream outlet and one with a very shallow RPG footprint. The author is a W20 player, though. So this may be a good way to see what non hobby people see this like:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://kotaku.com/hunter-reckoning-5th-ed-dungeons-and-dragons-ttrpg-worl-1849172952\" target=\"_blank\">https://kotaku.com/hunter-reckoning-...orl-1849172952</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T13:00:41-07:00","id":1486662,"title":"","content":"&quot; And it\u2019s fantastic. If your experience with TTRPGs has started and ended with <i>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</i>, then this is a game to pay attention to.&quot;<br /> <br /> To me at least, that's pretty damning with faint praise. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T14:09:47-07:00","id":1486671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1486609#post1486609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting one, Kotaku is a mainstream outlet and one with a very shallow RPG footprint. The author is a W20 player, though. So this may be a good way to see what non hobby people see this like:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://kotaku.com/hunter-reckoning-5th-ed-dungeons-and-dragons-ttrpg-worl-1849172952\" target=\"_blank\">https://kotaku.com/hunter-reckoning-...orl-1849172952</a></div> </div> </div> </div>The first part is mostly saying it is good because it is &quot;more drama than D&amp;D&quot;, again and again. Then it gets into explaining WoD in general in a non-specific way (splat or edition). Finally it gets to explain the game and why it is good: because it is a good opening for D&amp;D players to know WoD.<br /> <br /> At the end she admits that she plays WtA20, that she didn't even read V5, her understanding of the new edition overall is poor and what she did understood <b><i>she didn't even liked</i></b>, expending another good chunk of the H5 review on explaining classic WoD rules, comparing and praising the old rules.<br /> <br /> Fantastic...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T15:00:48-07:00","id":1486678,"title":"","content":"I never said it was a good review, just that it's what to expect from a mainstream outlet <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (I tried not to prejudice you folks against it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T15:22:19-07:00","id":1486685,"title":"","content":"Well, we'll see if &quot;any publicity is good publicity,&quot; here I guess. It seems like more mainstream sites understand the target audience for this game (people that have only played D&amp;D looking for something else to try). Only time will tell if that's a smart idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T15:30:13-07:00","id":1486686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1486685#post1486685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we'll see if &quot;any publicity is good publicity,&quot; here I guess. It seems like more mainstream sites understand the target audience for this game (people that have only played D&amp;D looking for something else to try). Only time will tell if that's a smart idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does seem like a low bar to aim for. Practically all the Kotaku and Polygon articles about RPG's are &quot;oh you have to check X out because it's not D&amp;D!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T15:45:43-07:00","id":1486690,"title":"","content":"It was a fun reading, as far as reviews go. It was badly written for a review, which says a lot about Kotaku, but also because of that was really informative about the writer's opinions as she couldn't stop from leaking her true opinions: it has barely any WoD in it, it is <b>really</b> close to D&amp;D as it is just <i>heroes vs monsters</i> and the best you can do about that is to dive in the melodrama aspect, and no mechanic impressed her whatsoever. Indeed, take in the fact that she didn't mentioned no dramatic rule, nothing about Desperation, she just focused on the basic rules she already had a reference to understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T16:10:37-07:00","id":1486692,"title":"","content":"I find it ironic that they also have a lot of high praise for D&amp;D 5, whenever its time for official promos of Wizards stuff and interviews with Wizards staff, but whenever they cover a RPG on their own it's &quot;THANK GOD IT's NOT D&amp;D!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T12:22:04-07:00","id":1486892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1483612#post1483612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/HOkgA46.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>I have heard of but not seen a movie called The Hebrew Hammer. It gives off a very strong vibe similar to blacksploitation films, but adjusted to give the vibes to Hasidic (I think) Jewish people. This picture immediately makes me think of that movie, although I think the protagonist in it carried guns.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T17:38:55-07:00","id":1486927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1486686#post1486686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That does seem like a low bar to aim for. Practically all the Kotaku and Polygon articles about RPG's are &quot;oh you have to check X out because it's not D&amp;D!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I must admit I'm surprised they're both still around, the last I recall of them was buzzfeed tier 'socially conscious' articles. You're usually circling the drain when you get there.<br /> <br /> I'm strangely pleased to see kotaku still around and branching out even if the review isn't very useful if you don't care about d&amp;d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-18-2022, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T20:37:58-07:00","id":1486944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1486927#post1486927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm strangely pleased to see kotaku still around and branching out even if the review isn't very useful if you don't care about d&amp;d.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest I do care about D&amp;D and the review still isn't very useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T06:32:45-07:00","id":1486995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1486671#post1486671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first part is mostly saying it is good because it is &quot;more drama than D&amp;D&quot;, again and again. Then it gets into explaining WoD in general in a non-specific way (splat or edition). Finally it gets to explain the game and why it is good: because it is a good opening for D&amp;D players to know WoD.<br /> <br /> At the end she admits that she plays WtA20, that she didn't even read V5, her understanding of the new edition overall is poor and what she did understood <b><i>she didn't even liked</i></b>, expending another good chunk of the H5 review on explaining classic WoD rules, comparing and praising the old rules.<br /> <br /> Fantastic...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. That old 1990s snobbery. 'This isn't AD&amp;D you know!' was a constant refrain back then. Meaning, rules are for nerds and cool goth kids wing it. The WoD was good simply because it wasn't D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> I was like 15 when the millennium struck, so I didn't really think about that snobbery in any kind of critical fashion. Now I can see how noxious (and obnoxious) it was. <br /> <br /> Interestingly, I have seen this attitude re-emerging in recent years. I hope to God it's a short-lived trend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1486692#post1486692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it ironic that they also have a lot of high praise for D&amp;D 5, whenever its time for official promos of Wizards stuff and interviews with Wizards staff, but whenever they cover a RPG on their own it's &amp;quot;THANK GOD IT's NOT D&amp;D!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a sign of crappy journalism. Basically writing puff pieces to get free stuff and keep your PR mates happy. (I've been there. I used to write for a free magazine back in the 00s where we did a lot of that because there was next to no pay and we lived off the freebies.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-19-2022, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T06:54:51-07:00","id":1487000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1486995#post1486995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was like 15 when the millennium struck, so I didn't really think about that snobbery in any kind of critical fashion. Now I can see how noxious (and obnoxious) it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>While he was really good at it, my first long term ST was so snob about it that, <b>despite being a fan of high fantasy himself</b> he preferred to adapt the Storyteller System to play Final Fantasy instead of just playing D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> Yes, it was noxious, it was obnoxious, and it promoted some very horrible behaviors as the apex of RPG virtue, like not caring about the rules or about the people that want good rules, and punishing players for playing &quot;wrong&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{