itle":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1486995#post1486995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. That old 1990s snobbery. 'This isn't AD&amp;D you know!' was a constant refrain back then. Meaning, rules are for nerds and cool goth kids wing it. The WoD was good simply because it wasn't D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> I was like 15 when the millennium struck, so I didn't really think about that snobbery in any kind of critical fashion. Now I can see how noxious (and obnoxious) it was. <br /> <br /> Interestingly, I have seen this attitude re-emerging in recent years. I hope to God it's a short-lived trend.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I though kotaku were on the socially conscious side of things? Diversity, inclusively and all that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-19-2022, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T19:48:13-07:00","id":1487093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1487033#post1487033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I though kotaku were on the socially conscious side of things? Diversity, inclusively and all that?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are. But, you know...<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1487032#post1487032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thats what happens when you pay staff bugger all.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T21:27:48-07:00","id":1487106,"title":"","content":"You guys DO know what happened to Kotaku's parent company, Gawker, right?<br /> <br /> They were <i>sued into bankruptcy</i> by Hulk Hogan, who was <i>funded by a third party</i> with an ax to grind, and then bought up by venture capitalists. They're &quot;paid bugger all&quot; because their owners want Gawker and Kotaku to DIE.<br /> <br /> Whether or not you think Hogan was in the right to sue Gawker, <i>he</i> didn't pay for his lawyers. Peter Thiel, a billionaire with dirty laundry that regularly got aired out by Gizmodo and Valleywag (two other Gawker affiliates, like Kotaku), paid for said lawyers. And Thiel didn't do <i>any</i> of this for Hogan, he did it to <i>silence</i> a news outlet he couldn't control.<br /> <br /> Sorry for going way off topic, but Gawker/Kotaku didn't wake up one morning and choose to burn it all down. They were <i>sabotaged</i>, in a way that would impress a Ventrue. With that out of the way, we should probably get back to talking about Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 07-20-2022, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-29T20:08:16-07:00","id":1488434,"title":"","content":"So just gonna keep this brief. I bought this book on impulse, mildly excited to have a 5th edition treatment of the imbued. What I feel like I got was not Hunter: The Reckoning so much as the diet soda version of Hunter: The Vigil. That's devaluing the content of the book, certainly, but...yeah. I don't have any use for what I was given. I feel like the Vigil already did this in both editions of that game and my admittedly cursory impression is that they did it better. I'm not especially interested in delving further into the book- I was quite disappointed seeing the central focus of the last game entirely omitted from this version. Frankly, I feel tricked into buying the stupid thing. I could have done more research, absolutely. But I don't feel like expecting the imbued in a book calling itself Hunter the Reckoning was unreasonable. It feels like using that title specifically is intended as nothing but a cash grab. I know I'm not gonna be alone in being disappointed by this book. And to be 100% honest I've been just lukewarm enough about what has come out so far for 5th edition that this could just be where I give up on the new old world of darkness entirely. Not sure yet. Sorry if this sounds too whiny or whatever. Just felt like it was worth noting my personal reaction as a old school fan of the original game to this new edition, for whatever it might be worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T00:25:22-07:00","id":1488439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1488434#post1488434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So just gonna keep this brief. I bought this book on impulse, mildly excited to have a 5th edition treatment of the imbued. What I feel like I got was not Hunter: The Reckoning so much as the diet soda version of Hunter: The Vigil. That's devaluing the content of the book, certainly, but...yeah. I don't have any use for what I was given. I feel like the Vigil already did this in both editions of that game and my admittedly cursory impression is that they did it better. I'm not especially interested in delving further into the book- I was quite disappointed seeing the central focus of the last game entirely omitted from this version. Frankly, I feel tricked into buying the stupid thing. I could have done more research, absolutely. But I don't feel like expecting the imbued in a book calling itself Hunter the Reckoning was unreasonable. It feels like using that title specifically is intended as nothing but a cash grab. I know I'm not gonna be alone in being disappointed by this book. And to be 100% honest I've been just lukewarm enough about what has come out so far for 5th edition that this could just be where I give up on the new old world of darkness entirely. Not sure yet. Sorry if this sounds too whiny or whatever. Just felt like it was worth noting my personal reaction as a old school fan of the original game to this new edition, for whatever it might be worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to hear that. Can you get a refund? I think you'd have a good chance of getting your money back if you explained the situation. Not everyone is glued to TTRPG social media and the like, so it's an easy (and understandable) mistake to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T03:20:40-07:00","id":1488444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1488434#post1488434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So just gonna keep this brief. I bought this book on impulse, mildly excited to have a 5th edition treatment of the imbued. What I feel like I got was not Hunter: The Reckoning so much as the diet soda version of Hunter: The Vigil. That's devaluing the content of the book, certainly, but...yeah. I don't have any use for what I was given. I feel like the Vigil already did this in both editions of that game and my admittedly cursory impression is that they did it better. I'm not especially interested in delving further into the book- I was quite disappointed seeing the central focus of the last game entirely omitted from this version. Frankly, I feel tricked into buying the stupid thing. I could have done more research, absolutely. But I don't feel like expecting the imbued in a book calling itself Hunter the Reckoning was unreasonable. It feels like using that title specifically is intended as nothing but a cash grab. I know I'm not gonna be alone in being disappointed by this book. And to be 100% honest I've been just lukewarm enough about what has come out so far for 5th edition that this could just be where I give up on the new old world of darkness entirely. Not sure yet. Sorry if this sounds too whiny or whatever. Just felt like it was worth noting my personal reaction as a old school fan of the original game to this new edition, for whatever it might be worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am really sorry to hear that and I hope you manage to refund the book or do something else to make you feel better about the ordeal.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit curious though, you seem to be like someone who hangs around on forums, did you not see any of the discussions about the removal of the Imbued? I'm in no way blaming you,just trying to figure out what's wrong with the WW communication. One of the things that White Wolf did was specifically call out that they will not be in here. So on one hand you have someone who is obviously more interested and informed than the average RPG buyer, but on the other the ways WW is communicating is such a mess that the message is muddled even further. I wonder if it's because it's not really spelled out it any of their dev and marketing material, but because of Word of God comes from carefully listening to their once in a blue moon addresses to the nation on youtube/twitch?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T07:15:50-07:00","id":1488456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1488444#post1488444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am really sorry to hear that and I hope you manage to refund the book or do something else to make you feel better about the ordeal.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit curious though, you seem to be like someone who hangs around on forums, did you not see any of the discussions about the removal of the Imbued? I'm in no way blaming you,just trying to figure out what's wrong with the WW communication. One of the things that White Wolf did was specifically call out that they will not be in here. So on one hand you have someone who is obviously more interested and informed than the average RPG buyer, but on the other the ways WW is communicating is such a mess that the message is muddled even further. I wonder if it's because it's not really spelled out it any of their dev and marketing material, but because of Word of God comes from carefully listening to their once in a blue moon addresses to the nation on youtube/twitch?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, for some reason the fact that Hunter The Reckoning had a new edition at all had gone completely under my radar. I do pop into the forums every now and then. I may have just missed it or assumed that any buzz about the new game was just discussing the older setting. However it happened I was caught by surprise when I came across it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T07:25:05-07:00","id":1488458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1488456#post1488456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, for some reason the fact that Hunter The Reckoning had a new edition at all had gone completely under my radar. I do pop into the forums every now and then. I may have just missed it or assumed that any buzz about the new game was just discussing the older setting. However it happened I was caught by surprise when I came across it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the reply. Guess there will be a lot of confusion coming from people who are not actively looking for information.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-30T20:10:44-07:00","id":1488525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1463822-hunter-the-reckoning-done-with-development?p=1488434#post1488434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So just gonna keep this brief. I bought this book on impulse, mildly excited to have a 5th edition treatment of the imbued. What I feel like I got was not Hunter: The Reckoning so much as the diet soda version of Hunter: The Vigil. That's devaluing the content of the book, certainly, but...yeah. I don't have any use for what I was given. I feel like the Vigil already did this in both editions of that game and my admittedly cursory impression is that they did it better. I'm not especially interested in delving further into the book- I was quite disappointed seeing the central focus of the last game entirely omitted from this version. Frankly, I feel tricked into buying the stupid thing. I could have done more research, absolutely. But I don't feel like expecting the imbued in a book calling itself Hunter the Reckoning was unreasonable. It feels like using that title specifically is intended as nothing but a cash grab. I know I'm not gonna be alone in being disappointed by this book. And to be 100% honest I've been just lukewarm enough about what has come out so far for 5th edition that this could just be where I give up on the new old world of darkness entirely. Not sure yet. Sorry if this sounds too whiny or whatever. Just felt like it was worth noting my personal reaction as a old school fan of the original game to this new edition, for whatever it might be worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately this was a predictable outcome already announced on this very thread a long time ago. Yeah, it was a bad move and it will leave/is leaving a bad taste on many mouths that, like you, didn't got wind of the content change before.<br /> <br /> My only disagreement, that I already stated several times and will continue to do so, is that it isn't diet soda <i>Hunter: the Vigil</i>. It is diet soda <i>Hunters Hunted</i>.<br /> <br /> The worse is to think that it is actually a lesser version even for a 92's supplement...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}